        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EPIGEN</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001001245</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Origin and dynamics of admixture in Brazilians and its effect on the pattern of deleterious mutations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26124090</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001245</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The EPIGEN-Brasil Initiative is so far the largest Latin American initiative in population genomics and genetic epidemiology.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST011890</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Trans-ethnic meta-analysis identifies new loci associated with longitudinal blood pressure traits.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33603002</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7893038/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used the genotype data (Illumina Infinium Omni2.5) from 1442 participants from the Bambui Study in the context of the EPIGEN project39.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:26124090</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Origin and dynamics of admixture in Brazilians and its effect on the pattern of deleterious mutations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26124090</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/article/MED/26124090</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We present the results of the EPIGEN Brazil Initiative</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A project combining population-based genomic data from northeastern, southeastern and southern Brazil to investigate ancestry, admixture, kinship, inbreeding and deleterious genetic variation, known as the EPIGEN Brazil Initiative.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26124090</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000739"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9952852/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed admixture mapping (followed by fine-mapping) of BMI using data of ~2.3 million SNPs for three Brazilian population-based cohorts, from Northeast (Salvador), Southeast (Bambuí), and South (Pelotas), with distinct admixture and socio-demographic backgrounds, studied by the EPIGEN-Brazil Initiative (https://epigen.grude.ufmg.br,).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9952852/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed admixture mapping (followed by fine-mapping) of BMI using data of ~2.3 million SNPs for three Brazilian population-based cohorts, from Northeast (Salvador), Southeast (Bambuí), and South (Pelotas), with distinct admixture and socio-demographic backgrounds, studied by the EPIGEN-Brazil Initiative (https://epigen.grude.ufmg.br,).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4669662/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SCAALA composes the EPIGEN-Brazil initiative, it is based on three well-defined ongoing population-based cohorts from Brazil’s regions</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000062"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/26124090</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>three populations with different histories from the Northeast (African ancestry: 50%), Southeast, and South (both with European ancestry &gt;70%) of Brazil</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


