        <obo:IAO_0000115>A research programme comprising two cohorts, the Lothian Birth Cohorts of 1921 and 1936, whose members took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Surveys of 1932 and 1947 and were recruited in older age, mostly in Edinburgh and the Lothians, for repeated study of cognitive ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
