        <rdfs:comment>These participants included 600 cases with ischaemic stroke at ages 18 to 69 years and 600 controls matched for age and sex from the Sahlgrenska Academy Study on Ischemic Stroke (SAHLSIS 28 ) and 2,060 population-based participants from the prospective Malmö Diet and Cancer Study (MDC 29 ) of whom 1,812 have not had a cardiovascular event and 248 had an ischaemic stroke during follow-up.</rdfs:comment>
