        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90232793</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of African American adults aged 18–70 with hypertensive chronic kidney disease, enrolled at clinical centres across the United States in a randomized trial of antihypertensive drug regimens and blood-pressure goals (1995–2001) and then followed in the AASK Cohort Study to identify risk factors for progressive kidney disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AASK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AASK Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American Study of Kidney disease and hypertension</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">African American Study of Kidney Disease and Hypertension</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90232793</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of 969 protein quantitative trait loci in an African American population with kidney disease attributed to hypertension.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35870639</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35870639+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we report the genetic determinants of the serum proteome in 466 African Americans with chronic kidney disease attributed to hypertension from the richly phenotyped African American Study of Kidney Disease and Hypertension (AASK) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of African American adults aged 18–70 with hypertensive chronic kidney disease, enrolled at clinical centres across the United States in a randomized trial of antihypertensive drug regimens and blood-pressure goals (1995–2001) and then followed in the AASK Cohort Study to identify risk factors for progressive kidney disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12819322</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17591527</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18472682</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AASK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18472682+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The African American Study of Kidney Disease and Hypertension (AASK) was conducted over a 7-year period at 21 clinical centers across the United States to investigate whether one of two levels of blood pressure control and/or one of three classes of antihypertensive medications was more effective at slowing the rate of renal disease in African Americans with renal insufficiency presumed secondary to hypertension.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90286909</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of patients who have visited the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam at VU University Medical Center (now Amsterdam UMC, location VUmc) in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, since the center opened in 2000 and consented to the research use of their clinical data, numbering almost 7,000 individuals by 2019. Patients undergo a one-day diagnostic screening that includes neuropsychological testing, MRI, EEG and lumbar puncture, are asked to consent to the storage of blood, DNA and cerebrospinal fluid in the center&apos;s biobank, and are mostly followed up annually; the ongoing observational study combines patient care with research on early diagnosis, heterogeneity and vascular factors in dementia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ADC also denotes National Alzheimer&apos;s Coordinating Center (COHO:0000480); this term is Amsterdam Dementia Cohort.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AmDem</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Amsterdam</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Amsterdam Dementia Cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90286909</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Quantitative trait loci mapping of circulating metabolites in cerebrospinal fluid to uncover biological mechanisms involved in brain-related phenotypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40021830</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40021830+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Individuals originated from two separate cohorts including cognitively healthy subjects (n = 490) and a well-characterized memory clinic sample, the Amsterdam Dementia Cohort (ADC, n = 487).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of patients who have visited the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam at VU University Medical Center (now Amsterdam UMC, location VUmc) in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, since the center opened in 2000 and consented to the research use of their clinical data, numbering almost 7,000 individuals by 2019. Patients undergo a one-day diagnostic screening that includes neuropsychological testing, MRI, EEG and lumbar puncture, are asked to consent to the storage of blood, DNA and cerebrospinal fluid in the center&apos;s biobank, and are mostly followed up annually; the ongoing observational study combines patient care with research on early diagnosis, heterogeneity and vascular factors in dementia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29562540</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40021830</obo:IAO_0000119>
