    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90244700</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based longitudinal cohort of men and women aged 65 years and older sampled from Medicare eligibility lists in four US communities (Forsyth County, North Carolina; Sacramento County, California; Washington County, Maryland; Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania) from 1989, with mostly Black participants added in 1992–1993, to identify factors related to the onset and course of coronary heart disease and stroke in older adults.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CHS also denotes Children&apos;s Health Study (COHO:0001592); this term is Cardiovascular Health Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cardiovascular Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244700</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Circulating Soluble CD163, Associations With Cardiovascular Outcomes and Mortality, and Identification of Genetic Variants in Older Individuals: The Cardiovascular Health Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36314488</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36314488+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Methods and Results We measured plasma sCD163 in 5214 adults (aged ≥65 years, 58.7% women, 16.2% Black) of the CHS (Cardiovascular Health Study).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based longitudinal cohort of men and women aged 65 years and older sampled from Medicare eligibility lists in four US communities (Forsyth County, North Carolina; Sacramento County, California; Washington County, Maryland; Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania) from 1989, with mostly Black participants added in 1992–1993, to identify factors related to the onset and course of coronary heart disease and stroke in older adults.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:1669507</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36314488</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://chs-nhlbi.org/CHSOverview</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study recruited 5,888 adults aged 65 or older at entry in four U.S. communities</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454571</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based, multi-generational cohort begun in 1948 with the Original Cohort of 5,209 men and women aged 30–62, a random sample of the adult population of Framingham, Massachusetts, and extended by the Offspring Cohort of 5,124 of their children and the children&apos;s spouses (1971), the Third Generation Cohort of 4,095 grandchildren (2002–2005), the New Offspring Spouse Cohort (2003–2005) and the ethnically diverse Omni cohorts, begun in 1994 among residents of Framingham and surrounding towns and extended in 2003–2005, all examined approximately every 2–4 years to define cardiovascular disease risk factors and, increasingly, the genetic and molecular epidemiology of cardiovascular and other diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym FHS also denotes NHLBI Family Heart Study (COHO:0000582); this term is Framingham Heart Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Framingham Heart Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454571</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A Genome-Wide Interaction Study of Erythrocyte ω-3 Polyunsaturated Fatty Acid Species and Memory in the Framingham Heart Study Offspring Cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38141771</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38141771+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Offspring cohort from the Framingham Heart Study was cross-sectionally analyzed in this genome-wide interaction study (GWIS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based, multi-generational cohort begun in 1948 with the Original Cohort of 5,209 men and women aged 30–62, a random sample of the adult population of Framingham, Massachusetts, and extended by the Offspring Cohort of 5,124 of their children and the children&apos;s spouses (1971), the Third Generation Cohort of 4,095 grandchildren (2002–2005), the New Offspring Spouse Cohort (2003–2005) and the ethnically diverse Omni cohorts, begun in 1994 among residents of Framingham and surrounding towns and extended in 2003–2005, all examined approximately every 2–4 years to define cardiovascular disease risk factors and, increasingly, the genetic and molecular epidemiology of cardiovascular and other diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26705418</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.framinghamheartstudy.org/fhs-about/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39350372+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Framingham Heart Study, which is a longitudinal, multi-generational community-based cohort based in Framingham, Massachusetts, USA.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000386 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000386">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90829960</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ongoing population-based cohort of people aged 30 or above living in two geographically defined areas of Bonn, Germany, invited in random order by the German Centre for Neurodegenerative Diseases (DZNE) for deep phenotyping, imaging and omics studies of health and ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Rheinland Studie</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Rhineland</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Rhineland Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Rhineland Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000386"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90829960</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Population-based genome-wide association study of plasma complex lipid species.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42069741</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42069741+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Thus, we perform genome-wide association studies on 970 lipid species and 267 fatty acid composite measures using samples from the population-based Rhineland Study (n = 6096).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000386"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ongoing population-based cohort of people aged 30 or above living in two geographically defined areas of Bonn, Germany, invited in random order by the German Centre for Neurodegenerative Diseases (DZNE) for deep phenotyping, imaging and omics studies of health and ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13135507/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.rheinland-studie.de/en/the-study/background/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000386"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Rhineland</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000386"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13135507/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used data from the Rhineland Study, an ongoing population-based cohort study in Bonn, Germany, to perform a GWAS on circulating complex lipid levels and composition measured using the Metabolon Complex Lipids Platform.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
