    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001411"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90461825</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HCHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HCHS-SOL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HCHS/SOL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HCHS_SOL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Hispanic Community Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Hispanic Community Health Study / Study of Latinos</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SOL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Study of Latinos</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hispanic Community Health Study/Study of Latinos</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90461825</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study reveals shared and distinct genetic architecture of fatty acids and oxylipins in the Hispanic Community Health Study/Study of Latinos.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39644095</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39644095+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of 81 fatty acids and oxylipins in 11,584 Hispanic Community Health Study/Study of Latinos (HCHS/SOL) participants with genetic and lipidomic data measured at study baseline (58.6% female, mean age = 46.1 years (standard deviation 13.8)).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20609343</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39644095</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
