    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90308732</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pair of harmonized longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort studies of aging and Alzheimer&apos;s disease run at Rush University, the Religious Orders Study (from 1994, nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States) and the Rush Memory and Aging Project (from 1997, lay persons from northeastern Illinois), whose older participants enrol without dementia and agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ROSMAP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ROSMAP 1</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ROSMAP 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Religious Orders Study/Rush Memory and Aging Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Rush</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Religious Orders Study and Rush Memory and Aging Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90308732</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide search for pleiotropy in more than 100,000 harmonized longitudinal cognitive domain scores.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37349795</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10286470/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included non-Hispanic white participants of the Framingham Heart Study (FHS), National Institute on Aging sponsored Alzheimer’s Disease Research Centers whose phenotypic information was assembled and curated by the National Alzheimer’s Coordinating Center (NACC), the Adult Changes in Thought (ACT) Study, the Alzheimer’s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI), and the Religious Orders Study/Rush Memory and Aging Project (ROSMAP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pair of harmonized longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort studies of aging and Alzheimer&apos;s disease run at Rush University, the Religious Orders Study (from 1994, nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States) and the Rush Memory and Aging Project (from 1997, lay persons from northeastern Illinois), whose older participants enrol without dementia and agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
