    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90295958</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A clinic-based prospective cohort of about 57,000 adult Mayo Clinic patients who are US residents, enrolled at Rochester, Minnesota, Jacksonville, Florida and La Crosse, Wisconsin, established to supply control groups for case-control studies, form a prospective cohort for common outcomes and support electronic health record and genotype-driven research.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MAYO</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MAYO clinic biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Mayo Clinic study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mayo Clinic Biobank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90295958</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A large meta-analysis identifies genes associated with anterior uveitis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37949852</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10638276/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We also included 115,418 participants from the MAYO-RGC Project Generation, which brings together the Mayo Clinic Biobank (N = 53,227)49 as well as 30 Mayo-based disease registries/studies who were successfully sequenced.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A clinic-based prospective cohort of about 57,000 adult Mayo Clinic patients who are US residents, enrolled at Rochester, Minnesota, Jacksonville, Florida and La Crosse, Wisconsin, established to supply control groups for case-control studies, form a prospective cohort for common outcomes and support electronic health record and genotype-driven research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31699749</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MAYO</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31699749+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were all Mayo Clinic patients, 18 years of age or older and US residents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90452968</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Danish cohort of children and adolescents, formerly called The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank, run since 2009 from the Children&apos;s Obesity Clinic at Copenhagen University Hospital Holbæk, that combines an obesity clinic cohort with a BMI above the 90th percentile, included continuously and followed longitudinally during multidisciplinary obesity treatment, with a population-based reference cohort recruited cross-sectionally from schools in 11 municipalities in Zealand; by 2020 it held data on more than 5,250 obesity clinic and more than 4,200 population-based participants, with biosamples, genotyping and cardiometabolic phenotyping, as a platform for research on childhood obesity and its complications.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HOLBAEK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TDCOB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Danish Childhood Obesity Data- and Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Holbaek Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HOLBAEK Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90452968</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Plasma proteome variation and its genetic determinants in children and adolescents.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39972214</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11906355/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our discovery cohort included 2,147 children and adolescents aged 5–20 years from the HOLBAEK Study, 45% of whom were from the general population and 55% from the Children’s Obesity Clinic in Holbæk, Denmark (Fig. 1a).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Danish cohort of children and adolescents, formerly called The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank, run since 2009 from the Children&apos;s Obesity Clinic at Copenhagen University Hospital Holbæk, that combines an obesity clinic cohort with a BMI above the 90th percentile, included continuously and followed longitudinally during multidisciplinary obesity treatment, with a population-based reference cohort recruited cross-sectionally from schools in 11 municipalities in Zealand; by 2020 it held data on more than 5,250 obesity clinic and more than 4,200 population-based participants, with biosamples, genotyping and cardiometabolic phenotyping, as a platform for research on childhood obesity and its complications.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39753034</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39972214</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00928473</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HOLBAEK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TDCOB</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11754075/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population consisted of children and adolescents from the HOLBAEK Study (previously known as The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank),17 including an obesity clinic cohort with a BMI above the 90th percentile for sex and age (BMI standard deviation score [SDS] &gt; 1.28) according to a Danish reference; and a population-based cohort, recruited from schools in 11 municipalities in Zealand, Denmark.18</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90296696</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FINNGEN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FinnGen Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FinnGen study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Finngen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">FinnGen</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90296696</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Distinct and shared genetic architectures of gestational diabetes mellitus and type 2 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38182742</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38182742+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted the largest genome-wide association study of GDM to date in 12,332 cases and 131,109 parous female controls in the FinnGen study and identified 13 GDM-associated loci, including nine new loci.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36653562</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.finngen.fi/en</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FINNGEN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Finngen</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9849126/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The FinnGen study (https://www.finngen.fi/en) is an ongoing research project that utilizes samples from a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks and digital healthcare data from national health registers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000312"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90627781</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BRRD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIHR BioResource for Rare Diseases</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIHR BioResource-Rare Diseases</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Institutes of Health Research BioResource-Rare Diseases Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NIHR BioResource Rare Diseases Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90627781</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-Scale Whole-Genome Sequencing Reveals the Genetic Architecture of Primary Membranoproliferative GN and C3 Glomerulopathy.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31919107</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:31919107%20AND%20SRC:MED&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed whole-genome sequence data from 165 primary membranoproliferative GN cases and 10,250 individuals without the condition (controls) as part of the National Institutes of Health Research BioResource-Rare Diseases Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32581362</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BRRD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7610553/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed WGS of 13,037 individuals enrolled at 57 National Health Service (NHS) hospitals in the United Kingdom and 26 hospitals in other countries (Fig. 1a, Extended Data Fig. 1a, Supplementary Table 1), in three batches, to clinical standard (Fig. 1b).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000312"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7610553/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Study participants were enrolled by one of three mechanisms between December 2012 and March 2017 under the overall coordination of the National Institute for Health Research BioResource (NBR) at the University of Cambridge.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90024610</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer&apos;s disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer&apos;s disease and cognitive decline.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ABIL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AIBL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Imaging, Biomarker &amp; Lifestyle study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Imaging, Biomarker and Lifestyle Flagship Study of Ageing</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Imaging, Biomarkers and Lifestyle flagship study of aging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Australian Imaging, Biomarkers and Lifestyle Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Australian Imaging, Biomarker &amp; Lifestyle Flagship Study of Ageing</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
