        <rdfs:comment>It recruited predominantly European (EA), South Asian (SA) and African Caribbean (AC) participants living in West and North London; details have been previously described [20].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90453794</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GALAXY</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GALAXY cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Gut-and-Liver Axis in Alcoholic Liver Fibrosis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90453794</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Plasma proteome variation and its genetic determinants in children and adolescents.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39972214</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11906355/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GALA–ALD/HP, gut and liver axis–alcohol-related liver disease/healthy participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35654907</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/668031</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GALAXY</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11906355/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For replication of the genetic effects on plasma protein levels, we included 1,000 additional children and adolescents from the HOLBAEK Study and 558 adults with alcohol-related liver disease aged 19–82 years, matched with healthy controls recruited from the Region of Southern Denmark5.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90105059</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>YFS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Young Finns Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cardiovascular Risk in Young Finns Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90105059</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetics of osteopontin in patients with chronic kidney disease: The German Chronic Kidney Disease study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35385482</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9015153/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GWAS revealed 3 loci (p&lt;5.0E-08), two of which replicated in the population-based Young Finns Study (YFS) cohort (p&lt;1.67E-03): rs10011284, upstream of SPP1 encoding the OPN protein and related to OPN production, and rs4253311, mapping into KLKB1 encoding prekallikrein (PK), which is processed to kallikrein (KAL) implicated through the kinin-kallikrein system (KKS) in blood pressure control, inflammation, blood coagulation, cancer, and cardiovascular disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38115890</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>YFS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10726240/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The prospective YFS has followed a population-based cohort from childhood to adulthood that were sampled from five cities with university hospitals in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Oulu, Tampere, and Turku) and their rural surrounds.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


