    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Croatia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90668445</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>A Retrospective Study to Identify New &quot;Omics&quot; Biomarkers of Chronic/Persistent Low Back Pain</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PainOMICS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PainOmicc Retrospective Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PainOmics retrospective study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PainOmics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Painomics</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PainOMICS Retrospective Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90668445</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study in 10,000 individuals links plasma N-glycome to liver disease and anti-inflammatory proteins.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40593539</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a multicenter study using data from seven studies – TwinsUK (N = 3918), EPIC-Potsdam (N = 2192), PainOmics (N = 1873), SOCCS (N = 1742), SABRE (N = 544), QMDiab (N = 325), and CEDAR (N = 170) with a total sample size N = 10,764.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27798002</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28459826</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37293449</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789</obo:IAO_0000119>
