    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90093140</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of periodontal pocketing in Finnish adults.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34847907</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34847907+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aim of this study was to investigate genome-wide associations of periodontal condition measured as deepened periodontal pockets (≥ 4 mm) in Finnish adults.MethodsThis study was based on the data of the national Health 2000 Survey (BRIF8901) in Finland and the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 Study totalling 3,245 individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal research programme of the University of Oulu comprising two general-population birth cohorts from the two northernmost provinces of Finland, Oulu and Lapland, the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) and 1986 (NFBC1986), whose members have been followed since the fetal period to study health and well-being.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39820013</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
