    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90809085</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of mothers and children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California from January 2011 to January 2016, oversampling children later diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or other developmental delay alongside general-population controls, with maternal first- and second-trimester blood samples from the RPGEH pregnancy cohort, to study maternal immune and metabolic markers and child neurodevelopment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym IMPaCT also denotes Identification of Men with a genetic predisposition to ProstAte Cancer (COHO:0000097), written IMPACT; this term is Immune and Metabolic Markers during Pregnancy and Child Development Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IMPACT_KPNC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IMPaCT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IMPaCT Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IMPaCT cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Immune and Metabolic Markers during Pregnancy and Child Development Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90809085</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic survey of biomarkers at early and mid-pregnancy identifies pregnancy-specialized immune regulation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42378311</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The IMPaCT cohort included 2436 mothers across three child outcome groups (ASD N = 339, DD N = 1193, GP N = 904) with blood sample measurements taken at two timepoints (14–147 days apart) [S7c Fig] per individual over the first and second trimesters (Fig 1a).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of mothers and children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California from January 2011 to January 2016, oversampling children later diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or other developmental delay alongside general-population controls, with maternal first- and second-trimester blood samples from the RPGEH pregnancy cohort, to study maternal immune and metabolic markers and child neurodevelopment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>IMPACT_KPNC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>IMPaCT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population for the IMPaCT (Immune and Metabolic Markers during Pregnancy and Child Development) Study was selected from children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California (KPNC) from January 2011 to January 2016, who survived to age 2 years and whose mothers received health care during the 2 years prior to delivery.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All mothers had previously provided written consent to participate in the Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health (RPGEH) pregnancy cohort</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000011"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000378"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000381"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000386"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000582"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90029070</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of large prospective population-based cohort studies from the United States and Europe, founded with the Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility-Reykjavik Study, the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Heart Study and the Rotterdam Study, formed to facilitate genome-wide association meta-analyses and replication across cohorts with similarly measured phenotypes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHARGE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHARGE Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90029070</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic analysis of over half a million people characterises C-reactive protein loci.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35459240</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35459240+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We report the largest genome-wide association study (GWAS) on C-reactive protein (CRP), a marker of systemic inflammation, in UK Biobank participants (N = 427,367, European descent) and the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology (CHARGE) Consortium (total N = 575,531 European descent).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444"/>
