    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90244554</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of investigators who attend the National Institute on Drug Abuse Genetics and Epigenetics Cross-cutting Research Team meetings and have genome-wide association data on opioid addiction, pooling previously unpublished genome-wide association studies of opioid addiction from twelve cohort samples, ten with European-ancestry and seven with African-ancestry participants, among them Yale-Penn, the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism and the Urban Health Study in the United States, the Vancouver Injection Drug Users Study in Canada, deCODE in Iceland, the Genetic Epidemiology of Opioid Dependence in Bulgaria study, the Comorbidity and Trauma Study in Australia and the AIDS Linked to the IntraVenous Experience cohort, to study the genetics of opioid addiction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GENOA also denotes Genetic Epidemiology Network of Arteriopathy (COHO:0000434) and Genetics of Opioid Addiction Study (COHO:0000467); this term is Genetics of Opioid Addiction Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENOA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Opioid Addiction Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244554</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-trait genome-wide association study of opioid addiction: OPRM1 and beyond.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36207451</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36207451+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We applied genomic structural equation modeling to conduct a GWAS of the new Genetics of Opioid Addiction Consortium (GENOA) data together with published studies (Psychiatric Genomics Consortium, Million Veteran Program, and Partners Health), comprising 23,367 cases and effective sample size of 88,114 individuals of European ancestry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of investigators who attend the National Institute on Drug Abuse Genetics and Epigenetics Cross-cutting Research Team meetings and have genome-wide association data on opioid addiction, pooling previously unpublished genome-wide association studies of opioid addiction from twelve cohort samples, ten with European-ancestry and seven with African-ancestry participants, among them Yale-Penn, the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism and the Urban Health Study in the United States, the Vancouver Injection Drug Users Study in Canada, deCODE in Iceland, the Genetic Epidemiology of Opioid Dependence in Bulgaria study, the Comorbidity and Trauma Study in Australia and the AIDS Linked to the IntraVenous Experience cohort, to study the genetics of opioid addiction.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36207451</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9546890/supplementaryFiles</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GENOA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9546890/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>V.R., T.T., G.E., D.F.G., K.S., and T.T. contributed the deCODE cohort to the GENOA analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9546890/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>JG, HRK, and HZ contributed the Yale-Penn cohort to the GENOA analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9546890/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>LW, DL, KB, TF, AA, BP, and HE contributed the COGA cohort to the GENOA analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454192</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GENOA also denotes Genetic Epidemiology Network of Arteriopathy (COHO:0000434) and Genetics of Opioid Addiction Consortium (COHO:0000466); this term is Genetics of Opioid Addiction Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENOA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENetics of Opioid Addiction</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Opioid Addiction research collaborative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Opioid Addiction research program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Opioid Addiction Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454192</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association, polygenic risk score and sex study on opioid use disorder treatment outcomes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38102185</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10724251/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data were collected as part of the GENetics of Opioid Addiction (GENOA) and Pharmacogenetics of Opioid Substitution Treatment Response (POST) programs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25187714</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27103815</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37494403</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38102185</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GENOA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10724251/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, participants (nGENOA = 1536, nPOST = 3319) were recruited from 76 CATC sites across Ontario, Canada (GENOA, 2013–2016, POST, 2018–present).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
