        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Southern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90270269</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym REDS-III also denotes REDS-III Brazil Sickle Cell Disease Cohort (COHO:0001397); this term is Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology Donor Evaluation Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>REDS-III</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Recipient Epidemiology Donor Evaluation Study III</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90270269</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of early ischaemic stroke risk in Brazilian individuals with sickle cell disease implicates ADAMTS2 and CDK18 and uncovers novel loci.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36602125</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10155195/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This was conducted within the Brazil Sickle Cell Disease Cohort Study as part of the Recipient Epidemiology Donor Evaluation Study III (REDS-III).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24188564</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>REDS-III</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9763692/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The red blood cell (RBC)-Omics study, part of the larger NHLBI-funded Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study (REDS-III), aims to understand the genetic contribution to blood donor RBC characteristics.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10155195/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Brazil SCD Cohort Study is part of the National Institutes of Health, National Heart Lung and Blood Institute (NHLBI) REDS-III program.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24188564+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The international component consists of distinct programs in Brazil, China, and South Africa, which involve US and in-country investigators.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


