        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90102551</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A health and demographic surveillance and research platform in Guinea-Bissau, run by the Bandim Health Project with Statens Serum Institut, that has followed women and children in an urban surveillance system in the capital, Bissau, since 1978 and in a nationally representative rural surveillance system of 182 clusters since 1989-1990, to study health interventions, child mortality and the non-specific effects of vaccines. Randomised trials are run within it, such as the 2008-2013 trial of early BCG vaccination in low-birth-weight newborns in Bissau.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BHP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Bandim Health Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
