        <rdfs:comment>The cohort from the Center for Applied Genomics is composed of approximately 85,000 juvenile subjects below 18 years of age and of a diverse set of ancestries.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000489"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A paediatric biobank of the Center for Applied Genomics at Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia, recruiting children at the hospital since 2006 with broad consent for research use of their samples and electronic health records (about 85,000 juvenile subjects of diverse ancestries by 2025), used for genome-wide and phenome-wide studies of childhood disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
