    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000496 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000496">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90451702</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ongoing nationwide multicentre observational study in Finland, established in 1997 and run from the Folkhälsan Research Center and the University of Helsinki, of nearly 9,000 adults with type 1 diabetes recruited and clinically characterised at study centres across the country and followed through re-examinations, national registries and medical records, to identify factors leading to diabetic kidney disease and other diabetic complications.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FinnDiane</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FinnDiane Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000496"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90451702</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide characterization of 54 urinary metabolites reveals molecular impact of kidney function.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39746953</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11696681/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The analysis included in total of 8011 individuals from the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study (FinnDiane, n = 3244, including 1632 men and 1612 women)9,10, Generation Scotland (GS, n = 2743, including 1373 men and 1370 women)11, and the VIKING study (VIKING, n = 2024, including 811 men and 1213 women)12 (Fig. 1, Supplementary Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000496"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ongoing nationwide multicentre observational study in Finland, established in 1997 and run from the Folkhälsan Research Center and the University of Helsinki, of nearly 9,000 adults with type 1 diabetes recruited and clinically characterised at study centres across the country and followed through re-examinations, national registries and medical records, to identify factors leading to diabetic kidney disease and other diabetic complications.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39235140</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39746953</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://research.folkhalsan.fi/genetics/finndiane-study</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000496"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FinnDiane</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000496"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11696681/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we performed genome-wide association study (GWAS) meta-analyses in a total of 8011 individuals to investigate single nucleotide variants (SNVs) associated with 54 urinary metabolites measured by NMR in one Finnish cohort of individuals with type 1 diabetes (T1D) and two Scottish cohorts from a general population setting.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


