        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal multicentre genetic-neuroimaging cohort of about 2,000 healthy 14-year-old adolescents recruited from high schools at eight European sites in England, Ireland, France and Germany, followed up at ages 16, 19 and 22 with behavioural, neuropsychological, MRI and genome-wide data, to study the genetic and neurobiological basis of impulsivity, reinforcer sensitivity and emotional reactivity and their value in predicting psychiatric disorders.</obo:IAO_0000115>
