        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90275731</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective observational cohort of adults with proven or probable Lyme borreliosis in the Netherlands, included at the start of antibiotic treatment from 2015 and followed for one year with questionnaires and repeated blood sampling, run by RIVM with the Lyme borreliosis expert centres of Amsterdam UMC and Radboudumc to study the prevalence and determinants of persistent symptoms after treatment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LymeProspect cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LymeProspect study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">LymeProspect</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90275731</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A comprehensive genetic map of cytokine responses in Lyme borreliosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38714679</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11076587/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LymeProspect cohort consisted of 1138 patients with a new physician-confirmed LB (either EM or disseminated manifestation) who were included at the initiation of antibiotic therapy and followed for one year</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective observational cohort of adults with proven or probable Lyme borreliosis in the Netherlands, included at the start of antibiotic treatment from 2015 and followed for one year with questionnaires and repeated blood sampling, run by RIVM with the Lyme borreliosis expert centres of Amsterdam UMC and Radboudumc to study the prevalence and determinants of persistent symptoms after treatment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30987580</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38714679</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6466793/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LymeProspect study has been designed to investigate the prevalence, severity, and a wide range of hypotheses on the etiology of persistent symptoms among patients treated for Lyme borreliosis in the Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


