        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4622045/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study cohort was recruited from the general population living in Nagahama city, a largely rural city of 125,000 inhabitants in Shiga prefecture, located in the center of Japan.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90103632</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CKD Genetics Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CKDGen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CKDGen Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chronic Kidney Disease Genetics (CKDGen) Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chronic Kidney Disease Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90103632</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Discovery and prioritization of variants and genes for kidney function in &gt;1.2 million individuals.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34272381</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:34272381%20AND%20SRC:MED&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>By GWAS meta-analysis for creatinine-based estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) from the Chronic Kidney Disease Genetics Consortium and UK Biobank (n = 1,201,909), we expand the number of eGFRcrea loci (424 loci, 201 novel; 9.8% eGFRcrea variance explained by 634 independent signal variants).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CKDGen</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90239583</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Japanese genome cohort project launched after the 2011 Great East Japan Earthquake and run by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Iwate Medical University, comprising two prospective cohorts in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study of adults and the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study, with an integrated biobank of health information, biospecimens and genome and omics data.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym TMM also denotes Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort Study (COHO:0000938) and Tohoku Medical Megabank Project Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (COHO:0000939); this term is Tohoku Medical Megabank Project.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TMM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ToMMo</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tohoku Medical Megabank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tohoku Medical Megabank Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90239583</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Association Study of Axial Length in Population-based Cohorts in Japan: The Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization Eye Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36246171</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36246171+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 33 483 participants aged &gt; 18 years who were recruited into the community-based cohort (CommCohort) and the birth and three-generation cohort (BirThree Cohort) of the ToMMo Eye Study were examined.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Japanese genome cohort project launched after the 2011 Great East Japan Earthquake and run by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Iwate Medical University, comprising two prospective cohorts in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study of adults and the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study, with an integrated biobank of health information, biospecimens and genome and omics data.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27374138</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TMM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ToMMo</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Tohoku Medical Megabank</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7738642/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To overcome the above-mentioned issues, we established the Tohoku Medical Megabank (TMM) Project, which is conducted by Tohoku University Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (ToMMo) and Iwate Medical University Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (IMM).9 We decided to conduct the TMM Project in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures and started two prospective cohort studies in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures: a population-based adult cohort study, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study (TMM CommCohort Study), which recruited more than 80,000 participants, and a birth and three-generation cohort study, the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (TMM BirThree Cohort Study), which recruited more than 70,000 participants, including fetuses and their parents, siblings, grandparents, and extended family members.10</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7738642/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To overcome the above-mentioned issues, we established the Tohoku Medical Megabank (TMM) Project, which is conducted by Tohoku University Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (ToMMo) and Iwate Medical University Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (IMM).9 We decided to conduct the TMM Project in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures and started two prospective cohort studies in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures: a population-based adult cohort study, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study (TMM CommCohort Study), which recruited more than 80,000 participants, and a birth and three-generation cohort study, the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (TMM BirThree Cohort Study), which recruited more than 70,000 participants, including fetuses and their parents, siblings, grandparents, and extended family members.10</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13175889/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These people were recruited from health checkups conducted in two prefectures of Northeastern Japan: Miyagi (n = 32,459) and Iwate (n = 20,906).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90321087</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym FHCRC also denotes Whole Genome Association Analysis of Hematopoietic Cell Transplant (HCT) Outcomes (COHO:0000535); this term is Fred Hutchinson Prostate Cancer Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FHCRC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center Prostate Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center, Seattle US</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fred Hutchinson Prostate Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90321087</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Germline Genetic Variants Associated with Somatic TMPRSS2:ERG Fusion Status in Prostate Cancer: A Genome-Wide Association Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37555839</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37555839+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association study with 396 TMPRSS2:ERG(+) cases, 390 TMPRSS2:ERG(-) cases, and 2,386 cancer-free controls from the Physicians&apos; Health Study (PHS), the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (HPFS), and a Seattle-based Fred Hutchinson (FH) Cancer Center Prostate Cancer Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17700570</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28145099</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37555839</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FH</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FHCRC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10592169/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The FH Study included 402 European-American male residents of King County, Washington, aged 35–74 years and diagnosed with prostate cancer either in 1993–1996 or in 2002–2005, and underwent radical prostatectomy as primary treatment for clinically localized disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90102555</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A retrospective cohort of patients with a haematological malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome who had a first allogeneic haematopoietic cell transplant at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 to 2011, together with their donors, genotyped to find variants associated with graft-versus-host disease, recurrent malignancy and other complications after transplantation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym FHCRC also denotes Fred Hutchinson Prostate Cancer Study (COHO:0000534); this term is Whole Genome Association Analysis of Hematopoietic Cell Transplant (HCT) Outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FHCRC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FHCRC study cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Fred Hutch cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>STAMPEED: Whole Genome Association Analysis of Hematopoietic Cell Transplant (HCT) Outcomes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Whole Genome Association Analysis of Hematopoietic Cell Transplant (HCT) Outcomes</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90102555</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic associations with immune-mediated outcomes after allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34996099</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The FHCRC study cohort included 4270 recipients of European ancestry who had a first allogeneic HCT with marrow or growth factor-mobilized blood cells at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 through 2011.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A retrospective cohort of patients with a haematological malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome who had a first allogeneic haematopoietic cell transplant at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 to 2011, together with their donors, genotyped to find variants associated with graft-versus-host disease, recurrent malignancy and other complications after transplantation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FHCRC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population represents a large cohort from the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and consists of 4,471 recipients and 4,628 donors containing 4,258 recipient-donor pairs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


