        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family feeding study in rural northern China that recruited 3,153 Han Chinese participants from 658 families, each ascertained through a proband with untreated prehypertension or stage-1 hypertension, of whom 1,906 eligible probands and their siblings, spouses and offspring underwent seven-day low-sodium, high-sodium and high-sodium with potassium supplementation dietary interventions, to localise and identify genes influencing blood pressure responses to dietary sodium and potassium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
