        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of about 1,500 healthy men and women of European ancestry aged 30 to 60, recruited without diabetes, hypertension or dyslipidaemia at centres in 13-14 European countries by the European Group for the Study of Insulin Resistance, with baseline oral glucose tolerance tests and euglycaemic insulin clamps and follow-up after 3 and 10 years to study how insulin resistance relates to atherosclerosis, cardiovascular disease and type 2 diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
