        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90270327</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal cohort of about 11,500 children aged 9-10, including about 1,720 twins, recruited largely through schools at 21 data acquisition sites across the United States to reflect the nation&apos;s diversity, and followed for ten years with annual assessments and biennial MRI to study adolescent brain and cognitive development.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ABCD also denotes Amsterdam Born Children and their Development (COHO:0001451); this term is Adolescent Brain Cognitive Development Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ABCD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ABCD Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ABCD study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
