        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000548"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6428304/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patient recruitment at the baseline visit (Visit 1) was performed from 2/2010 through 8/2014 in two University based study centers in Germany through direct written or spoken invitation to participate, press articles, flyers or public presentations (S1 Fig).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000549 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000549">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90091013</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A US prospective multicentre cohort of men aged 65 or older recruited at six clinical centres (Birmingham, Minneapolis, Palo Alto, near Pittsburgh, Portland and San Diego), designed to examine risk factors for osteoporosis, fractures and prostate cancer in older men, with ancillary studies such as MrOS Sleep (2003-2005, in-home polysomnography of 3,135 men).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MrOS also denotes MrOS Gothenburg (COHO:0000892); this term is Osteoporotic Fractures in Men Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MrOS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MrOS-USA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Osteoporotic Fractures in Men (MrOS) Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Osteoporotic Fractures in Men Study USA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Osteoporotic Fractures in Men Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000549"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90091013</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Whole-genome association analyses of sleep-disordered breathing phenotypes in the NHLBI TOPMed program.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34446064</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8394596/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Osteoporotic Fractures in Men Study (MrOS) is a multi-center cohort study initially designed to examine the risk factors for osteoporosis, fractures, and prostate cancer in older males [28, 29].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000549"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A US prospective multicentre cohort of men aged 65 or older recruited at six clinical centres (Birmingham, Minneapolis, Palo Alto, near Pittsburgh, Portland and San Diego), designed to examine risk factors for osteoporosis, fractures and prostate cancer in older men, with ancillary studies such as MrOS Sleep (2003-2005, in-home polysomnography of 3,135 men).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13269534/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6467367/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8394596/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
