        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90129599</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A European consortium bringing together the European genome-wide association consortia working on Alzheimer disease, which collated and uniformly genotyped a new dataset of about 20,000 clinically diagnosed Alzheimer disease cases and 22,000 controls from 15 European countries and pools them with existing European cohorts for genetic studies of Alzheimer disease and related dementias.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EADB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EADB consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>European Alzheimer DNA BioBank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>European Alzheimer’s Disease DNA Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>European Alzheimer’s and Dementia Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">European Alzheimer &amp; Dementia Biobank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90129599</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide meta-analysis for Alzheimer&apos;s disease cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36066633</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36066633+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Initiated by the European Alzheimer &amp; Dementia Biobank (EADB), the largest collaborative effort on genetics underlying CSF biomarkers was established, including 31 cohorts with a total of 13,116 individuals</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A European consortium bringing together the European genome-wide association consortia working on Alzheimer disease, which collated and uniformly genotyped a new dataset of about 20,000 clinically diagnosed Alzheimer disease cases and 22,000 controls from 15 European countries and pools them with existing European cohorts for genetic studies of Alzheimer disease and related dementias.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35379992</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EADB</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000258"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02838-5/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2838_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The EADB studies (EADI, Bonn, DemGene, GR@ACE/DEGESCO, EADB-core and GERAD) are described in more details in (Bellenguez et al., 2022).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9547780/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the EMIF-AD MBD data, a total of 2,136 proteins were quantified centrally using 11-plex tandem mass tag spectrometry in 366 individuals from the EMIF-AD MBD study [61] (subset of Amsterdam Dementia Cohort within EADB).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9547780/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All, except the Swedisch Birth cohort and clinical AD samples, are part of EADB</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001046"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12092188/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The EADB studies (EADI, Bonn, DemGene, GR@ACE/DEGESCO, EADB-core and GERAD) are described in more details in (Bellenguez et al., 2022)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001062"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13263136/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We applied the same QC protocol to all the EADB studies: EADB-core, EADI, GR@ACE/DEGESCO, GERAD, Bonn and DemGene.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8087277/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Genotyping of the 100-plus Study was performed in the context of EADB (European Alzheimer DNA biobank) funded by the JPco-fuND FP-829-029 (ZonMW project number, 33051061).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001522"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01024-z/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1024_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Belgium: The participants were part of a large prospective cohort1 of Belgian AD patients and healthy elderly control individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02838-5/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2838_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This consortium groups together 20,464 Alzheimer’s disease (AD) cases and 22,244 controls after quality controls from 16 European countries (Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Czech Republic, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Italy, Portugal, Spain, Sweden, Switzerland, The Netherlands and the UK).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


