        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective cohort of 74,942 Chinese women aged 40–70 recruited in 1996–2000 from selected urban communities of Shanghai, most of whom gave blood, urine or buccal-cell samples, followed by biennial in-person recontact and linkage to cancer and vital statistics registries, to study environmental exposures, biomarkers and the risk of cancer and other chronic diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SWHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai Womens Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
