        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of about 2,900 volunteers of Southern Chinese origin aged 15–55 in Hong Kong, openly recruited through newspaper advertisements, posters and e-mails regardless of back symptoms, who underwent lumbar spine MRI, questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, to study the genetic and environmental determinants of intervertebral disc degeneration.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HKDD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HKDDDPC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
