    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000565 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000565">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST000945</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25632367</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective registry and biorepository of Intermountain Healthcare, Utah, begun in 1993, that enrols consenting patients at the cardiac catheterisation laboratories of Intermountain hospitals in Salt Lake City and Ogden, with a blood sample taken at angiography and electronic follow-up for cardiovascular outcomes such as death, myocardial infarction, heart failure and stroke. It was later renamed the INSPIRE biobank registry and now collects samples and data from consenting Intermountain patients with any health condition.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym IHCS also denotes International HIV Controllers Study (COHO:0000917); this term is Intermountain Heart Collaborative Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IHCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IMHC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IMHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INSPIRE biobank registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Intermountain</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Intermountain Heart Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Intermountain Inspire Registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Intermountain Heart Collaborative Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000565"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST000945</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of ADAMTS7 as a novel locus for coronary atherosclerosis and association of ABO with myocardial infarction in the presence of coronary atherosclerosis: two genome-wide association studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21239051</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3297116/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The meta-analysis of angiographic CAD versus control was restricted to those studies that ascertained both cases and controls via coronary angiography. These were PennCath, MedStar, Emory GeneBank, the Intermountain Heart Collaborative Study, and Verona Heart Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000565"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25632367</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Antithrombotic therapy in patients with acute coronary syndrome in the intermountain heart collaborative study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25632367</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4302371/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Study subjects were identified from all persons registered in the Intermountain Heart Collaborative Study (IHCS) with a diagnosis of ACS between 2004 and 2009</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000565"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective registry and biorepository of Intermountain Healthcare, Utah, begun in 1993, that enrols consenting patients at the cardiac catheterisation laboratories of Intermountain hospitals in Salt Lake City and Ogden, with a blood sample taken at angiography and electronic follow-up for cardiovascular outcomes such as death, myocardial infarction, heart failure and stroke. It was later renamed the INSPIRE biobank registry and now collects samples and data from consenting Intermountain patients with any health condition.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29803983</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10482040/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
