        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FVG</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>INGI-FVG</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4997959/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In particular, our study used 370 individuals from INGI-CARL, a population coming from Carlantino, a small village located in Puglia (Southern Italy), and 843 defined as INGI-FVG, making reference to 6 villages situated in the Friuli Venezia Region in North-Eastern Italy for a total of 1207 samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90566795</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>OAI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Osteoarthritis Initiative</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90566795</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Translational genomics of osteoarthritis in 1,962,069 individuals.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40205036</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Osteoarthritis Initiative (OAI) is a prospective longitudinal study designed to identify risk factors for the incidence and progression of symptomatic tibiofemoral knee osteoarthritis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23372535</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>OAI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were recruited at four clinical sites: 1) Brown University (Providence, RI); 2) The Ohio State University (Columbus, OH); 3) University of Maryland and The Johns Hopkins University (Baltimore, MD); and 4) University of Pittsburgh (Pittsburgh, PA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90651081</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SWOG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Southwest Oncology Group</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SWOG Cancer Research Network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90651081</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common variation in a long non-coding RNA gene modulates variation of circulating TGF-β2 levels in metastatic colorectal cancer patients (Alliance).</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38745123</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To this end, we used clinical, genotyping, and pre-treatment candidate protein marker data obtained from patients with mCRC randomized to the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB, now part of the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology (Alliance)) and the Southwest Oncology Group, CALGB/SWOG 80405.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25028457</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27519183</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SWOG</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The US National Cancer Institute (NCI) has developed research networks focused on improving survival and health outcomes for cancer patients through the conduct of large‐scale clinical trials, including the National Clinical Trials Network (NCTN), the NCI Cancer Centers Program, and the NCI Community Oncology Research Program (NCORP). The NCTN provides funding and clinical trial infrastructure support to over 3000 sites via membership in NCTN network groups, including the SWOG Cancer Research Network (SWOG; formerly the Southwest Oncology Group).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
