        <rdfs:comment>WHIMS, an ancillary study of the WHI Hormone Trials, was designed to investigate the effects of hormone therapy (conjugated equine estrogens (CEE) alone vs. placebo or CEE plus medroxyprogesterone [E + P] acetate vs. placebo) on cognitive outcomes among 7479 women aged 65–80 years recruited from 39 clinical sites across the United States who were cognitively unimpaired at randomization (1996–1999)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
