        <obo:IAO_0000115>A long-running programme of studies of type 2 diabetes and related chronic disease among Mexican Americans in Starr County, Texas, on the Texas-Mexico border, run from the University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston, which include a random sample of 14% of the county&apos;s population reported in 1983, type 2 diabetes case-control collections in 1987-2006, and a household survey of randomly selected blocks with examinations in 2002-2006 and re-examinations in 2010-2014, to study the prevalence, risk factors, genetics and complications of diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
