    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32071038</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe trial, in which people aged 40–69 without known diabetes registered with 181 general practices in Denmark were screened stepwise for diabetes in 2001–2006 and those with screen-detected type 2 diabetes, in practices cluster-randomised to routine care or intensive multifactorial treatment (with or without GP training in motivational interviewing), were followed for cardiovascular events and mortality.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ADDITION also denotes Anglo-Danish-Dutch Study of Intensive Treatment in People with Screen Detected Diabetes in Primary Care (COHO:0000614); this term is ADDITION-Denmark.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADDITION</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADDITION study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADDITION-DK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ADDITION-Denmark</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32071038</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The effect of training GPs in motivational interviewing on incident cardiovascular disease and mortality in people with screen-detected diabetes. Results from the ADDITION-Denmark randomised trial.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32071038</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32071038+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the ADDITION-Denmark trial, 181 general practices were cluster randomised in a 2:1:1 ratio to: (i) to screening plus routine care of individuals with screen-detected diabetes (control group);</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe trial, in which people aged 40–69 without known diabetes registered with 181 general practices in Denmark were screened stepwise for diabetes in 2001–2006 and those with screen-detected type 2 diabetes, in practices cluster-randomised to routine care or intensive multifactorial treatment (with or without GP training in motivational interviewing), were followed for cardiovascular events and mortality.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32071038</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADDITION</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADDITION-DK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7330202/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, between 2001 and 2006, a population-based stepwise screening programme was performed among people aged 40–69 years without known diabetes in 181 general practices in Denmark.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7330202/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe study7 was a trial of intensive treatment of people with screen-detected diabetes, which included training in motivational interviewing for GPs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21705063</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pragmatic cluster-randomised trial in 343 general practices in Denmark, the Netherlands and the UK, in which registered patients aged 40–69 without known diabetes were screened and the 3,057 with screen-detected type 2 diabetes received routine care or early intensive multifactorial treatment and were followed for cardiovascular events and death.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ADDITION also denotes ADDITION-Denmark (COHO:0000613); this term is Anglo-Danish-Dutch Study of Intensive Treatment in People with Screen Detected Diabetes in Primary Care.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADDITION</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADDITION-Europe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anglo-Danish-Dutch Study of Intensive Treatment in People with Screen Detected Diabetes in Primary Care</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21705063</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Effect of early intensive multifactorial therapy on 5-year cardiovascular outcomes in individuals with type 2 diabetes detected by screening (ADDITION-Europe): a cluster-randomised trial.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21705063</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3136726/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a pragmatic, cluster-randomised, parallel-group trial done in Denmark, the Netherlands, and the UK, 343 general practices were randomly assigned screening of registered patients aged 40–69 years without known diabetes followed by routine care of diabetes or screening followed by intensive treatment of multiple risk factors.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pragmatic cluster-randomised trial in 343 general practices in Denmark, the Netherlands and the UK, in which registered patients aged 40–69 without known diabetes were screened and the 3,057 with screen-detected type 2 diabetes received routine care or early intensive multifactorial treatment and were followed for cardiovascular events and death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21705063</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
