        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12973162/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the SCCS enrolled ~85,000 English‐speaking individuals aged 40–79 years during years 2002–2009 in 12 states in the southeastern United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Taiwan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90707270</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based cohort of more than 565,000 participants recruited by Academia Sinica with 16 major medical centres across Taiwan, genotyped on arrays optimised for Han Chinese ancestry and linked to retrospective and prospective electronic medical records, for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk studies of common disease and pharmacogenetic response.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TPMI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Taiwan Precision Medicine Initiative</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90707270</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic risk loci for Parkinson&apos;s disease and dementia in a large-scale population-based Taiwanese cohort (TPMI).</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41810385</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41810385+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we investigated genetic risk factors for PD and PDD in Taiwanese individuals from the Taiwan Precision Medicine Initiative (TPMI), the largest non-European cohort integrating genetic and electronic medical record data.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based cohort of more than 565,000 participants recruited by Academia Sinica with 16 major medical centres across Taiwan, genotyped on arrays optimised for Han Chinese ancestry and linked to retrospective and prospective electronic medical records, for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk studies of common disease and pharmacogenetic response.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41092961</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TPMI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Taiwan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41092961+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we present the Taiwan Precision Medicine Initiative (TPMI), established by Academia Sinica in collaboration with 16 major medical centres around Taiwan, which has recruited 565,390 participants who consent to provide DNA samples for genetic profiling and grant access to their electronic medical records (EMRs) for research.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90134637</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal family-based cohort of highly admixed residents of Baependi, a small rural town in Minas Gerais, Brazil, recruited from 2005 through probands and their relatives and followed up in 2010 and 2016 to study genetic and environmental influences on cardiovascular risk factors, sleep, circadian rhythms and mental health.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym BHS also denotes Busselton Health Study (COHO:0000389) and Bogalusa Heart Study (COHO:0000464); this term is Baependi Heart Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BAEPENDI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Baependi</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Baependi Heart Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90134637</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide analyses identify SCN5A as a susceptibility locus for premature atrial contraction frequency.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36267918</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9576575/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Baependi Heart Study was set up in 2005 to develop a longitudinal family-based cohort study that reflects on some of the genetic and lifestyle-related peculiarities of the Brazilian populations, in order to evaluate genetic and environmental influences on CVD risk factor traits (Egan et al., 2016).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal family-based cohort of highly admixed residents of Baependi, a small rural town in Minas Gerais, Brazil, recruited from 2005 through probands and their relatives and followed up in 2010 and 2016 to study genetic and environmental influences on cardiovascular risk factors, sleep, circadian rhythms and mental health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27797990</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BAEPENDI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Baependi</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27797990+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Probands were recruited in Baependi, a small rural town in the state of Minas Gerais, Brazil, following by first-degree and then increasingly more distant relatives.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
