    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90321087</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of US male physicians enrolled in two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, PHS I (begun in 1982 with 22,071 physicians aged 40–84) and PHS II, testing low-dose aspirin, beta-carotene and vitamins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer, and followed thereafter as a prospective cohort.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Physicians Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Physicians&apos; Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90321087</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Germline Genetic Variants Associated with Somatic TMPRSS2:ERG Fusion Status in Prostate Cancer: A Genome-Wide Association Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37555839</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37555839+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>However, few studies have investigated germline genetic variants associating with TMPRSS2:ERG fusion status.MethodsWe performed a genome-wide association study with 396 TMPRSS2:ERG(+) cases, 390 TMPRSS2:ERG(-) cases, and 2,386 cancer-free controls from the Physicians&apos; Health Study (PHS), the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (HPFS), and a Seattle-based Fred Hutchinson (FH) Cancer Center Prostate Cancer Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of US male physicians enrolled in two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, PHS I (begun in 1982 with 22,071 physicians aged 40–84) and PHS II, testing low-dose aspirin, beta-carotene and vitamins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer, and followed thereafter as a prospective cohort.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38893188</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11171146/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>PHS I was initiated in 1982 and was a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of 22,071 US male physicians aged 40–84 years aimed at evaluating the impact of aspirin and beta-carotene on cardiovascular disease (CVD) and cancer outcomes, respectively [22].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627">
