        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of 1,091 people born in 1936 who took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Survey of 1947, recruited in 2004–2007 at a mean age of 70, mostly living in Edinburgh and the Lothians, and retested about every 3 years with cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging and lifestyle assessments to study non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LBC1936</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
