        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sample collected at the University of Munich, Germany, of about 3,000 healthy volunteers of German descent from the Munich area, assessed with structured psychiatric interviews covering themselves and their first-degree relatives, together with about 1,000 patients with schizophrenia and about 300 people with other diagnoses, including Alzheimer&apos;s disease patients from the psychiatric memory clinic, used as a case and control resource in genetic studies of psychiatric, neurological and neurodegenerative disorders.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym PAGES also denotes Paediatric Asthma Gene Environment Study (COHO:0000721); this term is Phenomics and Genomics Sample.</obo:IAO_0000116>
