        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90255648</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium formed under the Slim Initiative in Genomic Medicine for the Americas that pooled type 2 diabetes case-control samples of Mexicans and other Latin Americans from the Diabetes in Mexico Study, the Mexico City Diabetes Study, the Multiethnic Cohort Study and the UNAM/INCMNSZ Diabetes Study to characterise the genetic basis of type 2 diabetes in Mexican and Latin American populations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SIGMA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SIGMA Type 2 Diabetes Genetics Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Slim Initiative for Genomic Medicine in the Americas</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Slim Initiative in Genomic Medicine for the Americas</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Slim Initiative in Genomic Medicine for the Americas Type 2 Diabetes Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>T2D SIGMA Studies</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SIGMA Type 2 Diabetes Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000736"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90255648</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The power of TOPMed imputation for the discovery of Latino-enriched rare variants associated with type 2 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37148359</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244266/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We aggregated data from six Latino cohorts with a sample size of 18,885 individuals (8150 with type 2 diabetes [cases] and 10,735 without [controls]): the Slim Initiative for Genomic Medicine in the Americas (SIGMA) [1–3]; the Mexican Biobank (MXBB) [10]; the Mass General Brigham (MGB) Biobank [11]; and the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging (GERA) [12] (Fig. 1 and ESM Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
