        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90432107</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A research cohort of customers of the AncestryDNA consumer genetic testing service who consented to AncestryDNA&apos;s Human Diversity Project and contribute genotype data and survey responses to genetic studies, including a COVID-19 survey of US-based adult customers used in genome-wide association studies of COVID-19 and influenza outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AncestryDNA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AncestryDNA cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AncestryDNA research participants</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Human Diversity Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">AncestryDNA Human Diversity Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000742"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90432107</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic risk factors for COVID-19 and influenza are largely distinct.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39103650</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11319199/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To understand the extent to which the same host genetic factors influence the risk of coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) and influenza, we first performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of influenza infection based on survey data from 296,313 participants of the AncestryDNA COVID-19 study who consented to the research8.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000742"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A research cohort of customers of the AncestryDNA consumer genetic testing service who consented to AncestryDNA&apos;s Human Diversity Project and contribute genotype data and survey responses to genetic studies, including a COVID-19 survey of US-based adult customers used in genome-wide association studies of COVID-19 and influenza outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35410379</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39103650</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000742"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AncestryDNA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000742"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11319199/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>US-based AncestryDNA customers over the age of 18 who had consented to the research, were invited to complete five surveys assessing COVID-19 outcomes, as well as providing other demographic information and comorbidities, as described previously8.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


