    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90308728</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-site, multi-generational family study in which probands recruited through alcohol treatment centres and their relatives, together with community comparison families, have been assessed over more than 30 years (nearly 18,000 individuals from over 2200 families) with psychiatric interviews, questionnaires, electrophysiology and DNA to identify genetic factors in alcohol use disorder and related outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COGA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90308728</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genomic risk for post-traumatic stress disorder in families densely affected with alcohol use disorders.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37344610</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37344610+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We examined genome-wide associations for DSM-IV PTSD among 4,978 trauma-exposed participants (31% with alcohol dependence, 50% female, 30% African ancestry) from the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism (COGA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-site, multi-generational family study in which probands recruited through alcohol treatment centres and their relatives, together with community comparison families, have been assessed over more than 30 years (nearly 18,000 individuals from over 2200 families) with psychiatric interviews, questionnaires, electrophysiology and DNA to identify genetic factors in alcohol use disorder and related outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37581339</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>COGA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10550787/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>At the study&apos;s inception, high‐risk families were ascertained through probands who were undergoing treatment for AUDs at six sites across the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000024"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000547"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000618"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000732"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90502765</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A colorectal cancer genetic epidemiology consortium, approved at the University of Southern California and funded within the NCI GAME-ON post-GWAS initiative, that pools genome-wide genotype data from colorectal cancer case-control studies such as the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Study, the Colon Cancer Family Registry and the Kentucky and Newfoundland case-control studies to find and characterise colorectal cancer susceptibility variants.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CORECT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ColoRectal Transdisciplinary Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Colorectal Cancer Transdisciplinary Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90502765</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association studies and Mendelian randomization analyses provide insights into the causes of early-onset colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38408508</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11213623/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a GWAS meta-analysis of 6176 EOCRC cases and 65 829 controls from the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium (GECCO), the Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study (CORECT), the Colon Cancer Family Registry (CCFR), and the UK Biobank.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A colorectal cancer genetic epidemiology consortium, approved at the University of Southern California and funded within the NCI GAME-ON post-GWAS initiative, that pools genome-wide genotype data from colorectal cancer case-control studies such as the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Study, the Colon Cancer Family Registry and the Kentucky and Newfoundland case-control studies to find and characterise colorectal cancer susceptibility variants.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25105248</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
