    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000783 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000783">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90319889</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective cohort of about 140,000 registered residents aged 40–69 years in 11 public health centre areas across Japan, enrolled as Cohort I in 1990 and Cohort II in 1993 with questionnaires, blood samples and health check-up data and followed with repeat surveys, to study causes of cancer, cardiovascular disease and other diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>JPHC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>JPHC Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Japan Public Health Center Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study on Cancer and Cardiovascular Diseases</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000783"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90319889</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic architecture of alcohol consumption identified by a genotype-stratified GWAS and impact on esophageal cancer risk in Japanese people.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38277453</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10816704/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The J-CGE consisted of the following Japanese population-based and hospital-based studies: the HERPACC Study (25), the J-MICC Study (26, 27), the JPHC Study (28), and the TMM Study (29).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000783"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based prospective cohort of about 140,000 registered residents aged 40–69 years in 11 public health centre areas across Japan, enrolled as Cohort I in 1990 and Cohort II in 1993 with questionnaires, blood samples and health check-up data and followed with repeat surveys, to study causes of cancer, cardiovascular disease and other diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:11763136</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25104790</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000783"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>JPHC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000783"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10816704/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 175,672 individuals were included in this GWAS meta-analysis of six Japanese cohorts, namely, the Hospital-based Epidemiologic Research Program at Aichi Cancer Center (HERPACC) Study (n = 4958) (25), the Japan Multi-Institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) Study (n = 13,236) (26, 27), the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective (JPHC) Study (n = 10,037) (28), the Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort (TMM) Study (n = 7857) (29), the Nagahama Prospective Cohort for Comprehensive Human Bioscience (Nagahama) Study (n = 4591) (30), and the BioBank Japan (BBJ) Study (n = 134,993) (31, 32) after imputation and quality control (QC) of individual subject genotype data (Supplementary Materials and tables S1 and S2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000377"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000688"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001017"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90308666</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-ancestry consortium that combined genome-wide association data from 29 studies (67,162 stroke cases and 454,450 controls, mainly of European and East Asian ancestry) in a meta-analysis of stroke and its aetiological subtypes, drawing on contributing groups such as METASTROKE, SiGN, CHARGE and COMPASS.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MEGASTROKE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MEGASTROKE project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MegaStroke</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MegaStroke consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MEGASTROKE consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90308666</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry meta-analysis identifies 5 novel loci for ischemic stroke and reveals heterogeneity of effects between sexes and ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37601974</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37601974+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide meta-analysis of 16 biobanks across multiple ancestries to study the genetics of ischemic stroke (60,176 cases, 1,310,725 controls) as part of the Global Biobank Meta-analysis Initiative (GBMI) and further combined the results with previously published MegaStroke.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-ancestry consortium that combined genome-wide association data from 29 studies (67,162 stroke cases and 454,450 controls, mainly of European and East Asian ancestry) in a meta-analysis of stroke and its aetiological subtypes, drawing on contributing groups such as METASTROKE, SiGN, CHARGE and COMPASS.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29531354</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MEGASTROKE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MegaStroke</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000377"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>BioBank Japan Project was started in 2003 and collected DNA and clinical information from a total of 200,000 patients suffering from at least one of 47 common diseases.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5968830/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Consortia providing stroke data: COMPASS Consortium, EPIC-CVD Consortium, EPIC-InterAct Consortium, ISGC, METASTROKE Consortium, Neurology Working Group of the CHARGE Consortium, NINDS-SiGN, UK Young Lacunar DNA Study, and MEGASTROKE Consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5968830/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Consortia providing stroke data: COMPASS Consortium, EPIC-CVD Consortium, EPIC-InterAct Consortium, ISGC, METASTROKE Consortium, Neurology Working Group of the CHARGE Consortium, NINDS-SiGN, UK Young Lacunar DNA Study, and MEGASTROKE Consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000688"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5968830/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Consortia providing stroke data: COMPASS Consortium, EPIC-CVD Consortium, EPIC-InterAct Consortium, ISGC, METASTROKE Consortium, Neurology Working Group of the CHARGE Consortium, NINDS-SiGN, UK Young Lacunar DNA Study, and MEGASTROKE Consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001017"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Case and control subjects included in the discovery phase were subjects of European ancestry aged &gt;55 years in the Genetics of Cerebral Hemorrhage with Anticoagulation13 (GOCHA) study (multicenter study in the US) and aged &gt;18 years in the Genetic and Environmental Risk Factors for Hemorrhagic Stroke (GERFHS) studies I and II in Cincinnati, OH; Hospital del Mar Intracerebral Hemorrhage study and Vall d’Hebron Hospita lCH study in Barcelona, Spain; Jagiellonian University Hemorrhagic Stroke Study in Krakow, Poland; and the Lund Stroke Register study in Lund, Sweden.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000785 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000785">
