    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000787"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90501352</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome- and phenome-wide association study of plasma procalcitonin concentrations in individuals of European ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41406505</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12902255/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The two Swedish cohorts “Malmö Diet and Cancer study” (MDCS) and “Malmö Preventive Project” (MPP) have ethics approval from the Regional Ethics Committee at the University of Lund (LU 51–90, LU 244-02, and Dnr 2009/633).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000787"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of 33,346 residents of the city of Malmö in southern Sweden, recruited by pre-specified birth-year groups for health examinations from 1974 to 1992, whose samples and data are used in genetic and biomarker studies of disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12902255/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000787"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MPP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000787"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12902255/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We included participants from three cohorts for the GWAS meta-analysis: the Malmö Diet and Cancer study (MDCS) and the Malmö Preventive Project (MPP), both consisting of participants from the city of Malmö in southern Sweden; the Prevention of REnal and Vascular ENd-stage Disease (PREVEND) study, consisting of participants from the city of Groningen in northern Netherlands; and conducted the PheWAS in the UK Biobank (UKB) from the United Kingdom.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


