    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Singapore"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South-Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000763"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90011771</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SIMES</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SiMES</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Singapore Malay Eye Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90011771</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association for HbA1c in Malay Identified Deletion on SLC4A1 that Influences HbA1c Independent of Glycemia.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32936915</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32936915+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Genetic determinants of HbA1c can vary across populations and many of the genetic variants influencing HbA1c level were specific to populations.ObjectiveTo discover genetic variants associated with HbA1c level in nondiabetic Malay individuals.Design and participantsWe conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) analysis for HbA1c using 2 Malay studies, the Singapore Malay Eye Study (SiMES, N = 1721 on GWAS array) and the Living Biobank study (N = 983 on GWAS array and whole-exome sequenced).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17365815</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SIMES</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SiMES</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Singapore"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17365815+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study summarizes the rationale and study design of a population-based study of eye diseases among adult Malays in Singapore.MethodsA population-based cross-sectional study of Malays was designed in Singapore.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000763"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10630666/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>At baseline visit, Malay, Indian, and Chinese subjects from SEED were recruited under 3 studies: the Singapore Malay Eye Study (year 2004–2006), the Singapore Indian Eye Study (year 2007–2009), and the Singapore Chinese Eye Study (year 2009–2011).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
