        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Spanish study included cases newly diagnosed with urothelial carcinoma of the bladder between 1998 and 2001 at 18 hospitals in five regions of Spain and hospital controls individually matched to the cases on age at diagnosis/interview, sex, and hospital (706 White cases and 772 White controls with complete exposure information and genotyping data).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841456</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women&apos;s and Children&apos;s Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese MONN cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MONN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MONN study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SZ-MONN-NIPT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Shenzhen Maternal and Neonatal NIPT cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841456</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry, trans-generational GWAS meta-analysis of gestational diabetes and glycaemic traits during pregnancy reveals limited evidence of pregnancy-specific genetic effects.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42225636</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13226718/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The largest and most recent GDM GWASs to date include the FinnGen study (12,332 cases; 131,109 controls; European ancestry)21 and the MONN study (12,024 cases; 67,845 controls; East Asian ancestry)29, which together identified 27 loci associated with GDM.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women&apos;s and Children&apos;s Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38064665</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38372780</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40325049</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MONN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SZ-MONN-NIPT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We integrated NIPT data and time-dependent platelet count measurements in 5 periods of pregnancy and conducted, to the best of our knowledge, the first and the hitherto largest-scale GWAS on platelet count and GT during pregnancy, among 100 186 Chinese pregnant women from 2 hospitals at Shenzhen, China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90449045</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A series of clinically and neuropathologically characterised brain donors with Alzheimer disease and cognitively normal elderly controls, assembled by the Translational Genomics Research Institute (Phoenix, United States) from NIA-supported Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Center brain banks, the Miami Brain Bank and brain banks in the United Kingdom and the Netherlands, and genotyped for genome-wide association studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease within the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TGEN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TGEN2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TGen series</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Translational Genomics Research Institute</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Translational Genomics Research Institute series 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90449045</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>X-chromosome-wide association study for Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39633006</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12092188/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The sex-stratified models were adjusted on PCs and/or the genotyping center only, except for two ADGC studies (PFIZER and TGEN2) and the CHARGE studies (FHS, RS and CHS), where models were additionally adjusted on age (Supplementary Table S6 and Supplementary Material).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A series of clinically and neuropathologically characterised brain donors with Alzheimer disease and cognitively normal elderly controls, assembled by the Translational Genomics Research Institute (Phoenix, United States) from NIA-supported Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Center brain banks, the Miami Brain Bank and brain banks in the United Kingdom and the Netherlands, and genotyped for genome-wide association studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease within the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39633006</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TGEN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TGEN2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4154667/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The TGen series was also funded by NIA grant AG041232, the Banner Alzheimer&apos;s Foundation, The Johnnie B. Byrd Sr. Alzheimer&apos;s Institute, the Medical Research Council, and the state of Arizona and also includes samples from the following sites: Newcastle Brain Tissue Resource (funding via the Medical Research Council, local NHS trusts and Newcastle University), MRC London Brain Bank for Neurodegenerative Diseases (funding via the Medical Research Council), South West Dementia Brain Bank (funding via numerous sources including the Higher Education Funding Council for England (HEFCE), Alzheimer&apos;s Research Trust (ART), BRACE as well as North Bristol NHS Trust Research and Innovation Department and DeNDRoN), The Netherlands Brain Bank</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000800 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000800">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90243964</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A lung cancer genetic epidemiology consortium, one of the NIH-funded GAME-ON post-GWAS consortia and working with the International Lung Cancer Consortium, that integrates genome-wide data from multiple lung cancer studies of European populations to identify lung cancer susceptibility loci.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TRICL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Transdisciplinary Research In Cancer of the Lung</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Transdisciplinary Research In Cancer of the Lung (TRICL) Research Team</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Transdisciplinary Research in Cancer of the Lung</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000800"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90243964</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Analysis of Lung Cancer and the Germline Impact on Somatic Mutation Burden.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35511172</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9360465/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The family history GWAS (GWAx) on 48 843 self-reported family history LC patients and 195 387 controls from the UK Biobank (Supplementary Table 1, available online) identified 5 loci (5p15.33, 6p21.32, 12p13.33, 13q13.1, and 15q25.1) that had previously been discovered from the traditional GWAS previously performed on the Transdisciplinary Research In Cancer of the Lung cohort (Supplementary Table 2 and Supplementary Figure 1, available online).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000800"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A lung cancer genetic epidemiology consortium, one of the NIH-funded GAME-ON post-GWAS consortia and working with the International Lung Cancer Consortium, that integrates genome-wide data from multiple lung cancer studies of European populations to identify lung cancer susceptibility loci.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42152146</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000800"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TRICL</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90709864</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MCS also denotes HARMONISATION study (COHO:0001101); this term is UK Millennium Cohort Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Millennium Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UKMillennium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">UK Millennium Cohort Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90709864</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic heterogeneity and homogeneity among orofacial cleft subtypes: genome-wide association studies in the cleft collective.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41075272</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12627943/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Genotyping was performed on 200 ng of DNA using the Illumina Infinium global screening array-24 v1.0 in the Millennium cohort (606 434 SNPs) and using the Illumina Infinium global screening array-24 v3.0 in the Cleft Collective (645 027 SNPs).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24550246</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
