    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000817 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000817">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90624144</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ongoing longitudinal cohort of primarily middle-aged adults, all cognitively unimpaired at enrolment from the community, begun in 1995 in the National Institutes of Health intramural program and later continued at Johns Hopkins University, with repeated cognitive, clinical, CSF, blood and MRI assessments to study the earliest phases of Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BIOCARD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BIOCARD cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BIOCARD study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Biomarkers for Older Controls at Risk for Dementia</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Biomarkers of Cognitive Decline Among Normal Individuals</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624144</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Novel modelling approaches to elucidate the genetic architecture of resilience to Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40111762</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC12295682/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data from participants were sourced from an array of cohort studies, including the Adult Changes in Thought (ACT) Study, the Alzheimer’s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI), Biomarkers for Older Controls at Risk for Dementia (BIOCARD), the Baltimore Longitudinal Study of Aging (BLSA), the National Alzheimer’s Coordinating Center (NACC), the Religious Orders Study (ROS), the Rush Memory and Aging Project (MAP), the Minority Aging Research Study (MARS), the Washington University Memory &amp; Aging Project (WASHU) and the Wisconsin Registry for Alzheimer’s Prevention (WRAP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ongoing longitudinal cohort of primarily middle-aged adults, all cognitively unimpaired at enrolment from the community, begun in 1995 in the National Institutes of Health intramural program and later continued at Johns Hopkins University, with repeated cognitive, clinical, CSF, blood and MRI assessments to study the earliest phases of Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41604611</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
