        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S030228382302780X-mmc3.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Los Angeles Bladder Cancer Study (LABCS)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000830"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer in Los Angeles County, United States, with cases aged 25–64 diagnosed in 1987–1996 identified through the Los Angeles County Cancer Surveillance Program and matched neighbourhood controls, used to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19174821</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000830"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LABCS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000830"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2653778/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We collected detailed information on UTIs in a large population-based case–control study of bladder cancer in Los Angeles County, where we have identified risk factors including cigarette smoking (Castelao et al, 2001) and use of permanent hair dyes among women (Gago-Dominguez et al, 2001, 2003), and protective factors including use of non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) (Castelao et al, 2000) and consumption of carotenoids and vitamin C (Castelao et al, 2004).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000831 -->

