    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pakistan"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90432122</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A growing biobank and national consortium of case–control studies in Pakistan that aims to enrol one million participants (about 250,000 from 48 clinical sites in 17 cities by September 2023) across some 50 diseases, with whole-exome sequencing and recontact, used for genetic association and loss-of-function studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PGR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pakistan Genome Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pakistan Genomics Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pakistan Genomic Resource</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90432122</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>NOTCH3 p.Arg1231Cys is markedly enriched in South Asians and associated with stroke.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39271666</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399414/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study focused on two distinct cohorts, including 75 K individuals from the Pakistan Genomic Resource (PGR) and 380 K individuals (n = 380,537) from the United Kingdom Biobank (UKB) The PGR 75 K individuals were recruited and consented in Pakistan for whole exome sequencing (WES) (n = 75,819), including a stroke case:control discovery cohort of 31 K (n = 31,737; n = 5135 cases and n = 26,602 controls) sequenced by the Regeneron Genetics Center and a follow-up cohort of 44 K (n = 44,082), including 30 K with self-report stroke case:control status used for replication and meta-analysis (n = 30,399; n = 160 cases and n = 30,239 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A growing biobank and national consortium of case–control studies in Pakistan that aims to enrol one million participants (about 250,000 from 48 clinical sites in 17 cities by September 2023) across some 50 diseases, with whole-exome sequencing and recontact, used for genetic association and loss-of-function studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39271666</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pakistan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399414/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>PGR is a growing biobank that aims to enroll 1 million participants across Pakistan and as of September 2023, ~250,000 participants across n = 48 clinical sites in n = 17 cities from all over Pakistan have been enrolled.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST009965</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, randomised, placebo-controlled smoking-cessation trial (NCT01314001) run from 2010 to 2014 at four academic medical centres in the United States and Canada, in which 1246 treatment-seeking smokers stratified by nicotine metabolite ratio were assigned to placebo, nicotine patch or varenicline.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PNAT-2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PNAT2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pharmacogenetics of Nicotine Addiction Treatment (PNAT)-2 clinical trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pharmacogenetics of Nicotine Addiction and Treatment clinical trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pharmacogenetics of Nicotine Addiction Treatment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST009965</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis of nicotine metabolism and cigarette consumption measures in smokers of European descent.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32157176</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7483250/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In support of this, a secondary analysis in PNAT2 showed no apparent impact of the rs56113850 T allele on increasing (COT+3HC)/CPD (Figure S13).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, randomised, placebo-controlled smoking-cessation trial (NCT01314001) run from 2010 to 2014 at four academic medical centres in the United States and Canada, in which 1246 treatment-seeking smokers stratified by nicotine metabolite ratio were assigned to placebo, nicotine patch or varenicline.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25588294</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
