        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90094399</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based study of residents of the municipality of Tromsø, Norway, run by UiT The Arctic University of Norway, begun in 1974 and repeated in seven surveys (Tromsø1–Tromsø7) that together enrolled 45,473 people, as a multipurpose health survey of chronic diseases and their risk factors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Tromso Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Tromsø Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tromso</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tromso Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tromsø Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000852"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90094399</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Elevated plasma concentration of complement factor C5 is associated with risk of future venous thromboembolism.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34339498</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34339498+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We wanted to investigate (1) whether plasma complement component C5 (C5) levels are influenced by genetic variants or chronic inflammation and (2) the association between plasma C5 and risk of future VTE in a nested case-control study of 415 patients with VTE and 848 age- and sex-matched controls derived from the Tromsø Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000852"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study of residents of the municipality of Tromsø, Norway, run by UiT The Arctic University of Norway, begun in 1974 and repeated in seven surveys (Tromsø1–Tromsø7) that together enrolled 45,473 people, as a multipurpose health survey of chronic diseases and their risk factors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12184346/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000852"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Tromso</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000852"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12184346/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Tromsø Study is a population-based study conducted in 1974 in the municipality of Tromsø, Norway.17 It consists of seven waves, known as Tromsø1 through Tromsø7, and a total of 45 473 people attended one or more surveys.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


