    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90624411</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of cohort and case-control studies with genome-wide genotype data that pools them in meta-analyses of genome-wide association studies of atrial fibrillation, to identify genetic loci for atrial fibrillation; together with the Broad AF Study, its studies formed the majority of the 2018 multi-ethnic meta-analysis of more than half a million individuals.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AFGen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AFGen Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Atrial Fibrillation Genetics (AFGen) consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Atrial Fibrillation Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624411</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Cross-population GWAS and proteomics improve risk prediction and reveal mechanisms in atrial fibrillation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40645996</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12254421/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eight studies (the Nord-Trøndelag Health Study [HUNT], deCODE, DiscoverEHR, Michigan Genomics Initiative [MGI], AFGen consortium4, FinnGen R12, Swedish Infrastructure for Medical Population-Based Life-Course and Environmental Research [SIMPLER, https://www.simpler4health.se/], and Million Veteran Program[MVP]) contributed to the discovery analysis for the European GWAS, comprising 192,851 atrial fibrillation (AF) cases and 1,239,541 controls6,41,42.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of cohort and case-control studies with genome-wide genotype data that pools them in meta-analyses of genome-wide association studies of atrial fibrillation, to identify genetic loci for atrial fibrillation; together with the Broad AF Study, its studies formed the majority of the 2018 multi-ethnic meta-analysis of more than half a million individuals.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29892015</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AFGen</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3843/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3843_MOESM307_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The meta-analyses described in this manuscript included the following studies described elsewhere: The Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility Study (AGES) Reykjavik study169 , the Atrial Fibrillation Biobank LMU (AFLMU) in the context of the Arrhythmia-Biobank-LMU (formerly known as AFNET) and the Cooperative Health Research in the Region of Augsburg (KORA)169</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


