        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90448086</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Cardiovascular Resilience Identifies Protective Variation in the CETP Gene.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37929782</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37929782+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our discovery genome-wide association study of N=12 031 ASCVD event-free individuals from the ASPREE (Aspirin in Reducing Events in the Elderly) trial identified 2 independent variants, rs9939224 (P-8) and rs56156922 (P-6), in the CETP (cholesteryl ester transfer protein) gene.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A placebo-controlled randomized trial of daily low-dose aspirin in 19,114 community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over (65 or over for US minorities) in Australia and the United States without prior cardiovascular events, dementia or independence-limiting physical disability, followed as a cohort after the trial to study healthy ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40796244</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ASPREE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12596486/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ASPREE was a large-scale placebo-controlled randomized trial (NCT01038583) of daily low-dose (100 mg) enteric-coated aspirin conducted in 19 114 adults aged over 70 years residing in Australia and the USA (≥ 65 years for US minorities) who had no prior cardiovascular events, dementia, or independence-limiting physical disability at trial enrolment.21 The median enrolment age of the cohort was 74 years [interquartile range (IQR) 72–78 ].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000857 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000857">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
