        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective single-centre population-based study of community-dwelling elderly people without stroke or dementia, randomly selected from the community register of Graz, Austria, and enrolled between 1991 and 2004, examining the effects of vascular risk factors on brain structure and function in normal ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ASPS also denotes Austrian Stroke Prevention Family Study (COHO:0000858); this term is Austrian Stroke Prevention Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ASPS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Austrian Stroke Prevention Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90239648</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic architecture of orbital telorism.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34791242</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9071440/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In short, we included 34 130 participants from four population-based studies, namely the UK Biobank (20) (N = 28 919), the Austrian Stroke Prevention Study (ASPS) (N = 183), the ASPS Family Study (ASPS-Fam) (21,22) (N = 302) and the Rotterdam Study (23,24) (N = 4726).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective single-centre population-based study of community-dwelling elderly people without stroke or dementia, randomly selected from the community register of Graz, Austria, and enrolled between 1991 and 2004, examining the effects of vascular risk factors on brain structure and function in normal ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8064143/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
