    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000861 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000861">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90435134</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of about 1,220 mainly vaccine-naive individuals with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, across the full spectrum from asymptomatic to critical COVID-19, recruited early in the pandemic at 16 sites in Germany and South Tyrol, Italy, by a national host-genetics consortium built on the German COVID-19 Omics Initiative, with whole genome sequencing to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DeCOI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">DeCOI cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000861"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90435134</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Systematic assessment of COVID-19 host genetics using whole genome sequencing data.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39715278</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11706450/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Following quality control (see Methods), the DeCOI cohort comprised 1,220 individuals from across the entire phenotypic spectrum of SARS-CoV-2 infections (Figs 1A–1C and S1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000861"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of about 1,220 mainly vaccine-naive individuals with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, across the full spectrum from asymptomatic to critical COVID-19, recruited early in the pandemic at 16 sites in Germany and South Tyrol, Italy, by a national host-genetics consortium built on the German COVID-19 Omics Initiative, with whole genome sequencing to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39715278</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000861"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DeCOI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000861"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11706450/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the host genetic analyses participants were recruited at 16 different sites, 15 of which were situated in Germany, and one in the German-speaking region of Italy (South Tyrol), from individual COVID-19 studies that were being conducted at the respective institutions.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


