        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multidisciplinary, multi-institutional cohort of about 1,600 older adults aged 60–80 and 600 younger adults aged 20–35 recruited as volunteers in the Berlin metropolitan area, Germany, with baseline assessments completed in 2014 across geriatrics, internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics, to identify factors associated with healthy versus unhealthy ageing; a subsample of the older group was re-examined in 2018–2020 in the GendAge study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
