    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000913"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90277442</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic architecture of vitamin B12 and folate levels uncovered applying deeply sequenced large datasets.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23754956</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3674994/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Health2006 is a population-based epidemiological study of general health, diabetes and cardiovascular disease of 3,471 individuals aged 18–74 years [48].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000913"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of 3,471 adults aged 18–69, randomly sampled from the Danish Central Personal Register in the southern part of Copenhagen and examined in 2006–2008 at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Denmark, to study general health, allergy, diabetes and cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3674994/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5300151/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000913"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Health2006</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000913"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5300151/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>They were recruited from the Danish Central Personal Register as random samples of the population in the southern part of Copenhagen and included questionnaires, physical examinations, and blood tests as previously described in detail [9,10].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000914 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000914">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90013452</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal population-based study of 5,133 adults from the German city of Heidelberg and its surroundings, started in the 1990s with a baseline battery of health-related personality questionnaires to characterise associations between personality and somatic disease, and later followed up and genotyped.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HeiDE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HeiDE study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Heidelberger Langzeitstudie zu Risikofaktoren und Diagnose chronischer Erkrankungen</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000914"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90013452</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Heidelberg Five personality dimensions: Genome-wide associations, polygenic risk for neuroticism, and psychopathology 20 years after assessment.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33590662</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33590662+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>HeiDE is a longitudinal population-based study that started in the 1990s and, at baseline, assessed an array of health-related personality questionnaires in 5133 individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000914"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal population-based study of 5,133 adults from the German city of Heidelberg and its surroundings, started in the 1990s with a baseline battery of health-related personality questionnaires to characterise associations between personality and somatic disease, and later followed up and genotyped.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33590662</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8503053/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000914"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HeiDE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000914"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8503053/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, HeiDE (‘Heidelberger Langzeitstudie zu Risikofaktoren und Diagnose chronischer Erkrankungen’) is a population-based study carried out in the German city of Heidelberg and surrounding area with an initial aim of characterising associations of personality and somatic disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000868"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90827692</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A global collaboration of 51 studies from 11 countries with genome-wide genotyping and data on heart failure events and prognosis, including population-based cohorts, hospital-based electronic health record cohorts, case-control studies and clinical trials, formed to conduct large-scale genetic association studies of heart failure risk, prognosis and subtypes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HERMES</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HERMES Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Heart Failure Molecular Epidemiology for Therapeutic Targets</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Heart Failure Molecular Epidemiology for Therapeutic Targets Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90827692</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Body Mass Index, Clinical Outcomes, and Mortality in Heart Failure: A Mendelian Randomization Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42017882</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13211948/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Twenty-two cohorts participating in the Heart Failure Molecular Epidemiology for Therapeutic Targets (HERMES) Consortium, comprising 50,636 individuals with established HF of European ancestry, were included in the genetic study (Supplemental Table 2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A global collaboration of 51 studies from 11 countries with genome-wide genotyping and data on heart failure events and prognosis, including population-based cohorts, hospital-based electronic health record cohorts, case-control studies and clinical trials, formed to conduct large-scale genetic association studies of heart failure risk, prognosis and subtypes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34480422</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HERMES</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Cardiovascular Health Study (CHS) is a population-based cohort study of risk factors for heart disease and stroke in adults ≥65 years conducted across four field centers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Framingham Heart Study (FHS) is a community-based cohort that enrolled three generations of participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BioVU cohort consisted of patients at Vanderbilt University Medical Center who have consented to be a part of the program.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The deCODE Icelandic heart failure (HF) sample set included patients diagnosed with HF at Landspitali – The National University Hospital (LUH) in Reykjavik and the Primary Health Care Clinics of the Reykjavik capital region, following ICD-9 and ICD-10 codes for heart failure, as described in this manuscript.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000868"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Henry Ford Heart Failure Pharmacogenomic Registry (HFPGR) was approved by the Institutional Review Board at the Henry Ford Health System, and all patients gave written informed consent prior to participation.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>TRIUMPH (TRanslational Initiative on Unique and novel strategies for Management of Patients with Heart failure, NTR1893), is an observational prospective study of patients admitted with acute HF in 14 hospitals in the Netherlands between September 2009 and December 2013.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8712846/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the nine case collections, seven were primarily focused on HF while two identified HF cases from an at‐risk population (COGEN and LURIC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000916 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000916">
