    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000925 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000925">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST000679</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection of families with multiple siblings affected by rheumatoid arthritis, gathered in the United States by the North American Rheumatoid Arthritis Consortium using well-defined clinical criteria and a severe-phenotype selection of probands, later extended with case-control collections (NARAC-II, NARAC-III), for linkage and association studies of rheumatoid arthritis genetics.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NARAC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NARAC dataset</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">North American Rheumatoid Arthritis Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST000679</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study meta-analysis identifies seven new rheumatoid arthritis risk loci.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20453842</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4243840/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study expands upon our previous GWAS meta-analysis of 3,393 cases and 12,462 controls by (a) adding a new GWAS dataset of 483 RA cases recruited from the Boston area (Brigham Rheumatoid Arthritis Sequential Study, BRASS) and 1,449 shared controls, (b) adding 513 cases and 431 controls recruited from Sweden (Epidemiological Investigation of Rheumatoid Arthritis, EIRA), (c) incorporating a recently published GWAS of 2,418 cases and 4,504 controls recruited from North America (Canada and North American Rheumatoid Arthritis Consortium-III, NARAC-III), and (d) adding additional shared controls to the NARAC-III dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of families with multiple siblings affected by rheumatoid arthritis, gathered in the United States by the North American Rheumatoid Arthritis Consortium using well-defined clinical criteria and a severe-phenotype selection of probands, later extended with case-control collections (NARAC-II, NARAC-III), for linkage and association studies of rheumatoid arthritis genetics.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:11254450</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NARAC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11254450+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We report the first major genomewide screen of multiplex families with RA gathered in the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90559273</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The central national biobank of South Korea, opened by the Korea National Institute of Health as the hub of the Korea Biobank Network with regional hospital biobanks, which holds and distributes biospecimens and data from general-population cohort studies such as the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study and from hospital patients for biomedical and public health research.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NBK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">National Biobank of Korea</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90559273</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>rs762855 single nucleotide polymorphism modulates the risk for diffuse-type gastric cancer in females: a genome-wide association study in the Korean population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39862296</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11842433/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Furthermore, from the National Biobank of Korea (NBK) (https://biobank.nih.go.kr/cmm/main/engMainPage.do), we obtained genetic data from 803 patients with GC, including 394 with DGC and 409 with IGC, whose genotypes were sequenced using the Affy 6.0 platform.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The central national biobank of South Korea, opened by the Korea National Institute of Health as the hub of the Korea Biobank Network with regional hospital biobanks, which holds and distributes biospecimens and data from general-population cohort studies such as the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study and from hospital patients for biomedical and public health research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24159511</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24159540</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NBK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11842433/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition, within the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study (KoGES) database, housed in the NBK, the control group comprised 3,693 urban residents from KoGES_health examinee (KoGES_HEXA) and 1,816 rural residents from KoGES_cardiovascular disease association study (KoGES_CAVAS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8898610/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For access and sharing, biological resources of the BICWALZS were stored in the BICWALZS consortium biobank (www.bicwalzs.com/) as well as the National Biobank of Korea (www.nih.go.kr/biobank) which is a central biobank supporting for the Korea Biobank Project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24159511+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Korea Biobank Project, which was initiated in 2008, constructed the Korea Biobank Network consisting of the National Biobank of Korea (NBK) with 17 regional biobanks in Korea.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000927 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000927">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000986"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90837544</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective cohort of more than 140,000 participants in Norrbotten and Västerbotten, the two northernmost regions of Sweden, initiated in the mid-1980s and managed by Umeå University, combining three sub-cohorts (the Västerbotten Intervention Programme, the expanded Northern Sweden MONICA study and the Mammography Screening Project) with over 240,000 stored blood samples, for research on the aetiology, prevention and early detection of cancer, cardiovascular and other diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NSHDS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Northern Swedish Health and Disease Study Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000927"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90837544</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genomic and transcriptomic analyses of aortic stenosis enhance therapeutic target discovery and disease prediction.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41419686</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12807872/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study (NSHDS) comprises three sub-surveys, the Västerbotten Intervention Program (VIP), the Northerns Sweden MONICA study and the Mammography Screening Program (MSP), whereof VIP and MONICA are actively recruiting.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000927"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based prospective cohort of more than 140,000 participants in Norrbotten and Västerbotten, the two northernmost regions of Sweden, initiated in the mid-1980s and managed by Umeå University, combining three sub-cohorts (the Västerbotten Intervention Programme, the expanded Northern Sweden MONICA study and the Mammography Screening Project) with over 240,000 stored blood samples, for research on the aetiology, prevention and early detection of cancer, cardiovascular and other diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11790227/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000927"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NSHDS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000927"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11790227/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The NSHDS is a population-based prospective longitudinal cohort comprising &gt;140 000 participants in the two northernmost regions in Sweden, Norrbotten and Västerbotten, with &gt;240 000 blood samples and 1.5 million person-years of follow-up.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000928 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000928">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90129576</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Ontario site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which enrolled women with invasive breast cancer diagnosed in 1996–1998 identified through the Ontario Cancer Registry (all those aged 20–54 at high genetic risk and random samples of others, with high-risk cases diagnosed in 2001–2002 added), together with their relatives and population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BCFR-CA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BCFR-ON</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BCFR-ONT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>OFBCR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ontario Breast Cancer Family Registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ontario site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ontario Familial Breast Cancer Registry</rdfs:label>
