        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym TMM also denotes Tohoku Medical Megabank Project (COHO:0000533) and Tohoku Medical Megabank Project Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (COHO:0000939); this term is Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
