        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective birth cohort of pregnant South Asian women aged 18–40 and their offspring, recruited in urban Bangalore and rural Solur in Karnataka, India, and in the Peel region of Ontario, Canada, with questionnaires, anthropometry, a glucose tolerance test, and blood and DNA samples in pregnancy, newborn measurements and follow-up of the children to age 3, to study the environmental and genetic determinants of adiposity among South Asians.</obo:IAO_0000115>
