        <dcterms:title>Trans-ancestry genome-wide association study of childhood body mass index identifies novel loci and age-specific effects.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39885687</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11875162/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Early Growth Genetics (EGG) Consortium is a collaboration of multiple GWAS efforts to identify genetic loci that impact multiple traits related to early growth.16 We obtained summary statistics from the most recently published childhood standardized BMIz GWAS16 (excluding participants from the Norwegian Mother and Child Cohort [MoBa]) for inclusion in our meta-analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
