        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454593</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective observational cohort of postmenopausal Danish women enrolled in 1999–2001, all of whom had previously taken part in randomised placebo-controlled trials or been screened for earlier studies at the Center for Clinical and Basic Research in Copenhagen or Aalborg, established to identify risk factors for age-related diseases and linked to the Danish health registries.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PERF</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Epidemiologic Risk Factor study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Epidemiologic and Risk Factor study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Epidemiological Risk Factor cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Epidemiological Risk Factor study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>prospective epidemiological risk factor study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prospective Epidemiological Risk Factor Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454593</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Citrullinated and MMP-degraded vimentin is associated with chronic pulmonary diseases and genetic variants in PADI3/PADI4 and CFH in postmenopausal women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38155185</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10754934/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this paper we conducted a genome wide association study (GWAS) and phenome wide association study (PheWAS) for the VICM biomarker using the Prospective Epidemiologic Risk Factor (PERF) study13, an observational cohort with 5855 women linked to the Danish health registries.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective observational cohort of postmenopausal Danish women enrolled in 1999–2001, all of whom had previously taken part in randomised placebo-controlled trials or been screened for earlier studies at the Center for Clinical and Basic Research in Copenhagen or Aalborg, established to identify risk factors for age-related diseases and linked to the Danish health registries.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38155185</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
