    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001196"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001199"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90002423</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>A Multiethnic Genome-wide Scan of Prostate Cancer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Multiethnic Genome-wide Scan of Prostate Cancer</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90002423</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ethnic transcriptome-wide association study of prostate cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32986714</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32986714+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To better understand the genetic risk for prostate cancer across diverse populations, we performed PrediXcan and GWAS in a case-control study of 4,769 self-identified African American (2,463 cases and 2,306 controls), 2,199 Japanese American (1,106 cases and 1,093 controls), and 2,147 Latin American (1,081 cases and 1,066 controls) individuals from the Multiethnic Genome-wide Scan of Prostate Cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Controls were matched to cases on race/ethnicity, area of residence (California or Hawaii) and age at entry into cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study we plan to undertake a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of prostate cancer in the Multiethnic Cohort (MEC) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90444398</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ASTARRS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Army STARRS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Army Study To Assess Risk and rEsilience in Servicemembers</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Army Study to Assess Risk and Resilience in Service Members</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Army Study to Assess Risk and Resilience in Service members</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Army study to assess risk and resilience in servicemembers</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Army-STARRS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Army Study to Assess Risk and Resilience in Servicemembers</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Army Study to Assess Risk and Resilience in Servicemembers</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90444398</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Uncommon Protein-Coding Variants Associated With Suicide Attempt in a Diverse Sample of U.S. Army Soldiers.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38141912</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38141912+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we advance this search for genetic risk by analyzing the association between suicide attempt and uncommon variation exome-wide in a large, ancestrally diverse sample.MethodsWe sequenced whole genomes of 13,584 soldiers from the Army STARRS (Army Study to Assess Risk and Resilience in Servicemembers), including 979 individuals with a history of suicide attempt.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30104726</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958"/>
