        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841394</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family-based asthma genetics study initiated in Barbados in 1993 on nuclear and extended families, self-reported as African Caribbean, of paediatric asthmatic probands referred from local polyclinics or the Accident and Emergency Department of the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, with recruitment continuing through the Chronic Disease Research Centre in Barbados.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BAGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Barbados Genetics of Asthma Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Genetics and Epidemiology of Asthma in Barbados</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Barbados Asthma Genetics Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841394</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Determinants of mosaic chromosomal alteration fitness.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38714703</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11076528/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 1993, the Barbados Asthma Genetics Study (BAGS) was initiated on nuclear and extended asthmatic families who self-reported as African Caribbean, resulting in the first evidence for linkage for asthma and tIgE in an African-ancestry population, and the development of novel family-based methods.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family-based asthma genetics study initiated in Barbados in 1993 on nuclear and extended families, self-reported as African Caribbean, of paediatric asthmatic probands referred from local polyclinics or the Accident and Emergency Department of the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, with recruitment continuing through the Chronic Disease Research Centre in Barbados.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15940135</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38714703</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BAGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Barbados"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11076528/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Recruitment into the BAGS program was enhanced through its involvement in the international Genetics of Asthma International Network (1999-2001) and the current sample of &gt;1300 participants continues to grow through the efforts of collaborators and nursing staff at the Chronic Disease Research Centre in Barbados.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90129576</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d&apos;Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CECILE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CECILE Breast cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CECILE Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CECILE study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CECILE Breast Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90129576</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide interaction analysis of menopausal hormone therapy use and breast cancer risk among 62,370 women.</dcterms:title>
