        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90090980</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre case-control study of female breast cancer conducted in Seoul, South Korea, since 1995, which recruited women with histologically confirmed incident breast cancer at university hospitals in Seoul, among them Seoul National University Hospital and Asan Medical Center, and cancer-free controls from health examinees at the same hospitals or in community health screening programmes, collecting risk-factor information by face-to-face interviews with a structured questionnaire.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SEBCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SeBCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Seoul Breast Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000966"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90090980</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of novel breast cancer susceptibility loci in meta-analyses conducted among Asian and European descendants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32139696</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7057957/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study also contributed 5,574 cases and 3,793 controls 106 for the replication study genotyped by Sequenom. 107 Seoul Breast Cancer Study (SeBCS): 108 The SeBCS is a hospital-based case-control study conducted in two teaching hospitals 109 in Seoul.9,10 Total 2,342 incident breast patients histopathologically diagnosed with 110 primary breast cancer were included in this project and they were consecutively 111 recruited between 2001 and 2007.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
