        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90897930</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, conducted in 1992–1995 at 21 sickle cell referral centres in the United States and Canada, of whether hydroxyurea reduces vaso-occlusive events in adults with sickle cell anaemia and frequent painful episodes, whose participants were then followed observationally in 1996–2001.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MSH also denotes BioMe Biobank (COHO:0000424); this term is Multicenter Study of Hydroxyurea in Sickle Cell Anemia.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MSH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MSH_CSA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Multicenter Study of Hydroxyurea</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Multicenter Study of Hydroxyurea in Patients With Sickle Cell Anemia</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Multicenter Study of Hydroxyurea in Sickle Cell Anemia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000987"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90897930</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>FLT1 and other candidate fetal haemoglobin modifying loci in sickle cell disease in African ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40025045</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11873275/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohorts included: Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease (CSSCD: n = 841), Multicenter Study of Hydroxyurea (MSH: n = 178), Pulmonary Hypertension and the Hypoxic Response in Sickle Cell Disease (PUSH) study (n = 73), Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers Collaborative Data (C-data) project (n = 127), Treatment of Pulmonary Hypertension and Sickle Cell Disease with Sildenafil Treatment (Walk-PHaSST) trial (n = 181), Duke University Outcome Modifying Genes study (n = 152), and Silent Infarct Transfusion (SIT) trial (SITT: n = 488).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000987"/>
