    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21738479</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A network of cohorts of African ancestry and of other populations under-represented in genome-wide association studies, whose consortia meta-analyse the cohorts&apos; genome-wide data to find genetic variants for complex traits, such as white blood cell count, blood pressure and hypertension in African-ancestry cohorts (COGENT-BP) and kidney traits across diverse ancestries (COGENT-Kidney, established in 2014).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COGENT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Continental Origins and Genetic Epidemiology Network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21738479</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of white blood cell count in 16,388 African Americans: the continental origins and genetic epidemiology network (COGENT).</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21738479</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3128101/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The subjects participating in the GWAS consisted of a total of 16,388 self-identified African-American individuals from 7 population-based cohorts (ARIC, CARDIA, JHS, WHI, HANDLS, Health ABC, and GeneSTAR) that belong to the Continental Origins and Genetic Epidemiology Network (COGENT).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
