    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90103973</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The cohort studies of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, established in 2000 by the University of Pittsburgh in partnership with West Virginia University to find the factors behind poor oral health in northern Appalachia. They are a family-based etiology study (COHRA1), which recruited households in West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, and a longitudinal cohort (COHRA2), which since 2011 has recruited pregnant women in Pennsylvania and West Virginia and followed them and their children.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COHRA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90103973</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Analyses of Enamel Hypoplasia in Multiethnic Cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35172313</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our second cohort (n = 1,837) comes from the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia (COHRA), which was designed to address oral health disparities in the Appalachian region in the USA.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The cohort studies of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, established in 2000 by the University of Pittsburgh in partnership with West Virginia University to find the factors behind poor oral health in northern Appalachia. They are a family-based etiology study (COHRA1), which recruited households in West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, and a longitudinal cohort (COHRA2), which since 2011 has recruited pregnant women in Pennsylvania and West Virginia and followed them and their children.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18522740</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35172313</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36981009</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
