    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90245867</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FISSIC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Fangshan Family-Based Ischemic Stroke Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Fangshan Family-Based Ischemic Stroke Study in China</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Fangshan/Family-based Ischemic Stroke Study In China</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Fangshan/Family-based Ischemic Stroke Study in China</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fangshan Family-based Ischemic Stroke Study in China</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90245867</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of Novel Metabolic Subtypes Using Multi-Trait Limited Mixed Regression in the Chinese Population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36551856</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36551856+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To deconstruct the heterogeneity, we used baseline data from phase II of the Fangshan Family-Based Ischemic Stroke Study (FISSIC), and a total of 4632 participants were included.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17825112</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31823830</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36551856</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42259975</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FISSIC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9775185/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>FISSIC is an ongoing community observational study that started in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90558311</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FTLD-TDP WGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FTLD-TDP WGS International consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FTLD-TDP WGS consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>International FTLD-TDP WGS consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Whole genome sequencing consortium on Frontotemporal dementia with underlying TDP-43 pathology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>international FTLD-TDP whole-genome sequencing consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">International FTLD-TDP Whole-Genome Sequencing Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90558311</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Deciphering distinct genetic risk factors for FTLD-TDP pathological subtypes via whole-genome sequencing.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40280976</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40280976+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We report our comprehensive genome-wide association study as part of the International FTLD-TDP Whole-Genome Sequencing Consortium, including 985 patients and 3,153 controls compiled from 26 institutions/brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia, and meta-analysis with the Dementia-seq cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30739198</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40280976</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FTLD-TDP WGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40280976+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We report our comprehensive genome-wide association study as part of the International FTLD-TDP Whole-Genome Sequencing Consortium, including 985 patients and 3,153 controls compiled from 26 institutions/brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia, and meta-analysis with the Dementia-seq cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90134661</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GELCC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90134661</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Cross-ancestry genome-wide meta-analysis of 61,047 cases and 947,237 controls identifies new susceptibility loci contributing to lung cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35915169</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01115-x/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1115_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cross-ancestry genome-wide meta-analyses were conducted in the twelve different studies consisting of Affymetrix Axome Array Study (AFFY), the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia (FLCCA), the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium (GELCC), the Environment and Genetics in Lung cancer Etiology study (EAGLE), Helmholtz-Gemeinschaft Deutscher Forschungszentren Lung Cancer GWAS (GERMAN), the International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC), the Institute of Cancer Research (ICR), MD Anderson Cancer Center Study (MDACC), NCI Lung Cancer and Smoking Phenotypes in African- American Cases and Controls (NCI), OncoArray Consortium Lung Study (ONCO), the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO), and Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute Study (SLRI).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15272417</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29924316</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41390056</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.gelcc.org/node/3</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GELCC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13259588/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GELCC is a U.S.-based research network studying FLC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90101797</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenHAT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatments</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Hypertension-Associated Treatment</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90101797</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Contributors of Incident Stroke in 10,700 African Americans With Hypertension: A Meta-Analysis From the Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatments and Reasons for Geographic and Racial Differences in Stroke Studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34992631</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34992631+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Methods: In a population comprising over 10,700 AAs treated for hypertension from the Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatments (GenHAT) and Reasons for Geographic and Racial Differences in Stroke (REGARDS) studies, we performed an inverse variance-weighted meta-analysis of incident stroke.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12439737</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21887284</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26791477</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35886043</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GenHAT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3160956/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We note that both the Black and Hispanic groups likely had diverse ancestry given that participants were recruited in the US, Canada, and the Caribbean; therefore, some degree of population substructure is expected.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90132135</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Bergen, Norway COPD Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenKOLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of COPD in Norway Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90132135</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study of bronchodilator response in participants of European and African ancestry from six independent cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35769418</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9234425/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Six non-overlapping cohorts contributed to our primary analysis: the Framingham Heart Study (FHS) [21]; Genetic Epidemiology of COPD (COPDGene) [22]; Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate End-points (ECLIPSE) [23]; Treatment of Emphysema with a Gamma-Selective Retinoid Agonist (TESRA) [24]; the Bergen, Norway COPD Cohort, Genetics of Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease (GenKOLS) [25]; and the Subpopulations and Intermediate Outcome Measures in COPD Study (SPIROMICS) [26].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19300482</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25134640</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25241909</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31413559</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32944202</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
