    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454271</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROCAM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROCAM-2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PROCAM-2 Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454271</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A meta-analysis of genome-wide studies of resilience in the German population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39112778</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11746137/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, this study included participants with available genotype data and the relevant phenotypic information from the BiDirect Study (N = 1453) [7], the FOR2107 consortium (N = 1789) [8], the PROCAM-2 Study (N = 3879) [9, 10], both SHIP cohorts (SHIP-START/-LEGEND, N = 2230; SHIP-TREND, N = 2330) [11, 12], and the LIFE-Adult-Study (N = 4141) [13, 14].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38839884</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39112778</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
