        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11746137/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The independent studies recruited participants of European descent from the population living in and around the cities of Münster, Marburg, Greifswald and Leipzig, Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Austria"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90020165</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PsyCourse</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PsyCourse study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PsyCourse Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90020165</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study of the longitudinal course of executive functions.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34247186</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8272719/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the transdiagnostic PsyCourse Study, comprising patients of the affective-to-psychotic spectrum and controls, we investigated the genetic basis of the time course of two core executive subfunctions: set-shifting (Trail Making Test, part B (TMT-B)) and updating (Verbal Digit Span backwards) in 1338 genotyped individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30070057</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39721961</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PsyCourse</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Austria"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8272719/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We included 1338 genotyped individuals (dataset version 3.0) recruited in different centers in Germany and Austria, comprising patients from the affective-to-psychotic spectrum (377 bipolar I disorder, 100 bipolar II disorder, 420 schizophrenia, 95 schizoaffective disorder, 6 brief psychotic disorder, 9 schizophreniform disorder, and 73 with recurrent depression) and 258 psychiatrically healthy controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90558252</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Q-MEGA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Queensland Study of Melanoma: environmental and genetic associations</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Queensland study of Melanoma: Environment and Genetic Associations</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Queensland study of Melanoma: Environmental and Genetic Associations</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Queensland study of Melanoma: Environmental and Genetics Associations</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Queensland Study of Melanoma: Environmental and Genetic Associations</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90558252</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Exploring the Germline Genetics of In Situ and Invasive Cutaneous Melanoma: A Genome-Wide Association Study Meta-Analysis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39141363</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39141363+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three genome-wide association study meta-analyses were conducted of in situ melanoma vs controls, invasive melanoma vs controls, and in situ vs invasive melanoma (case-case) using 4 population-based genetic cohorts: the UK Biobank, the FinnGen cohort, the QSkin Sun and Health Study, and the Queensland Study of Melanoma: Environmental and Genetic Associations (Q-MEGA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18361720</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Q-MEGA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Q-MEGA brings together four population-based studies of CMM that were conducted in Queensland, Australia between 1987 and 1995 (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032">
