        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90301368</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A double-blind, randomised, multicentre trial run from 1996 to 2003 at 56 hospitals and neurology practices in the United States, Canada and Scotland, in which adults aged 35 or older with a recent nondisabling ischaemic stroke and a screening plasma homocysteine above the 25th percentile received high-dose or low-dose folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12, to test whether lowering homocysteine prevents recurrent stroke.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>VISP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
