    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A3044083+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To address many of these issues in the United States, the Federal Government has established an AIDS Clinical Trials Group (ACTG) program.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90705064</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>A Genetic Association study in Diverse Ancestries of Multiple Sclerosis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADAMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADAMS project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">genetic Association study in individuals from Diverse Ancestral backgrounds with Multiple Sclerosis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90705064</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Determinants of Multiple Sclerosis Susceptibility in People From Diverse Ancestral Backgrounds.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41791023</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41791023+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We recruited and genotyped a cohort of ancestrally diverse people with MS (pwMS) from across the United Kingdom.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37197821</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADAMS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10193065/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The genetic Association study in individuals from Diverse Ancestral backgrounds with Multiple Sclerosis (ADAMS) project aims to gather genetic and phenotypic data on a large cohort of ancestrally-diverse individuals with MS living in the UK.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Southern_Africa"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90243990</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ADVANCE also denotes Atherosclerotic Disease, Vascular Function, and Genetic Epidemiology Study (COHO:0001053) and Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease: Preterax and Diamicron-MR Controlled Evaluation (COHO:0001474); this term is ADVANCE trial.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADVANCE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADVANCE Study of DTG + TAF + FTC vs DTG + TDF + FTC and EFV + TDF+FTC in First-line Antiretroviral Therapy</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WRHI 060</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ADVANCE trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90243990</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Pharmacogenetics of Dolutegravir Plasma Exposure Among Southern Africans With Human Immunodeficiency Virus.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35512135</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35512135+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We characterized the pharmacogenetics of dolutegravir exposure after ART initiation in the ADVANCE trial in South Africa.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31339677</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03122262</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADVANCE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35512135+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We characterized the pharmacogenetics of dolutegravir exposure after ART initiation in the ADVANCE trial in South Africa.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST003116</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ADVANCE also denotes ADVANCE trial (COHO:0001052) and Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease: Preterax and Diamicron-MR Controlled Evaluation (COHO:0001474); this term is Atherosclerotic Disease, Vascular Function, and Genetic Epidemiology Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADVANCE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Atherosclerotic Disease VAscular functioN and genetiC Epidemiology study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Atherosclerotic Disease, VAscular FunctioN, and GenetiC Epidemiology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Atherosclerotic Disease, VAscular functioN, and genetiC Epidemiology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Atherosclerotic Disease, Vascular function, and Genetic Epidemiology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Atherosclerotic Disease, Vascular Function, and Genetic Epidemiology Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST003116</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A comprehensive 1,000 Genomes-based genome-wide association meta-analysis of coronary artery disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26343387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4589895/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Detailed descriptions of the eligibility criteria and the source population for all groups in the multi ethnic ADVANCE study are provided elsewhere</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18413559</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18443000</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21917174</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27030599</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADVANCE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4589895/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, between October 28, 2001 and December 31, 2003, 3,179 member of the Kaiser Permanente of Northern California health maintenance organization were enrolled into three CAD groups and two control groups.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90559231</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of elderly residents of Bordeaux, France, recruited from 2006 as an ophthalmological follow-up nested within the Three-City Study, assessing associations between eye diseases such as age-related macular degeneration and nutritional factors through plasma measurements, dietary-intake estimation and repeated eye examinations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ALIENOR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Alienor</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Antioxydants Lipides Essentiels Nutrition et Maladies Oculaires</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Antioxydants, LIpides Essentiels, Nutrition et maladies OculaiRes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Antioxydants, Lipides Essentiels, Nutrition et maladies OculaiRes</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90559231</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>HTRA1/lncRNA HTRA1-AS1 dominates in age-related macular degeneration reticular pseudodrusen genetic risk with no complement involvement.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41361163</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12685958/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Alienor cohort was funded by Laboratoires Théa (Clermont-Ferrand, France), Université de Bordeaux (Bordeaux, France), Fondation Voir et Entendre (Paris, France), Agence Nationale de la Recherche (2010-PRSP-011), CFSR Recherche (Club Francophone des Spécialistes de la Rétine), the French Ministry of Health (PHRC, 2012, PHRC12_157 ECLAIR) and CNSA (Caisse Nationale pour la Solidarité et l’Autonomie) (Paris, France).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of elderly residents of Bordeaux, France, recruited from 2006 as an ophthalmological follow-up nested within the Three-City Study, assessing associations between eye diseases such as age-related macular degeneration and nutritional factors through plasma measurements, dietary-intake estimation and repeated eye examinations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21125205</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26084364</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34203817</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40808916</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ALIENOR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Alienor</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26084364+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Antioxydants, Lipides Essentiels, Nutrition et maladies OculaiRes (ALIENOR) is a population-based study on eye diseases performed in elderly residents of Bordeaux, France.</rdfs:comment>
