        <rdfs:comment>The ALIENOR study included 963 participants aged ≥73 years from the Three-City (3C) study in Bordeaux, for an ophthalmic follow-up.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90104085</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson&apos;s Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson&apos;s disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients&apos; spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson&apos;s disease with less diagnostic misclassification.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>APDGC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Autopsy-Confirmed PD GWAS Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Autopsy-Confirmed Parkinson Disease Genetics Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Autopsy-confirmed Parkinson Disease GWAS Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Autopsy-Confirmed Parkinson Disease GWAS Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104085</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common X-Chromosome Variants Are Associated with Parkinson Disease Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33583074</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8601399/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PD cohorts include the International PD Genomics Consortium (IPDGC) NeuroX dataset, the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke (NINDS) PD dataset, the Autopsy-Confirmed PD GWAS Consortium (APDGC) dataset genotyped by the Center for Inherited Disease Research, the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium (NGRC) dataset, the UK PD Consortium, and the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2, referred to here as EBI MERGE.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson&apos;s Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson&apos;s disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients&apos; spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson&apos;s disease with less diagnostic misclassification.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25663231</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
