        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90239836</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sample of people in the United Kingdom with treatment-resistant schizophrenia who were prescribed clozapine, whose anonymised blood samples and clinical monitoring data were obtained through the clozapine monitoring services, first in collaboration with Novartis and later through the Zaponex Treatment Access System (second wave 2013–15, third wave 2019–21), for Cardiff University&apos;s genetic studies of schizophrenia and clozapine metabolism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CLOZUK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The CLOZUK cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CLOZUK study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90239836</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Pharmacokinetics and pharmacogenomics of clozapine in an ancestrally diverse sample: a longitudinal analysis and genome-wide association study using UK clinical monitoring data.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36804072</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36804072+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this GWAS, we analysed data from the UK Zaponex Treatment Access System clozapine monitoring service as part of the CLOZUK study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A sample of people in the United Kingdom with treatment-resistant schizophrenia who were prescribed clozapine, whose anonymised blood samples and clinical monitoring data were obtained through the clozapine monitoring services, first in collaboration with Novartis and later through the Zaponex Treatment Access System (second wave 2013–15, third wave 2019–21), for Cardiff University&apos;s genetic studies of schizophrenia and clozapine metabolism.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22614287</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36804072</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CLOZUK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10824469/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The fact that CLOZUK participants were recruited solely within the UK meant that only small sample sizes were available for individuals of non-European ancestries and that these individuals were identified using a genetics-based approach that relied on discrete biogeographical categories.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


