        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.</obo:IAO_0000115>
