        <obo:IAO_0000115>A biobank set up at Columbia University Irving Medical Center in New York City, United States, in response to the city&apos;s COVID-19 surge in March 2020, which kept residual blood and urine samples left over from clinical testing of consecutive patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19, of any age, sex or ancestry, treated at the medical center.</obo:IAO_0000115>
