    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001581"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90296493</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An NCI-supported consortium, begun in 2006, of case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia that combines data across its member studies, including in a genome-wide association study, to investigate the etiology of endometrial cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>E2C2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90296493</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A large-scale genome-wide cross-trait analysis for the effect of COVID-19 on female-specific cancers.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37636041</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10450412/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GWAS summary data of EC was obtained from a meta-analysis of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium (ECAC), the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium (E2C2), and the UK Biobank,49 involving 12,906 cases and 108,979 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An NCI-supported consortium, begun in 2006, of case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia that combines data across its member studies, including in a genome-wide association study, to investigate the etiology of endometrial cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24096698</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>E2C2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001581"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898362/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a GWAS within the E2C2 to identify genetic loci that predispose to EC. Details on the 15 participating studies are provided in Supplementary Table 1. The discovery phase of the GWAS (Stage 1) was conducted among women of European ancestry and was restricted to Type 1 EC, the most common subtype accounting for 80–90 % of all cases in women of European descent. Seven participating studies, including four cohort [California Teacher’s Study (CTS), Nurses’ Health Study (NHS), Multiethnic Cohort (MEC), Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO)] and three case–control studies [Connecticut Endometrial Cancer (CONN), Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center (FHCRC), Polish Endometrial Cancer Study (PECS)], were genotyped in Stage 1 (2,695 cases, 2,777 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Geography: 1 Asia, 25 North America, 10 Europe, 1 Australia</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085317/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 2695 cases and 2777 controls from the E2C2 consortium were genotyped using the Illumina Human OmniExpress array (2271 cases, 2219 controls from the United States) or the Illumina Human 660W array (424 cases, 558 controls from Poland)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078">
