        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10727334/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The authors thank the staff and participants of the ARIC, NOMAS, WHICAP, EDIS, MCS, and FHS studies for their important contributions.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study of the prevalence and risk factors of cognitive impairment and dementia in Chinese, Malay and Indian adults in Singapore, which drew participants aged 60 and over from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases study (the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, 2009–2011, the Singapore Malay Eye Study, 2010–2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study, 2013–2015). Participants were screened with the Abbreviated Mental Test and a history of progressive forgetfulness, and those who screened positive were invited for neuropsychological testing and brain MRI.</owl:annotatedTarget>
