        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley&apos;s villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
