        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based study at the Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States, that from 2003 enrolled adults with acute ischaemic stroke (consecutive patients admitted to its stroke unit through the emergency department, or seen in its neurology clinics or on other inpatient services), with stroke-free controls from the hospital&apos;s outpatient clinics matched on age, sex and ancestry, to study genetic influences on the risk and outcome of ischaemic stroke; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.</owl:annotatedTarget>
