    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13348699/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifically, these included the NJMU Global Screening Array project (10,248 cases and 9,298 controls), with participants recruited from five major cities in China (Nanjing, Shanghai, Beijing, Tianjin, and Guangzhou); the NJMU GWAS dataset (2,126 cases and 3,077 controls) [17]; and the NJMU OncoArray dataset (953 cases and 953 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90104085</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of academic Parkinson&apos;s disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson&apos;s Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson&apos;s disease enrolled in the centres&apos; studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson&apos;s disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PD Cognitive Genetics Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PDCGC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Parkinson&apos;s Disease Cognitive Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104085</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common X-Chromosome Variants Are Associated with Parkinson Disease Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33583074</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8601399/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the replication, we meta-analyzed 2 PD datasets (Table 2): the first composed of the Parkinson’s Disease Cognitive Genetics Consortium (PDCGC) and healthy individuals from the Adult Change in Thought (ACT) longitudinal cohort, referred to here as PDCGC &amp; ACT; and the second from McGill University (McGill), including samples from the Quebec Parkinson Network.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of academic Parkinson&apos;s disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson&apos;s Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson&apos;s disease enrolled in the centres&apos; studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26296077</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27571329</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38870440</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PDCGC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5056861/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed detailed longitudinal assessments of 740 patients with PD who were volunteer research participants enrolled at 7 sites for the PD Cognitive Genetics Consortium, including University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia; Feinstein Institute for Medical Research, Manhasset, New York; The Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, Maryland; Mayo Clinic, Jacksonville, Florida; Pacific Northwest Udall Center (PANUC), Portland, Oregon, and Seattle, Washington (all 6 are Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson’s Disease Research); and Rush University Medical Center, Chicago, Illinois.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21673961</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of ovarian cancer in Poland, with participants from Szczecin, Poznań, Opole and Rzeszów, that is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>POC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>POCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Polish Ovarian Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Poland Ovarian Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21673961</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Estrogen receptor beta rs1271572 polymorphism and invasive ovarian carcinoma risk: pooled analysis within the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21673961</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3108970/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This pooled analysis of nine population-based studies from Australia [the Australian Ovarian Cancer study and the Australian Cancer Study: Ovarian Cancer (AUS)], the United States [Genetic Epidemiology of Ovarian Cancer Study, Stanford University, California (STA); Hawaiian Ovarian Cancer Study, Honolulu, Hawaii (HAW); the North Carolina Ovarian Cancer Study, North Carolina (NCO); the University of Southern California Case-Control Studies of Ovarian Cancer, Los Angeles County, California (USC)], and Europe [MALOVA Ovarian Cancer Case-Control Study, Danish Cancer Society, Denmark (MAL); Studies of Epidemiology and Risk Factors in Cancer Heredity, United Kingdom (SEA); the United Kingdom Ovarian Cancer Population Study (UKO); the Polish Ovarian Cancer study, Poland (POC)] and one hospital-based study [Bavaria Case-Control Study (BAV)] included 4946 cases with primary histologically-confirmed invasive ovarian carcinoma and 6582 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of ovarian cancer in Poland, with participants from Szczecin, Poznań, Opole and Rzeszów, that is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21673961</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23513043</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>POC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
