    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90105058</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A study of the younger part of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study (SALT) cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry, twins born 1943–1958, who in 2008–2010 were sent an extensive self-report questionnaire, a request for saliva for DNA and an invitation to a web-based investigation, carried out by the registry with researchers in epidemiology, medicine, political science and economics.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SALT-Y</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SALTY</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study in Younger adults</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Screening Across the Lifespan Twin survey, Younger cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90105058</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis identifies 48 risk variants and highlights the role of the stria vascularis in hearing loss.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35580588</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9247887/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Danish Twin Registry (DTR; n = 1,314), the Estonian Genome Center at the University of Tartu (EGCUT; n = 55,523), FinnGen (n = 212,544), Framingham Heart Study (FHS; n = 2,536), Health Aging and Body Composition (HABC; n = 1,288), Italian Network of Genetic Isolates - Friuli Venezia Giulia (INGI-FVG; n = 339), the Rotterdam Study (RS, cohorts 1–3; n = 6,157), the Salus in Apulia study (SA; n = 1,780; formerly known as Great Age study), Screening Across the Lifespan Twin (SALT; n = 9,565, and SALTY - young; n = 5,133), Screening Twin Adults: Genes and Environment (STAGE; n = 8,345), TwinsUK (n = 5,125), UK Biobank (UKBB; n = 392,143), and the Women’s Genome Health Study (WGHS; n = 18,340).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of the younger part of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study (SALT) cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry, twins born 1943–1958, who in 2008–2010 were sent an extensive self-report questionnaire, a request for saliva for DNA and an invitation to a web-based investigation, carried out by the registry with researchers in epidemiology, medicine, political science and economics.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31747977</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38412344</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SALT-Y</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SALTY</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/twin-research-and-human-genetics/article/swedish-twin-registry-content-and-management-as-a-research-infrastructure/C22D50E7162D4A9F63706B2B4B84C75B</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The data collection began in the fall of 2008 by sending an extensive questionnaire to 24,914 Swedish twins, and it was completed in the summer of 2010.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369071/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>National health register information (until 2016) was linked to 5 subcohorts of child and adult twins (total twin pairs: n = 38 723) from the Swedish Twin Registry including: 17 593 pairs from the Child and Adolescent Twin Study of Sweden (CATSS), born 1992 to 2012; 2254 pairs from the Young Adult Twins in Sweden Study (YATSS), born 1985 to 1991; 9234 pairs from the Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment (STAGE), born 1958 to 1985; 3649 pairs from the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study in Younger adults (SALTY), born 1943 to 1958; and 5993 pairs from TwinGene, born 1911 to 1958 (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90243965</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI&apos;s Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI Severe Asthma Research Program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SARP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Severe Asthma Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Severe Asthma Research Program</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90243965</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic diversity fuels gene discovery for tobacco and alcohol use.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36477530</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9771818/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SARP (Severe Asthma Research Program) – The authors thank the SARP participants, investigators, clinical research staff and data coordinating center.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI&apos;s Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17208583</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28866107</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34536413</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SARP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5832534/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In November 2012 the NIH/NHLBI formed SARP III, a network of U.S. investigators and a data coordinating center (DCC) located at regional academic health centers involved in severe asthma research.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001117"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90984764</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children&apos;s Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SCCRIP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sickle Cell Clinical Research and Intervention Program</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90984764</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A polygenic score for acute vaso-occlusive pain in pediatric sickle cell disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34283174</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34283174+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To investigate this in sickle cell disease (SCD), we performed whole-genome sequencing (WGS) of 722 individuals with hemoglobin HbSS or HbSβ0-thalassemia from Baylor College of Medicine and from the St. Jude Children&apos;s Research Hospital Sickle Cell Clinical Research and Intervention Program (SCCRIP) longitudinal cohort study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children&apos;s Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29797644</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39373640</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41870384</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SCCRIP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11652775/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of 501 children aged at least 3 years old, who lived in Tennessee and enrolled in SCCRIP, 435 had sufficient environmental data to be mapped to a census tract (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116">
