        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genetic epidemiological study of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease in Punjabi-speaking Sikhs of North Indian origin, begun as a family-based study of Khatri Sikh families with at least two siblings affected by type 2 diabetes and extended as a case-control study, with participants recruited in northern India from 2003, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
