    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90044894</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years&apos; duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TODAY</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TODAY2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Treatment Options for type 2 Diabetes in Adolescents and Youth</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Treatment Options for Type 2 Diabetes in Adolescents and Youth</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90044894</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Association Study of Lipid Traits in Youth With Type 2 Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34568709</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34568709+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We genotyped 206 928 variants and imputed 17 642 824 variants in 1076 youth (mean age 15.0 ± 2.48 years) with T2D from the Treatment Options for Type 2 Diabetes in Adolescents and Youth (TODAY) and SEARCH for Diabetes in Youth (SEARCH) studies as part of the Progress in Diabetes Genetics in Youth (ProDiGY) consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years&apos; duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17448130</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22540912</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38815053</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TODAY</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TODAY2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11570374/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, 699 participants, 10 to 17 years old, diagnosed with type 2 diabetes by American Diabetes Association criteria, with duration 2 years or less, body mass index (BMI) ≥ 85th percentile for age and sex, were enrolled across 15 clinical centers in the United States</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90709786</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson&apos;s disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson&apos;s UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson&apos;s disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson&apos;s disease, including its relation to genetic variation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PRoBaND</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Parkinson&apos;s repository of biosamples and networked datasets</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TPD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tracking Parkinson&apos;s Disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tracking Parkinson&apos;s</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90709786</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide determinants of mortality and motor progression in Parkinson&apos;s disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38849413</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11161485/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Tracking Parkinson’s is a longitudinal, prospective, multi-centre observational study in the UK51.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson&apos;s disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson&apos;s UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson&apos;s disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson&apos;s disease, including its relation to genetic variation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26485428</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38849413</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
