    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90301397</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CLX</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COLONOMICS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Colonomics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90301397</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Germline genetic regulation of the colorectal tumor immune microenvironment.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38664626</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11046907/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three independent data sets were available for replication of our discovery phase findings: Colonomics (“CLX”, N = 99; clonality, abundance, TILs/hpf), the CRC Genetics Study (“CRCGEN”, N = 162; clonality, abundance), and the Nurses’ Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (N = 505; TILs).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36182938</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CLX</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Colon cancer patients were retrospectively selected during 2012 from those that had received radical surgery in the Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) between January 1996 and December 2000, and had fresh frozen tumor samples in the hospital biobank.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90026609</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, multicentre trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (now the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology), begun in the United States in 2008, of first-line endocrine therapy alone or with bevacizumab for women with hormone receptor-positive advanced-stage breast cancer who were postmenopausal or receiving ovarian suppression: a phase III comparison with letrozole, run in parallel with a phase II comparison with tamoxifen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CALGB 40503</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90026609</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Bevacizumab-induced hypertension and proteinuria: a genome-wide study of more than 1000 patients.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34616010</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8770703/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The genotyping and QC for CALGB 40503 has not been previously reported and it is described in the Supplementary File.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
