        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, multicentre trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (now the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology), begun in the United States in 2008, of first-line endocrine therapy alone or with bevacizumab for women with hormone receptor-positive advanced-stage breast cancer who were postmenopausal or receiving ovarian suppression: a phase III comparison with letrozole, run in parallel with a phase II comparison with tamoxifen.</owl:annotatedTarget>
