    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90255364</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-omics cohort of adult Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time. It combines whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>4D-SZ</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>4D-SZ study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">4D-SZ cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90255364</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Sex differences in the oral microbiome, host traits, and their causal relationships.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36660475</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9843272/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 4D-SZ cohort is a well-designed multi-omics cohort,15,16,17,18 with shotgun data for the metagenome across multiple body sites and the host genome, as well as metabolic traits, detailed questionnaires, and clinical information.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
