        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841377</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer&apos;s disease pathology.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BAC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BACS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Berkeley Aging Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Berkeley Aging Cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Berkeley aging cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Berkeley Aging Cohort Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841377</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large multi-ethnic genetic analyses of amyloid imaging identify new genes for Alzheimer disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37101235</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134547/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These cohorts included Memento [24], Mayo Clinic Study of Aging (MCSA) [25], Wisconsin Registry for Alzheimer&apos;s Prevention (WRAP) [26], Berkeley Aging Cohort study (BACS) [27], Korean study [28], and MISSION-AD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
