        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer&apos;s disease pathology.</owl:annotatedTarget>
