    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90662913</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CACTI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Coronary Artery Calcification in T1D</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90662913</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetics of C-Peptide and Age at Diagnosis in Type 1 Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39556808</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11755686/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a meta-GWAS of C-peptide that including four T1D studies: the Scottish Diabetes Research Network Type 1 Bioresource (SDRNT1BIO) (4,16), Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) (17,18), Coronary Artery Calcification in T1D (CACTI) (19,20), and Wisconsin Epidemiologic Study of Diabetic Retinopathy (WESDR) (21).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:14578303</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23340891</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24130360</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30943964</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CACTI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3687315/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study was performed at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes in Denver, Colorado, and at the Clinical Translational Research Center (CTRC) at the University of Colorado Hospital.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90472771</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CASP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Collaborative Association Study of psoriasis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Collaborative Association Study of Psoriasis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90472771</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>GWAS meta-analysis of psoriasis identifies new susceptibility alleles impacting disease mechanisms and therapeutic targets.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40021644</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11871359/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Individual level genotype data for the CASP GWAS, PsA GWAS, and Exomechip case-control studies are available on dbGaP (dbGaP: phs000019.v1.p1, phs000982.v1.p1, and phs001306.v1.p1, and WTCCC2 genotype data are archived at the European Genome-Phenome Archive (study ID EGAS00000000108).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19169254</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CASP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.311/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng311_MOESM30_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Additional selection criteria for Michigan cases included a requirement of at least two psoriatic plaques or a single plaque occupying &gt;1% of total body surface area outside scalp.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uganda"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90274713</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case–control study of prostate cancer in men of African ancestry, genotyped on the Illumina H3Africa array. It combines African American cases from Los Angeles, California, identified through the SEER cancer registry, and cancer-free controls from the African American Eye Disease Study in Inglewood, California, with incident cases and controls from other clinics at Mulago Hospital in Kampala, Uganda.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CA UG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CA UG Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CAUG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>California Uganda Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">California and Uganda Prostate Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90274713</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Characterizing prostate cancer risk through multi-ancestry genome-wide discovery of 187 novel risk variants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37945903</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10841479/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The present study included an additional 49,072 cases and 661,437 controls from the UK Biobank, the FinnGen study, the Electronic Medical Records and Genomics (eMERGE) Network, the BioVU Biobank, the BioMe Biobank, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO), the MD Anderson prostate cancer study (MD Anderson), the California and Uganda Prostate Cancer Study (CA UG), the VA Million Veteran Program (MVP), and the Maryland Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study (NCI-MD) (Supplementary Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control study of prostate cancer in men of African ancestry, genotyped on the Illumina H3Africa array. It combines African American cases from Los Angeles, California, identified through the SEER cancer registry, and cancer-free controls from the African American Eye Disease Study in Inglewood, California, with incident cases and controls from other clinics at Mulago Hospital in Kampala, Uganda.</owl:annotatedTarget>
