    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bangladesh"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90129578</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CBC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cryptosporidiosis Birth Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cryptosporidiosis and Enteropathogens in Bangladesh</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cryptosporidiosis and Enteropathogens in Bangladesh Birth Cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90129578</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Campylobacter-Positive Diarrhea Identifies Genes Involved in Toxin Processing and Inflammatory Response.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35420468</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9239263/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we aimed to identify genetic variants associated with host susceptibility to Campylobacter infection using two well-characterized birth cohorts: the Performance of Rotavirus and Oral Polio Vaccines in Developing Countries (PROVIDE) Study (19) and the Cryptosporidiosis Birth Cohort (CBC) (20).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29897482</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32019797</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40488529</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CBC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bangladesh"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10960603/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify host genetic risk factors associated with astrovirus disease susceptibility that may explain disease mechanism and vaccine targets, we performed genome-wide association studies in children enrolled in 2 birth cohorts, the Performance of Rotavirus and Oral Polio Vaccines in Developing Countries (PROVIDE) study and the Cryptosporidiosis and Enteropathogens in Bangladesh Birth Cohort (CBC) study in Dhaka, Bangladesh [15, 16].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90267154</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CCSS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Childhood Cancer Survivor Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267154</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study Identifies ROBO2 as a Novel Susceptibility Gene for Anthracycline-Related Cardiomyopathy in Childhood Cancer Survivors.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36508697</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36508697+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We addressed this gap using the Childhood Cancer Survivor Study (discovery) and the Children&apos;s Oncology Group (COG) study COG-ALTE03N1 (replication).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19364948</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31941657</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CCSS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7190022/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Childhood Cancer Survivor Study is a multi-institutional retrospective cohort study with longitudinal follow-up of five year survivors of the most common childhood cancers (leukemia, central nervous system tumors, Hodgkin lymphoma, non-Hodgkin lymphoma, renal tumors, neuroblastoma, soft tissue sarcomas, and bone sarcomas) diagnosed before age 21 years at one of 27 participating institutions in the United States and Canada.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156">
