        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Estonia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Iceland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Republic_of_Ireland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90244787</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ECRHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">European Community Respiratory Health Survey</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244787</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European and multi-ancestry genome-wide association meta-analysis of atopic dermatitis highlights importance of systemic immune regulation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37794016</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-023-41180-2/MediaObjects/41467_2023_41180_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants within the ECRHS were eligible for inclusion in this analysis if they were identified by random sampling of those who fulfilled the following criteria: 1) lived in centers that took part in genome-wide genotyping initiative under the auspices of GABRIEL7 AND 2) were initially selected to take part in the ECRHS clinical measurements as part of the random sample (i.e. not specifically selected for inclusion because of any pre-existing disease).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28974648</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30723731</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30764884</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ECRHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6355980/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This investigation included 24 centres from 11 countries: Iceland (Reykjavik), Norway (Bergen), Sweden (Gothenburg, Umeå and Uppsala), Estonia (Tartu), Germany (Erfurt and Hamburg), UK (Ipswich and Norwich), Belgium (Antwerp), France (Bordeaux, Grenoble, Montpellier and Paris), Spain (Albacete, Barcelona, Galdakao, Huelva and Oviedo), Italy (Pavia, Torino and Verona) and Australia (Melbourne).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Until now (December 2025) data for ECRHS IV has been collected in 7 countries with clinical investigations (Denmark, Norway, Estonia, Sweden, Iceland, Spain, Australia) and one country with questionnaire data only (United kingdom).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5738606/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>No estimate for Melbourne, Australia or Basel, Switzerland, as information on asthma medication use was not recorded during postal survey.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC119432</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We gathered data from the 30 centres within regions: United Kingdom and Republic of Ireland), northern Europe (Iceland, Norway, Sweden), central Europe (Belgium, France, the Netherlands), southern Europe (Italy and Spain), Australia and New Zealand, and United States (Portland was the only area in the United States).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90267392</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Colorectal and Pancreatic Neoplasm Virtual Biorepository</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EDRN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Early Detection Research Network Colorectal and Pancreatic Neoplasm Virtual Biorepository</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EDRN Colorectal and Pancreatic Neoplasm Virtual Biorepository</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267392</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Interaction Study with Smoking for Colorectal Cancer Risk Identifies Novel Genetic Loci Related to Tumor Suppression, Inflammation, and Immune Response.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36576985</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9992283/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>EDRN: This work and all authors were funded and supported by the NCI, EDRN Grant (U01 CA 84968-06). We acknowledge all contributors to the development of the resource at University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine, Department of Gastroenterology, Department of Pathology, Hepatology and Nutrition and Biomedical Informatics.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21031013</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
