        <rdfs:comment>To identify novel risk factors and corroborate previously identified risk factors for mean annual decline in FEV1% predicted in a large, contemporary, United States cohort of young cystic fibrosis (CF) patients.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90568440</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King&apos;s College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>E-Risk</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>E-Risk Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Environmental Risk (E-Risk) Longitudinal Twin Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Environmental Risk Longitudinal Twin Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90568440</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis of childhood ADHD symptoms and diagnosis identifies new loci and potential effector genes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40962958</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02295-y/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2295_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were members of E-Risk, which tracks the development of a 1994-95 birth cohort of</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King&apos;s College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40350583</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>E-Risk</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15113820+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Environmental Risk Longitudinal Twin Study (E-Risk) comprised 2163 twin children from England and Wales (49.1% male) identified at birth in 1994 and 1995 and included administration of the Test of Word Reading Efficiency at age 7 years and the Wechsler Preschool and Primary Scale of Intelligence-Revised as a test of IQ at age 5 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90428068</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GaPP2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GaPP2 trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Gabapentin for chronic pelvic pain in women</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90428068</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association reveals a locus in neuregulin 3 associated with gabapentin efficacy in women with chronic pelvic pain.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39258169</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11384074/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted an exploratory genome-wide association study using eligible GaPP2 participants aiming to identify genetic variants associated with gabapentin response.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32979978</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39258169</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GaPP2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11384074/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The trial, Gabapentin for chronic pelvic pain in women (GaPP2), was a UK-wide, multicenter, randomized, controlled trial of gabapentin versus placebo for the treatment of CPP.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/India"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90179179</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks&apos; gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India&apos;s Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GARBH-Ini</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GARBH-Ini cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GARBH-Ini pregnancy cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Interdisciplinary Group for Advanced Research on Birth Outcomes - DBT India Initiative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>interdisciplinary Group for Advanced Research on BirtH outcomes - DBT India Initiative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Interdisciplinary Group for Advanced Research on BirtH outcomes - DBT India Initiative</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90179179</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic variants associated with spontaneous preterm birth in women from India: a prospective cohort study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37492417</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363490/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Pregnant women enrolled between May 2015 to April 2021 in a large single-centre prospective cohort14 (GARBH-Ini: interdisciplinary Group for Advanced Research on BirtH outcomes - DBT India Initiative) in Haryana, India, were followed up with written informed consent till six months after delivery (cohort description provided in Appendix).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks&apos; gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India&apos;s Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30770926</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37492417</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39030058</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GARBH-Ini</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/India"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363490/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Pregnant women enrolled between May 2015 to April 2021 in a large single-centre prospective cohort14 (GARBH-Ini: interdisciplinary Group for Advanced Research on BirtH outcomes - DBT India Initiative) in Haryana, India, were followed up with written informed consent till six months after delivery (cohort description provided in Appendix).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90308666</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GBMI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Global Biobank Meta-analysis Initiative</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90308666</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry meta-analysis identifies 5 novel loci for ischemic stroke and reveals heterogeneity of effects between sexes and ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37601974</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37601974+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide meta-analysis of 16 biobanks across multiple ancestries to study the genetics of ischemic stroke (60,176 cases, 1,310,725 controls) as part of the Global Biobank Meta-analysis Initiative (GBMI) and further combined the results with previously published MegaStroke.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36777996</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/parcipating-biobanks</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GBMI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90267402</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) enrolled in the LNH03 (LNH 2003) programme of treatment trials of the Groupe d&apos;Etude des Lymphomes de l&apos;Adulte (GELA, later the Lymphoma Study Association, LYSA), who consented to DNA analysis. The programme&apos;s trials, opened from December 2003 at centres mainly in France and Belgium for patients of different ages and prognostic risk, were the randomised trials LNH03-1B, LNH03-2B and LNH03-6B, the phase 2 trial LNH03-3B, LNH03-39B and a phase 2 trial of R-miniCHOP in patients over 80. The patients&apos; germline DNA was genotyped as the case series of GELA&apos;s genome-wide association study of DLBCL, with controls drawn from the French component of EPIC.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GELA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Treatment program of DLBCL patients from the Groupe dEtude des Lymphomes de lAdulte</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Treatment program of DLBCL patients from the Groupe d&apos;Etude des Lymphomes de l&apos;Adulte</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
