    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90565134</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genizon</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genizon BioSciences</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genizon GWAS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90565134</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry genome-wide meta-analysis with 472,819 individuals identifies 32 novel risk loci for psoriasis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39885523</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11783861/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Currently published GWASs include eight Europe-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohorts, including CASP [7], Kiel [8], Genizon [8], PsA GWAS [9], WTCCC2 [10], Exomechip [11], PAGE [12], and GAPC [12], two South Asia-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohort including three batches [13], and one East Asia-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohort [14].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.</owl:annotatedTarget>
