        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90558259</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GMS CFLD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GMS of Severe CF Liver Disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GMS_CFLD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Modifier Study of Severe Cystic Fibrosis Liver Disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Modifier Study of Severe Liver Disease in Cystic Fibrosis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Modifier Study of Severe CF Liver Disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90558259</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic modifiers of body mass index in individuals with cystic fibrosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39260370</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11480786/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Cystic Fibrosis Genome Project (CFGP) is comprised of individuals with CF recruited by the CF Twin and Sibling Study (TSS)15 and Cystic Fibrosis-Related Diabetes (CFRD) Study16 (Johns Hopkins University), Genetic Modifier Study (GMS)17,18,19 and GMS of Severe CF Liver Disease (GMS CFLD)20,21 (University of North Carolina), and Early Pseudomonas Infection Control Observational (EPIC Obs) Study22 (University of Washington and Seattle Children’s Hospital).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19738092</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27062904</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30307979</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GMS CFLD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GMS_CFLD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6181334/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Severe CFLD subjects described in this analysis were enrolled in the Genetic Modifier Study of Severe CF Liver Disease from 34 North American CF Centers from the United States (n = 145 CFLD patients) and Canada (n = 34 CFLD patients), with a coordinating center at The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill as previously described [7].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Turkey"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3711243/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 158 CF patients evaluated for severe liver disease (CFLD; portal hypertension; enrolled 1/1999–12/2004), there were 128 patients who fulfilled criteria from 22 CF Centers in 10 countries (Australia, 8; Canada, 17; Czech Republic, 17; Germany, 3; Italy, 28; Netherlands, 1; Scotland, 2; Slovakia, 4; Turkey, 4; and U.S., 44).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3711243/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 191 CF patients evaluated for CFLD (portal hypertension; enrolled 1/2005–2/2007), there were 139 CF patients who fulfilled criteria from 35 CF Centers in 10 countries (Argentina, 5; Australia, 5; Canada, 24; Chile, 1; France, 9; Ireland, 8; Israel, 7; Italy, 14; United Kingdom, 4; and U.S., 62).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90244577</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pharmacogenetic sample of adult outpatients of white European ancestry with moderate to severe major depressive disorder who completed escitalopram treatment in two identically designed randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled GlaxoSmithKline trials run in the United States in 2003–2004 to compare bupropion XL with escitalopram for antidepressant efficacy and effects on sexual functioning; GlaxoSmithKline contributed their DNA to the NEWMEDS consortium for genetic studies of antidepressant response.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Glaxo Smith Kline</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Glaxo-Smith Kline</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">GSK</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244577</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identifying the Common Genetic Basis of Antidepressant Response.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35712048</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9117153/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The samples from GSK derived from two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled comparisons of the antidepressant efficacy and the effects on sexual functioning of Bupropion XL and escitalopram in outpatients with moderate to severe depression (22).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pharmacogenetic sample of adult outpatients of white European ancestry with moderate to severe major depressive disorder who completed escitalopram treatment in two identically designed randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled GlaxoSmithKline trials run in the United States in 2003–2004 to compare bupropion XL with escitalopram for antidepressant efficacy and effects on sexual functioning; GlaxoSmithKline contributed their DNA to the NEWMEDS consortium for genetic studies of antidepressant response.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16841623</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23091423</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35712048</obo:IAO_0000119>
