        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of patients aged 5 to 85 who presented with acute appendicitis at the emergency department of Jessa Hospital in Hasselt, Belgium, and had an appendectomy, recruited from June 2012 to October 2016 in a study led by Hasselt University with Jessa Hospital and Radboud University Medical Center. Questionnaires on diet, lifestyle and environment were collected together with blood, appendix tissue and stool samples, to study how environmental factors, the innate immune system and its genetic make-up, and the gut microbiota influence the development and severity of acute appendicitis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
