    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001188 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001188">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hong_Kong"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90281031</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective register of patients with diabetes, with a biobank, established in 1995 by the Chinese University of Hong Kong at its teaching hospital, the Prince of Wales Hospital, as a research-driven quality-improvement programme. Patients referred by hospital specialty clinics, community clinics and general practitioners to the hospital&apos;s Diabetes Mellitus and Endocrine Centre were enrolled consecutively for a structured assessment of complications and metabolic control and then followed until death, to study the risk factors, complications and outcomes of diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HKDR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Hong Kong Diabetes Registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hong Kong Diabetes Register</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001188"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90281031</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of a Common Variant for Coronary Heart Disease at PDE1A Contributes to Individualized Treatment Goals and Risk Stratification of Cardiovascular Complications in Chinese Patients With Type 2 Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37125963</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10234754/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the stage of genome-wide scan, we performed a meta-analysis in two independent case-control cohorts of Chinese patients with T2D: 1) 4,886 patients (1,358 case and 3,528 control subjects) from the Hong Kong Diabetes Register (HKDR) (recruitment period 1995–2014) and 2) 4,055 patients (1,159 case and 2,896 control subjects) recruited in 2013–2019 from the Hong Kong Diabetes Biobank (HKDB) phase 1 study (16).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001188"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective register of patients with diabetes, with a biobank, established in 1995 by the Chinese University of Hong Kong at its teaching hospital, the Prince of Wales Hospital, as a research-driven quality-improvement programme. Patients referred by hospital specialty clinics, community clinics and general practitioners to the hospital&apos;s Diabetes Mellitus and Endocrine Centre were enrolled consecutively for a structured assessment of complications and metabolic control and then followed until death, to study the risk factors, complications and outcomes of diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32722720</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40171472</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001188"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HKDR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001188"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hong_Kong"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10234754/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All patients in the above three cohorts were southern Han Chinese residing in Hong Kong.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001189 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001189">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90664511</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pan-Canadian databank set up in 2020 by CGEn, Canada&apos;s national platform for genome sequencing and analysis, within Genome Canada&apos;s Canadian COVID-19 Genomics Network, that brings together independent clinical and epidemiological studies enrolling people of any age infected with SARS-CoV-2 across Canada. Each partner study contributes blood (rarely saliva) samples for whole-genome sequencing at the CGEn centres and clinical information on a standard case report form, creating a resource for research on host genetic factors in SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGEn HostSeq Initiative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HostSeq</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HostSeq Databank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HostSeq project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">HostSeq initiative</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001189"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90664511</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Canadian COVID-19 host genetics cohort replicates known severity associations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38517939</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38517939+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HostSeq initiative recruited 10,059 Canadians infected with SARS-CoV-2 between March 2020 and March 2023, obtained clinical information on their disease experience and whole genome sequenced (WGS) their DNA.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001189"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pan-Canadian databank set up in 2020 by CGEn, Canada&apos;s national platform for genome sequencing and analysis, within Genome Canada&apos;s Canadian COVID-19 Genomics Network, that brings together independent clinical and epidemiological studies enrolling people of any age infected with SARS-CoV-2 across Canada. Each partner study contributes blood (rarely saliva) samples for whole-genome sequencing at the CGEn centres and clinical information on a standard case report form, creating a resource for research on host genetic factors in SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37131148</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38517939</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001189"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HostSeq</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001189"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38517939+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HostSeq initiative recruited 10,059 Canadians infected with SARS-CoV-2 between March 2020 and March 2023, obtained clinical information on their disease experience and whole genome sequenced (WGS) their DNA.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90013445</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multinational longitudinal cohort of children and adolescents under 16 with newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes, recruited from August 1999 to December 2000 at 18 paediatric departments in 15 countries of Europe and Japan by the Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes, an international group of paediatric diabetes centres, and followed through the first 12 months after diagnosis with meal-stimulated C-peptide tests, HbA1c, insulin doses, islet autoantibodies and HLA typing, to study residual beta-cell function and the partial remission period.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HSG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HSG remission phase cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes remission phase cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hvidoere Remission Phase Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90013445</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fine-mapping, trans-ancestral and genomic analyses identify causal variants, cells, genes and drug targets for type 1 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34127860</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8273124/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These studies include the Type 1 Diabetes Genetics Consortium (T1DGC), British 1958 Birth Cohort, Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID), Consortium for the Longitudinal Evaluation of African-Americans with Early Rheumatoid Arthritis (CLEAR), Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications (EDIC), Genetics of Kidneys and Diabetes Study (GoKinD), New York Cancer Project (NYCP), SEARCH for Diabetes in Youth study (SEARCH), Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet study (TrialNet), Tyypin 1 Diabetekseen Sairastuneita Perheenjäsenineen (IDDMGEN), Tyypin 1 Diabeteksen Genetiikka (T1DGEN), Northern Ireland GRID Collection, Northern Ireland Young Hearts Project, Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes (HSG), and International HapMap Project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multinational longitudinal cohort of children and adolescents under 16 with newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes, recruited from August 1999 to December 2000 at 18 paediatric departments in 15 countries of Europe and Japan by the Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes, an international group of paediatric diabetes centres, and followed through the first 12 months after diagnosis with meal-stimulated C-peptide tests, HbA1c, insulin doses, islet autoantibodies and HLA typing, to study residual beta-cell function and the partial remission period.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19435955</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19708904</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21429197</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33203694</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HSG</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
