    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001193 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001193">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90624430</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A French prospective multicentre cohort, sponsored by Assistance Publique – Hôpitaux de Paris, of women of European ancestry aged over 18 who gave birth in eight maternity departments of the Paris metropolitan area and were included two to five days after delivery between November 2011 and June 2016. The women gave a blood sample for DNA and were assessed for depression by trained clinicians with DSM-5 criteria at inclusion, at 8 weeks and at 1 year postpartum, to study how genetic factors and maternal stressors interact in the risk of postpartum depression.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IGEDEPP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Interaction Between Genetic Factors and Maternal Stressors During Pregnancy in the Risk of Postpartum Depression</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Interaction of Gene and Environment of Depression in PostPartum</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>interaction of gene and environment of depression during postpartum</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Interaction of Gene and Environment of Depression during PostPartum</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001193"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624430</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of early-onset and late-onset postpartum depression: the IGEDEPP prospective study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38555957</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11059250/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With the French multicenter interaction of gene and environment of depression during postpartum (IGEDEPP) cohort, we conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) on 234 women with early-onset PPD and 223 women with late-onset PPD, as well as 1,204 controls with no history of lifetime depression.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001193"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A French prospective multicentre cohort, sponsored by Assistance Publique – Hôpitaux de Paris, of women of European ancestry aged over 18 who gave birth in eight maternity departments of the Paris metropolitan area and were included two to five days after delivery between November 2011 and June 2016. The women gave a blood sample for DNA and were assessed for depression by trained clinicians with DSM-5 criteria at inclusion, at 8 weeks and at 1 year postpartum, to study how genetic factors and maternal stressors interact in the risk of postpartum depression.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33932643</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38555957</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01648816</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001193"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>IGEDEPP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001193"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11059250/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our study among the interaction of gene and environment of depression during postpartum (IGEDEPP) women, in the Paris areas (France), showed 1-year cumulative incidence of PPD of 18.1%, a prevalence of early-onset PPD of 8.3%, and a prevalence of late-onset PPD of 12.9% [6], in line with previous works [7].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001194 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001194">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90568440</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A school-based cohort of children and adolescents aged 5–17 from primary and secondary general-education schools across Catalonia, Spain, set up to study neurodevelopmental disorders, school performance and their genetic and environmental factors. Since the 2011–2012 school year, parents and teachers complete screening questionnaires for mental health problems and learning difficulties, children who screen positive are assessed by psychiatrists and neuropsychologists for DSM diagnoses, academic marks are taken from school records, and DNA is collected from saliva or buccal swabs.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INSchool</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INSchool cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Impact of Neurodevelopmental disorders and School performance: genes and environment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001194"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90568440</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis of childhood ADHD symptoms and diagnosis identifies new loci and potential effector genes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40962958</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02295-y/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2295_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The INSchool cohort consist of 3, 557 children from 23 schools in Catalonia (age range: 5-17 years; 234 mean age: 9.8 years, s.d.=2.9).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001194"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A school-based cohort of children and adolescents aged 5–17 from primary and secondary general-education schools across Catalonia, Spain, set up to study neurodevelopmental disorders, school performance and their genetic and environmental factors. Since the 2011–2012 school year, parents and teachers complete screening questionnaires for mental health problems and learning difficulties, children who screen positive are assessed by psychiatrists and neuropsychologists for DSM diagnoses, academic marks are taken from school records, and DNA is collected from saliva or buccal swabs.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38783053</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40962958</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41554769</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
