    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001197 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001197">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90809879</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multisite, population-based prospective cohort study of dementia, coordinated from Kyushu University. Community-dwelling residents aged 65 years or older at eight research sites across Japan (Hirosaki, Yahaba, Nakajima, Arakawa, Ama, Nakayama, Hisayama and Arao) were examined in 2016–2018 under a common standardized protocol, including questionnaires, cognitive assessment, blood tests, brain MRI and DNA samples, and are followed up for incident dementia, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for dementia and their interaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>JPSC-AD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Japan Prospective Studies Collaboration for Aging and Dementia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001197"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90809879</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Meta-analyses of genome-wide association studies identify novel loci influencing Japanese white matter hyperintensities.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41554961</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41554961+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we conducted a GWAS comprising 1001 Japanese individuals from the National Center for Geriatrics and Gerontology (NCGG) Biobank, followed by a meta-analysis with GWAS data from 9479 individuals in the Japan Prospective Studies Collaboration for Aging and Dementia (JPSC-AD), identifying three novel loci significantly associated with WMH volume (P -8).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001197"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multisite, population-based prospective cohort study of dementia, coordinated from Kyushu University. Community-dwelling residents aged 65 years or older at eight research sites across Japan (Hirosaki, Yahaba, Nakajima, Arakawa, Ama, Nakayama, Hisayama and Arao) were examined in 2016–2018 under a common standardized protocol, including questionnaires, cognitive assessment, blood tests, brain MRI and DNA samples, and are followed up for incident dementia, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for dementia and their interaction.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33129280</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001197"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>JPSC-AD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001197"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33129280+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japan Prospective Studies Collaboration for Aging and Dementia (JPSC-AD) is a multisite, population-based prospective cohort study of dementia, which was designed to enroll approximately 10,000 community-dwelling residents aged 65 years or older from 8 sites in Japan and to follow them up prospectively for at least 5 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001198 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001198">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90448927</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide Korean survey population of all ages, set up in 2010 by the National Institute of Food and Drug Safety Evaluation as the first integrated assessment of dietary exposure to hazardous substances from food, herbal medicine and functional food. Adults were drawn by region-, sex- and age-stratified probability sampling from 102 town and township clusters in 15 metropolitan areas and provinces, and children, adolescents and mothers were recruited through schools, kindergartens, health centres and hospitals. All were surveyed in 2010–2011 with food frequency and 24-hour recall questionnaires, blood and urine biomonitoring, and health examinations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KRIEFS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Korean research project on the integrated exposure assessment of hazardous substances for food safety</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Korean Research Project on the Integrated Exposure Assessment of Hazardous Substances for Food Safety</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90448927</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association between urinary arsenic concentration and genetic polymorphisms in Korean adults.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38223675</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10786758/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study’s participants were based on a population of 2144 individuals selected during 2010–2011 by the Korean Research Project on the Integrated Exposure Assessment of Hazardous Substances for Food Safety (KRIEFS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide Korean survey population of all ages, set up in 2010 by the National Institute of Food and Drug Safety Evaluation as the first integrated assessment of dietary exposure to hazardous substances from food, herbal medicine and functional food. Adults were drawn by region-, sex- and age-stratified probability sampling from 102 town and township clusters in 15 metropolitan areas and provinces, and children, adolescents and mothers were recruited through schools, kindergartens, health centres and hospitals. All were surveyed in 2010–2011 with food frequency and 24-hour recall questionnaires, blood and urine biomonitoring, and health examinations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26184046</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
