    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001202 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001202">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90502911</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A biobank cohort set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI) in 2004 that, from 2005 to 2019, enrolled adults undergoing clinically indicated thoracic surgery (resection of lung nodules or masses, diagnostic biopsy for interstitial lung disease, lung volume reduction surgery or lung transplantation) at Mayo Clinic, Temple University and the Universities of Colorado, Michigan and Pittsburgh, and banked their excess lung tissue and blood together with questionnaire, lung function and chest CT data. Participants with and without lung disease were included, to support research on the pathobiology of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, interstitial lung diseases such as idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, and related lung diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LTRC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lung Tissue Research Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001202"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90502911</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Whole genome sequencing analysis of body mass index identifies novel African ancestry-specific risk allele.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40216759</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11992084/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>NHLBI TOPMed: Lung Tissue Research Consortium (LTRC)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001202"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A biobank cohort set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI) in 2004 that, from 2005 to 2019, enrolled adults undergoing clinically indicated thoracic surgery (resection of lung nodules or masses, diagnostic biopsy for interstitial lung disease, lung volume reduction surgery or lung transplantation) at Mayo Clinic, Temple University and the Universities of Colorado, Michigan and Pittsburgh, and banked their excess lung tissue and blood together with questionnaire, lung function and chest CT data. Participants with and without lung disease were included, to support research on the pathobiology of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, interstitial lung diseases such as idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, and related lung diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/ltrc/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001662.v4.p2</obo:IAO_0000119>
