    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001203"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23423446+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In stage I, we performed a case-only GWAS in 731 invasive breast cancer cases from the German case-control study Mammary Carcinoma Risk Factor Investigation (MARIE).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001204 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001204">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841377</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective population-based cohort of residents of Olmsted County, Minnesota, United States, randomly sampled with age and sex stratification from the population enumerated by the Rochester Epidemiology Project medical records-linkage system: people aged 70–89 from 2004, extended in 2012 to ages 50–69 and later to younger adults. Participants have in-person clinical, neurological and neuropsychological evaluations with a consensus diagnosis of normal cognition, mild cognitive impairment or dementia, repeated about every 15 months together with neuroimaging and biomarkers, to study the prevalence, incidence, risk factors and biomarkers of mild cognitive impairment and dementia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MCSA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mayo Clinic Study of Aging</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001204"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841377</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large multi-ethnic genetic analyses of amyloid imaging identify new genes for Alzheimer disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37101235</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134547/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These cohorts included Memento [24], Mayo Clinic Study of Aging (MCSA) [25], Wisconsin Registry for Alzheimer&apos;s Prevention (WRAP) [26], Berkeley Aging Cohort study (BACS) [27], Korean study [28], and MISSION-AD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001204"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective population-based cohort of residents of Olmsted County, Minnesota, United States, randomly sampled with age and sex stratification from the population enumerated by the Rochester Epidemiology Project medical records-linkage system: people aged 70–89 from 2004, extended in 2012 to ages 50–69 and later to younger adults. Participants have in-person clinical, neurological and neuropsychological evaluations with a consensus diagnosis of normal cognition, mild cognitive impairment or dementia, repeated about every 15 months together with neuroimaging and biomarkers, to study the prevalence, incidence, risk factors and biomarkers of mild cognitive impairment and dementia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18259084</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40830522</obo:IAO_0000119>
