        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A birth cohort of women recruited at their first antenatal clinic visit at the Mater Hospital in Brisbane, Australia, in 1981–1983, and of their live singleton children, followed up after the birth, at 6 months and at 5, 14 and 21 years, and in adulthood (mothers at 27 years, children at 30 years) with later record linkage. Begun as a study of pregnancy and its outcomes, it has become a longitudinal study of growth, development and ageing that emphasises the transmission across generations of factors affecting adult health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
