    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841197</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomized, double-blind primary prevention trial of the Cancer Institute of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences and the US National Cancer Institute in Linxian, Henan province, China, a rural county with some of the world&apos;s highest rates of oesophageal and gastric cardia cancer, which in 1985 enrolled healthy adults aged 40–69 from four communes in northern Linxian and gave them daily combinations of vitamins and minerals or placebo in a fractional factorial design from March 1986 to May 1991. Its participants have since been followed as a prospective cohort for cancer incidence and cause-specific mortality.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Linxian Nutrition Intervention Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Linxian General Population Nutrition Intervention Trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841197</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome wide association analysis and association of genetic risk and lifestyle with upper gastrointestinal cancer among an endoscopy-screened cohort in China.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41963194</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S2095927326003270-mmc1.docx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, participants were drawn from multiple established studies, including the Shanxi Upper Gastrointestinal Cancer Genetics Project and the Linxian Nutrition Intervention Trial, as well as additional prospective cohort studies incorporating in the validation phase.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomized, double-blind primary prevention trial of the Cancer Institute of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences and the US National Cancer Institute in Linxian, Henan province, China, a rural county with some of the world&apos;s highest rates of oesophageal and gastric cardia cancer, which in 1985 enrolled healthy adults aged 40–69 from four communes in northern Linxian and gave them daily combinations of vitamins and minerals or placebo in a fractional factorial design from March 1986 to May 1991. Its participants have since been followed as a prospective cohort for cancer incidence and cause-specific mortality.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34022824</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35224031</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38282387</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:7960367</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
