    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90100588</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium formed in 2006 within the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Cohort Consortium by investigators of 12 prospective cohort studies to run PanScan, a multi-stage genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer funded by the NCI. PanScan I genotyped cases and controls from the cohorts and one case-control study, PanScan II (from 2007) those of eight case-control studies, and PanScan III new incident cases from 14 cohorts and from case series and case-control studies, mostly people of European ancestry from the United States and Europe.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PANSCAN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PanScan</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90100588</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of Recessively Inherited Genetic Variants Potentially Linked to Pancreatic Cancer Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34926279</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8678088/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To discover recessively inherited pancreatic cancer risk loci, we performed a re-analysis of the largest pancreatic cancer GWAS, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium (PanScan) and the Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4), including 8,769 cases and 7,055 controls of European ancestry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium formed in 2006 within the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Cohort Consortium by investigators of 12 prospective cohort studies to run PanScan, a multi-stage genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer funded by the NCI. PanScan I genotyped cases and controls from the cohorts and one case-control study, PanScan II (from 2007) those of eight case-control studies, and PanScan III new incident cases from 14 cohorts and from case series and case-control studies, mostly people of European ancestry from the United States and Europe.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25086665</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/cancer-types/pancreas/panscan</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PANSCAN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PanScan</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4191666/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Geographic region was defined as REGION_US (United States): AgHealth, CPS-II, DFCI, HPFS, MEC, NHS, NYU-WHS, PHS, PLCO, SELECT, VITAL, WHI; REGION_CNE (Central and Northern Europe): ATBC, EPIC, PANDoRA-Heidelberg, MCCS (Melbourne); and REGION_SE (Southern Europe): SBCS (Spain controls), PANKRAS-II (cases).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Also included are 61 pancreatic cancer cases and 67 control subjects from PanScan I as well as 173 pancreatic cancer cases from PanScan III of Asian ancestry from the Shanghai Men&apos;s and Women&apos;s Health Study (Supplemental Table 10, Wolpin et al. (Nat Genet, 2014)).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition to the cases from cohorts, we also included cases from the Gastrointestinal Cancer Clinic of Dana-Farber Cancer Institute Study (DFCI-GCC); from the University Hospital in Heidelberg, Germany, which is part of a larger European clinical case-control study (PANDoRA); and from clinic-based cases from eastern Spain (PANKRAS-II).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000485"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90274713</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCI Prostate Cancer Genome-Wide Association Study of Uncommon Susceptibility Loci Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PEGASUS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PEGASUS_PCa</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PEGASUS_Pca</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ProstatE cancer Genetic Association Study of Uncommon Susceptibility loci</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prostate cancer Genome-wide Association Study to Uncover Susceptibility loci</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prostate Cancer Genome-wide Association Study of Uncommon Susceptibility Loci</rdfs:label>
