        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267402</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Distinct germline genetic susceptibility profiles identified for common non-Hodgkin lymphoma subtypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36273105</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41375-022-01711-0/MediaObjects/41375_2022_1711_MOESM1_ESM.docx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology GWAS SCALE FL-376 791 Population-based case-control study, Scandinavia Patients with incident primary NHL diagnosed through rapid case-ascertainment network in Sweden and Denmark Frequency matched (age in 10-year intervals, sex and country) population controls prospectively identified every 6 months in nationwide population registers (incidence density sampling).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15687363</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21037568</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25294155</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SCALE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4411784/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, SCALE is a population-based case–control study of the etiology of malignant lymphomas conducted in Sweden and Denmark 1999 to 2002.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Colombia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ecuador"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mexico"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454506</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of COVID-19 patients with detailed clinical information, recruited from hospitals across Spain from March to December 2020 and in Latin America from March 2020 to July 2021 by a Spanish research consortium launched in May 2020 to study host genetic factors in COVID-19 and find biomarkers of its course and prognosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SCOURGE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Spanish Coalition to Unlock Research of Host Genetics on COVID-19</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Spanish Coalition to Unlock Research on Host Genetics on COVID-19</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454506</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Novel risk loci for COVID-19 hospitalization among admixed American populations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39361370</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39361370+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this second study nested in the SCOURGE consortium, we conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) for COVID-19 hospitalization in admixed Americans, comprising a total of 4702 hospitalized cases recruited by SCOURGE and seven other participating studies in the COVID-19 Host Genetic Initiative.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of COVID-19 patients with detailed clinical information, recruited from hospitals across Spain from March to December 2020 and in Latin America from March 2020 to July 2021 by a Spanish research consortium launched in May 2020 to study host genetic factors in COVID-19 and find biomarkers of its course and prognosis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35708486</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39361370</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SCOURGE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mexico"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11449485/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To account for potential heterogeneity in the recruitment and hospitalization criteria across the participating countries, we adjusted the models by groups of the recruitment areas classified into six categories: Brazil, Colombia, Ecuador, Mexico, Paraguay, and Spain.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11449485/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Spanish Coalition to Unlock Research on Host Genetics on COVID-19 (SCOURGE) recruited COVID-19 patients between March and December 2020 from hospitals across Spain and from March 2020 to July 2021 in Latin America (https://www.scourge-covid.org).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


