        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6133086/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Six large population-based cohorts (NTR and GenR from the Netherlands, TEDS from the UK, CATSS and TCHAD from Sweden and FinnTwin12 from Finland) analysed the co-occurrence of aggression measures with other psychopathologies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5581816/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A population-based prospective cohort study including all twins from the Swedish Twin Registry who were born in Sweden 1985–1986 (N = 2960) [19] was conducted. These twins were invited to participate in a longitudinal Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development (TCHAD), see [20].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90104613</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TRACK-TBI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Transforming Research and Clinical Knowledge in TBI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Transforming Research and Clinical Knowledge in Traumatic Brain Injury</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104613</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study of outcome from traumatic brain injury.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35301180</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8927841/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The majority of patients in the US cohort were recruited between 2014 and 2018 to TRACK-TBI, a NIH-NINDS funded prospective multicenter study aimed at improving the characterization of TBI through the collection of clinical and genetic data, plasma biomarkers, as well as neuroimaging and other multidimensional outcomes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35301180</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36939699</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TRACK-TBI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8927841/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Individuals included were recruited between 2000 and 2018 at 78 centres in Europe (CENTER-TBI, Cambridge, and Turku) and the US (TRACK-TBI and MGB) (Supplementary Methods).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


