        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2858234/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Payroll files of Wisconsin state employees served as the sampling frame.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90502757</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ZOE 2.0 cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ZOE2.0</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ZOE 2.0</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90502757</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Trans-ancestry genome-wide association study of childhood body mass index identifies novel loci and age-specific effects.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39885687</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39885687+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify genetic loci associated with early-childhood body mass index (BMI), we performed GWAS of BMI Z scores in eight ancestrally diverse cohorts: ZOE 2.0 cohort, the Santiago Longitudinal Study (SLS), the Vanderbilt University BioVU biobank, the Geisinger MyCode Health Initiative biobank, Study of Latino (SOL) Youth, Pelotas (Brazil) Birth Cohort, Cameron County Hispanic Cohort (CCHC), and Viva La Familia cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33139633</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ZOE2.0</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7663650/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifically, the ZOE 2.0 study population was children attending public preschools (Head Start) in North Carolina, United States, between August 2016 and February 2019.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Austria"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90860918</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PASTURE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Protection Against Allergy Study in Rural Environments</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Protection against Allergy STUdy in Rural Environments</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Protection against Allergy-Study in Rural Environments</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Protection Against Allergy: Study in Rural Environments</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90860918</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies of food allergy and IgE sensitization.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41724405</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PASTURE study is a prospective birth cohort study started in 2002 and is conducted in children from rural areas of 5 European countries (Austria, Finland, France, Germany, and Switzerland) (58).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
