        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
