        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90455614</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women&apos;s Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GGLAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GGLAD consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Glaucoma in People of African Descent</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Glaucoma in People of African Descent Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90455614</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A multi-cohort genome-wide association study in African ancestry individuals reveals risk loci for primary open-angle glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38242088</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11844349</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a mega-analysis in a discovery cohort that combined three African ancestry datasets: the ADAGES study (n = 1,999),36 the GGLAD consortium (n = 2,952),37 and the Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics (POAAGG) study (n = 6,324)38 (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
