        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women&apos;s Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31688885</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
