        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of patients with critical COVID-19 admitted from March 2020 to the intensive care unit of Uppsala University Hospital, Sweden, who were enrolled in the prospective observational PronMed cohort and invited to follow-up three to six months after discharge, in which researchers at Uppsala University and Karolinska Institutet investigate the mechanisms of acute and long-term organ dysfunction in critical COVID-19, including its host genetics.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34597274</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35052684</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36271419</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
