    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454540</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MSCIC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mount Sinai COVID Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mount Sinai COVID-19 Biobank Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mount Sinai COVID-19 Biobank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454540</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of long COVID.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40399555</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12165857/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>of Long COVID (GOLD), Helix Exome+ and Healthy Nevada Project COVID-19 Phenotypes (Helix), MexGen-COVID Initiative, COVID-19 Ioannina Biobank (Ioannina), Genome-wide assessment of the gene variants associated with severe COVID-19 phenotype in Iran (IrCovid), Japan COVID-19 Task Force (JapanTaskForce), Lifelines, Norwegian Mother, Father and Child Cohort Study (MoBa), Mount Sinai COVID Biobank (MSCIC), Penn Medicine BioBank (PMBB), Follow-UP study of patients with critical COVID-19/COVID-19 Cohort Study of the University Hospital of the Technical University Munich (SweCovid/COMRI), Tirschenreuth Study (TiKoCo), TwinsUK, UK Biobank and Understanding Society—UK Household Longitudinal Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32719485</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36482101</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MSCIC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-020-1004-3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this Correspondence, we provide an account of a 49-day period during which we built a COVID-19 research biobank with samples from patients hospitalized in a large New York City health system.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90320249</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>4D</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>4D Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DDDD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>German Diabetes and Dialysis Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Die Deutsche Diabetes Dialyse Studie</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90320249</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Lowering of Circulating Sclerostin May Increase Risk of Atherosclerosis and Its Risk Factors: Evidence From a Genome-Wide Association Meta-Analysis Followed by Mendelian Randomization.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37096546</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10586470/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We found that this variant showed a robust negative effect on sclerostin in all cohorts; however, the genetic effect estimate was particularly large in the 4D cohort, comprising individuals with end‐stage chronic kidney disease (CKD) (Supplementary Table 5B).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:10412782</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37779851</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37806305</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>4D</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DDDD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10627490/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, aged 18–80 years, who had received maintenance hemodialysis for less than 2 years were included by 178 dialysis centers in Germany into the 4 D study (Die Deutsche Diabetes Dialyse Studie/German Diabetes and Dialysis Study).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90455614</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADAGES</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90455614</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A multi-cohort genome-wide association study in African ancestry individuals reveals risk loci for primary open-angle glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38242088</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11844349</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included three African ancestry datasets in the discovery analyses (n=11,275): (1) African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study study (n=1,999), (2) Genetics of Glaucoma in People of African Descent consortium (n=2,952), and (3) Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics study (n=6,324).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19752422</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29361356</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30352225</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADAGES</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6050158/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>There were 3266 glaucoma patients and controls without glaucoma of African or European descent recruited from five study centers in different regions of the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90668017</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children&apos;s Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADMIRAL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADMIRAL Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Admixture and Risk of Acute Leukemia</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ADMIxture and Risk of Acute Leukemia Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90668017</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of childhood B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia reveals novel African ancestry-specific susceptibility loci.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41125582</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12546916/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we show differences in the genetic architecture of childhood B-ALL risk in African ancestral populations with an analysis of 4200 African American children, including 840 B-ALL cases, as a part of the ADMIxture and Risk of Acute Leukemia (ADMIRAL) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children&apos;s Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41125582</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADMIRAL</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12546916/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Archived newborn dried blood spots (DBS) with matching birth certificate information held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health were obtained for cases and calendar birth year-, sex-, and race/ethnicity-matched (based on mother’s race/ethnicity) controls with no cancer history were obtained as a part of a larger population-based case-control study with linked cancer registry information through the Michigan Cancer Surveillance Program</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST001595</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family study of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, United States, begun by the University of Maryland in 1997, which identified Amish adults with osteoporosis by bone mineral density screening and recruited their first-degree relatives aged 20 and over and their spouses, measuring bone density by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, to find genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis and bone health in large multigenerational families.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AFOS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Amish Family Osteoporosis Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001595</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>WNT16 influences bone mineral density, cortical bone thickness, bone strength, and osteoporotic fracture risk.</dcterms:title>
