        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST001189</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control sample of people of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry from the New York area, with Parkinson&apos;s disease cases recruited at the Center for Parkinson&apos;s Disease and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University and controls evaluated in the same way, assembled from two Columbia University studies, the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study, for a genome-wide association study of Parkinson&apos;s disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AJ GWAS dataset</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ash-Jewish</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ashkenazi Jewish Dataset</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">The Ashkenazi Jewish Dataset</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001189</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study identifies candidate genes for Parkinson&apos;s disease in an Ashkenazi Jewish population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21812969</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3166909/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The AJ GWAS dataset was created by combining participants from two studies the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control sample of people of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry from the New York area, with Parkinson&apos;s disease cases recruited at the Center for Parkinson&apos;s Disease and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University and controls evaluated in the same way, assembled from two Columbia University studies, the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study, for a genome-wide association study of Parkinson&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21812969</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ash-Jewish</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3166909/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We applied a GWAS approach to a relatively homogeneous Ashkenazi Jewish (AJ) population from New York to search for both &apos;rare&apos; and &apos;common&apos; genetic variants that confer risk of PD by examining any SNPs with allele frequencies exceeding 2%.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90301382</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ASSESS-AKI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ASSESS-AKI Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Assessment, Serial Evaluation, and Subsequent Sequelae in Acute Kidney Injury Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Assessment, Serial Evaluation, and Subsequent Sequelae of AKI Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Assessment, Serial Evaluation, and Subsequent Sequelae of Acute Kidney Injury Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90301382</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Association Study for AKI.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37273234</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10371295/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a genome-wide association study in 1369 participants in the Assessment, Serial Evaluation, and Subsequent Sequelae of AKI Study; a multiethnic population of hospitalized participants with and without AKI matched on demographics, comorbidities, and kidney function before hospitalization.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20799966</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32707221</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ASSESS-AKI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7374148/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>during preoperative evaluation for cardiac surgery at Yale University (New Haven, CT) and London Health Sciences Center (Ontario, Canada).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2944247/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The multi-center cohort includes various U.S. and Canadian sites and health care delivery systems</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST010723</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents&apos; registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Age-related diseases: understanding genetic and non-genetic influences - a study at the University of Regensburg</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Altersbezogene Untersuchungen zur Gesundheit der Universität Regensburg</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AugUR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AugUR study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Age-related diseases: Understanding Genetic and non-genetic influences - a study at the University of Regensburg</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST010723</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis for early age-related macular degeneration highlights novel loci and insights for advanced disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32843070</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7449002/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our studies were primarily population-based cohort studies, where the baseline survey data were used for this analysis from studies of the authors (GHS, LIFE, NICOLA, KORA, AugUR) as well as for publicly available studies from dbGaP (ARIC, CHS, WHI; accession numbers: phs000090.v5.p1, phs000287.v6.p1, phs000746.v2.p3).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents&apos; registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26489512</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37721739</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AugUR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
