        <rdfs:comment>Bambui (Brazil) Cohort Study of Ageing (BAMBUI): the EPIGEN-Brazil Initiative is funded by the Brazilian Ministry of Health (Department of Science and Technology from the Secretaria de Ciência, Tecnologia e Insumos Estratégicos) through Financiadora de Estudos e Projetos.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23251690</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33633342</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
