        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9558840/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BioImage study (NCT00738725) is a multi-ethnic, observational study aimed at characterizing subclinical atherosclerosis in 6,699 US adults (55-80 years at baseline, 2008- 2009) at risk for, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Barbados"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Latin_America_and_the_Caribbean"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90094651</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island&apos;s only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BNCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Barbados National Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90094651</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Associations between age of menarche and genetic variation in women of African descent: genome-wide association study and polygenic score analysis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34706928</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9011920/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Root consortium is comprised of six epidemiologic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry: the Nigerian Breast Cancer Study (Ibadan, Nigeria); the Barbados National Cancer Study (Barbados); the Southern Community Cohort (southern United States); the Baltimore Breast Cancer Study (Baltimore, United States); the Racial Variability in Genotypic Determinants of Breast Cancer Risk Study (Detroit and Pennsylvania, United States); and the Chicago Cancer Prone Study (Chicago, United States).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island&apos;s only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18814239</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22357627</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BNCS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Barbados"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20843400+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>BNCS is a case-control study of environmental risk factors for breast and prostate cancer in a predominantly African-origin population in Barbados.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST000679</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A single-centre prospective observational registry cohort of adults with rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed by a rheumatologist, enrolled from March 2003 at the Brigham and Women&apos;s Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Participants are followed with annual visits, semi-annual questionnaires and stored blood samples, to find biomarkers that predict drug response, toxicity, disease activity and prognosis and to describe the natural history of treated rheumatoid arthritis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BRASS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Brigham Rheumatoid Arthritis Sequential Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Brigham and Women&apos;s Hospital Rheumatoid Arthritis Sequential Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Brigham and Women&apos;s Rheumatoid Arthritis Sequential Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST000679</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study meta-analysis identifies seven new rheumatoid arthritis risk loci.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20453842</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4243840/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study expands upon our previous GWAS meta-analysis of 3,393 cases and 12,462 controls by (a) adding a new GWAS dataset of 483 RA cases recruited from the Boston area (Brigham Rheumatoid Arthritis Sequential Study, BRASS) and 1,449 shared controls, (b) adding 513 cases and 431 controls recruited from Sweden (Epidemiological Investigation of Rheumatoid Arthritis, EIRA), (c) incorporating a recently published GWAS of 2,418 cases and 4,504 controls recruited from North America (Canada and North American Rheumatoid Arthritis Consortium-III, NARAC-III), and (d) adding additional shared controls to the NARAC-III dataset.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A single-centre prospective observational registry cohort of adults with rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed by a rheumatologist, enrolled from March 2003 at the Brigham and Women&apos;s Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Participants are followed with annual visits, semi-annual questionnaires and stored blood samples, to find biomarkers that predict drug response, toxicity, disease activity and prognosis and to describe the natural history of treated rheumatoid arthritis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31002669</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33002337</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01793103</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BRASS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6474583/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Enrollment for the registry began in March of 2003 in the Brigham and Women’s Hospital Arthritis Center in the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293">
