        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute&apos;s Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease&apos;s complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.</owl:annotatedTarget>
