    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90451657</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses&apos; Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGEMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Cancer Institute Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Cancer Institute Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility initiative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90451657</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Deciphering the genetics and mechanisms of predisposition to multiple myeloma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39103364</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-50932-7/MediaObjects/41467_2024_50932_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses&apos; Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17529973</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22271044</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGEMS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3374121/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohort studies were: the Prostate, Lung Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO, subjects from continental USA) (Gohagan et al. 2000); the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II (CPS-II, from continental USA) (Calle et al. 2002) and the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study (ATBC, from Finland) (1994).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
