    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90824165</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHAVI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIAID Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90824165</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiancestry Genome-Wide Association Study Identifies Variants in a Zinc Finger Gene Cluster as Novel Regulators of HIV Control.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41640362</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20041166</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20205591</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21160409</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23935489</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24910414</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CHAVI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21160409+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) in a population of 1532 individuals from Malawi, a country with high prevalence of HIV-1 infection.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2791220/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients have been included from two sources (Text S1): [1] Euro-CHAVI, a Consortium of 8 European and 1 Australian Cohorts/Studies; and [2] MACS, the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study that enrolled homosexual and bisexual men in 4 US cities.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24910414+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Nine site-affiliated laboratories in Africa and the USA collected and processed PBMCs, and cryopreserved PBMC were shipped to CHAVI repositories in Africa and the USA for long-term storage.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90837424</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients&apos; first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CKC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese Keratoconus Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese keratoconus cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chinese Keratoconus Cohort Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90837424</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of Novel Loci With Keratoconus Susceptibility in a Chinese Genome-Wide Association Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38767907</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114610/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 958 patients with KC from the Chinese keratoconus (CKC) cohort study and 7186 controls were included in the current study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients&apos; first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38703249</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39186261</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40642536</obo:IAO_0000119>
