        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454186</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium of population- and hospital-based endometrial cancer studies in Europe, North America and Australia, whose cases of European ancestry were genotyped on the iCOGS and OncoArray arrays and compared with country-matched controls, mainly from the Breast Cancer Association Consortium, in genome-wide association studies of endometrial cancer risk.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ECAC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454186</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>GWAS meta-analysis identifies five susceptibility loci for endometrial cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40633141</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40633141+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Building on genome-wide association studies (GWASs) by the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium, we conducted a GWAS meta-analysis of 17,278 endometrial cancer cases and 289,180 controls, incorporating biobank samples from the UK, Finland, Estonia and Japan.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of population- and hospital-based endometrial cancer studies in Europe, North America and Australia, whose cases of European ancestry were genotyped on the iCOGS and OncoArray arrays and compared with country-matched controls, mainly from the Breast Cancer Association Consortium, in genome-wide association studies of endometrial cancer risk.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27135401</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30093612</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40633141</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ECAC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>606 ANECS samples all of endometrioid-only histology were used for the original endometrial cancer case-control GWAS and a further 538 were genotyped using iCOGS for the first additional genotyping phase.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001520"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13537468/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted replication analysis of the 15 loci detected in the discovery GWAS in two separate cohorts (Belgian and German), previously used within the collaboration of ECAC [5]. Replication in the Belgian population included 528 cases from the Leuven Endometrial Cancer Study (LES) and 1,266 controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre Study (LMBC). Replication analysis in the German population included 221 cases from the Bavarian Endometrial Cancer Study (BECS) and 251 healthy controls aged 55 years and older from the Bavarian Breast Cancer Cases and Controls (BBCC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the iCOGS genotyping stage, 4,330 women with a confirmed diagnosis of endometrial cancer and European ancestry were recruited via 11 studies in Western Europe, North America and Australia, collectively called the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium (ECAC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Belgium; hospital based cases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Germany; hospital-based cases, population-based cases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Norway; population based cases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>this population based case-control study was conducted among Swedish women aged 50-74 years, who were residing in Sweden between January 1st 1994 and December 31st 1995.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>National Study of the Genetics of Endometrial Cancer (NSECG) cases were identified from collaborating clinicians throughout the UK from 2008 to 2013, taking care not to recruit from centres involved in SEARCH.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001316"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>USA; Clinic based cases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90726611</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ECHA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ECHA study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>European Challenge for Healthy Aging project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>European Challenge for Healthy Aging study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">European Challenge for Healthy Aging</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90726611</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic associations with longevity in a Calabrian cohort: an exploratory genome-wide study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42176242</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11357-026-02334-4</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The oldest subjects (90-plus individuals) were enrolled in two European projects investigating genetic and environmental factors associated with aging: the European Challenge for Healthy Aging (ECHA) project [24] and the GEnetics of Healthy Ageing (GEHA) project [25].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16870633</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17989723</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20584770</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42176242</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ECHA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17989723+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Population pools of 1.6, 2.3 and 2.0 million inhabitants were screened, respectively, in Denmark, France and Italy to identify families matching the design requirements.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90662914</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children&apos;s Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EDC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epidemiology of Diabetes Complications study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pittsburgh Epidemiology of Diabetes Complications Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90662914</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetics of C-Peptide and Age at Diagnosis in Type 1 Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39556808</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11755686/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A meta-GWAS of AAD was performed that comprised all studies included in the C-peptide meta-GWAS plus the Pittsburgh Epidemiology of Diabetes Complications (EDC) study (22).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children&apos;s Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22851572</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37533055</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39932735</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EDC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3478551/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Pittsburgh Epidemiology of Diabetes Complications (EDC) study cohort provides a unique opportunity to examine mortality and life-expectancy changes over time in a U.S. cohort with long-term (&gt;30 years) follow-up, because the participants were all diagnosed with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes between 1950 and 1980.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001319 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001319">
