        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339754/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With funding from the Brazilian government, as detailed in Acknowledgements, a group of Brazilian epidemiologists and clinicians from six institutions (Federal Universities of Bahia, Espírito Santo, Minas Gerais and Rio Grande do Sul; University of São Paulo; and Oswaldo Cruz Foundation), led by the authors of this article, organized the Study in centres located in state capitals of the north-eastern, south-eastern and southern regions of Brazil.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kenya"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tanzania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uganda"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90652520</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EMBLEM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EMBLEM study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epidemiology of Burkitt Lymphoma in East-African Children and Minors</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epidemiology of Burkitt lymphoma in East African children and minors</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Epidemiology of Burkitt Lymphoma in East African Children and Minors</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90652520</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study identifies an African-specific locus on chromosome 21q22.12 associated with Burkitt lymphoma risk and survival.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40646133</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12380610/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the EMBLEM study enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0-15 years from six neighboring rural geographical areas—two each in Uganda, Kenya, and Tanzania (Figure 1a) during 2010-2016.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
