        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GO</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Aged Study was conducted in 1993 as a multi-wave mailout to 4562 twins (2281 pairs) aged over 50 years old who were registered with the Australian Twin Registry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The China Kadoorie Biobank (CKB) is a prospective cohort of 512,000 adults aged 30-79 years, recruited from ten rural and urban areas of China during 2004-2008.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study is based on material from Copenhagen Hospital Biobank (CHB), a regional biobank containing leftover EDTA whole blood samples from type and screen analyses in patients admitted to hospitals in the Capital Region of Denmark.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Estonia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Estonian Biobank cohort is a volunteer-based sample of the Estonian resident adult population (aged ≥18 years).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aim is to get 500,000 Finns to participate in the study through donations of samples to biobanks.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The osteoarthritis participants’ recruitment was conducted in the city of Larissa, central Greece.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hong_Kong"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Volunteers of southern Chinese ancestry living in Hong Kong were recruited for assessment which included a questionnaire for low back pain and associated symptoms and sagittal T2-weighted fast spin-echo MRI of the spine.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Iceland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The deCODE genetics osteoarthritis study is an ongoing population based study in Iceland that was initiated in 1997.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japanese cohort of knee OA GWAS (disease cohort) consists of 900 cases and 3,400 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The RAAK study is aimed at the biobanking of joint materials as well as mesenchymal stem cells and primary chondrocytes from patients (paired preserved and OA affected cartilage samples) and controls in the Leiden University Medical Center and collaborating outpatient clinics in the Leiden area in The Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HUNT Study is a longitudinal, population-based health study, which has been conducted in the county of Nord-Trøndelag, Norway, since 1984.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Samples were collected in 2 stages from 10 United Kingdom locations (London, Nottingham, Oxford, Sheffield, Southampton, Edinburgh, Newcastle-Upon-Tyne, Sheffield, Wansbeck, and Worcester).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The United States Million Veteran Program (MVP) is a national research program to learn how genes, lifestyle, and military exposures affect health and illness.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90267543</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GO-CAT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267543</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide analyses of platinum-induced ototoxicity in childhood cancer patients: Results of GO-CAT and United Kingdom MAGIC consortia.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36699085</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36699085+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Therefore, a genome-wide association study was performed in the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment (GO-CAT) cohort (n = 261) and the United Kingdom Molecular Genetics of Adverse Drug Reactions in Children Study (United Kingdom MAGIC) cohort (n = 248).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36699085</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GO-CAT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9870026/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participating centers included Radboud university medical center (Nijmegen, Netherlands), University Medical Center of Groningen (Groningen, Netherlands), Leiden University Medical Center (Leiden, Netherlands), Academic Medical Center (Amsterdam, Netherlands), Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Nazionale Tumori (Milan, Italy) and The Children’s Hospital at Westmead (Sydney, Australia).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90301252</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GODDAF</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Origin of Dupuytren Disease Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Origin of Dupuytren Disease study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Origin of Dupuytren Disease and Associated Fibromatosis study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90301252</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association meta-analysis implicates Hedgehog and Notch signaling in Dupuytren&apos;s disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38172110</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10764787/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We gratefully thank the participants and investigators of the GODDAF study, Lifelines biobank, BSSH-GODD study, United Kingdom Household Longitudinal study, the UK Biobank initiative, German Dupuytren Study, FinnGen study, PopGen and Kora studies for their important contributions.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28886342</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30688894</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37257093</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GODDAF</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the GODDAF study, case subjects were identified from plastic surgery clinics within the Netherlands, and DNA and phenotype data were obtained as previously described.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90336598</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site&apos;s undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GOI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Impulsivity project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90336598</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic contributions to performance on the Balloon Analogue Risk Task.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37582857</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618088/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Genetic, cognitive and behavioral data were similarly collected in the Genetics of Impulsivity (GOI) project, performed at the University of Georgia and the University of Chicago.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site&apos;s undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27449350</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29120849</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37582857</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GOI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618088/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 934 Caucasian-ancestry participants 18–30 years of age were tested at two sites (40% at Athens, GA and 60% Chicago, IL).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90295957</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family-based study of Latinos of Mexican or Central American origin in the Los Angeles area, run jointly by Cedars-Sinai Medical Center and the Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center, which from 2007 recruited probands with type 2 diabetes and either diabetic retinopathy or diabetes of at least ten years&apos; duration together with their siblings and parents, with retinopathy graded from fundus photographs, to study the genetics of diabetic retinopathy and other complications of diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GOLDR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Latinos Diabetic Retinopathy Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Latinos Diabetic Retinopathy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90295957</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide study investigating effector genes and polygenic prediction for kidney function in persons with ancestry from Africa and the Americas.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38190104</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10794846/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Genetics of Latinos Diabetic Retinopathy (GOLDR): GOLDR was supported in part by the Genetics of Latinos Diabetic Retinopathy (GOLDR) Study grant EY14684.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family-based study of Latinos of Mexican or Central American origin in the Los Angeles area, run jointly by Cedars-Sinai Medical Center and the Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center, which from 2007 recruited probands with type 2 diabetes and either diabetic retinopathy or diabetes of at least ten years&apos; duration together with their siblings and parents, with retinopathy graded from fundus photographs, to study the genetics of diabetic retinopathy and other complications of diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22330960</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25452868</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GOLDR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4212555/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Large family-based cohort of Latinos with type 2 diabetes recruited exclusively in the Los Angeles area.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90320242</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson&apos;s initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson&apos;s disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson&apos;s disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson&apos;s disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GP2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Global Parkinson&apos;s Disease Genetics Program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Global Parkinson&apos;s Genetics Program</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90320242</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of genetic risk loci and causal insights associated with Parkinson&apos;s disease in African and African admixed populations: a genome-wide association study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37633302</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37633302+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Individuals were included from several cohorts that were available as a part of the Global Parkinson&apos;s Genetics Program, the International Parkinson&apos;s Disease Genomics Consortium Africa, and 23andMe.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson&apos;s initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson&apos;s disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson&apos;s disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33513272</obo:IAO_0000119>
