        <owl:annotatedTarget>An electronic medical record-linked biorepository at Mayo Clinic, begun in 2006, that archives DNA, plasma and serum and a questionnaire from consecutive adult patients with known or suspected atherosclerotic vascular disease (such as carotid artery stenosis, abdominal aortic aneurysm or peripheral arterial disease) referred for non-invasive vascular evaluation or exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center, ascertaining disease and comorbidities with electronic phenotyping algorithms, to discover genetic and circulating biomarkers of atherosclerotic vascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
