    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST003864</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NFS-ORPS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NFS-ORPS/Cambridge</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">UK Nephropathy Family Study and Oxford Regional Prospective Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST003864</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Genetic Landscape of Renal Complications in Type 1 Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27647854</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5280020/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GWAS discovery stage included 3135–5156 subjects with T1D, depending on phenotypic comparison (Supplemental Figure 1), from four studies: FinnDiane,23 the EURODIAB Family Study,24 the Scania Diabetes Registry (SDR),25 and the UK Nephropathy Family Study and Oxford Regional Prospective Study (NFS-ORPS/Cambridge)26,27 (Supplemental Tables 2 and 3, Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19918004</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21335371</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27647854</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NFS-ORPS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NFS-ORPS/Cambridge</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5280020/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GWAS discovery stage included 3135–5156 subjects with T1D, depending on phenotypic comparison (Supplemental Figure 1), from four studies: FinnDiane,23 the EURODIAB Family Study,24 the Scania Diabetes Registry (SDR),25 and the UK Nephropathy Family Study and Oxford Regional Prospective Study (NFS-ORPS/Cambridge)26,27 (Supplemental Tables 2 and 3, Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3064014/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 2000 and 2005, the NFS recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes throughout England (8).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19918004</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal study of young people with type 1 diabetes in England, set up in 2000 within the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study of the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory. In 2000–2005 it recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol and Oxford, together with their parents. It followed them with annual urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratios and HbA1c measurements for phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NFS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UK Nephropathy Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nephropathy Family Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19918004</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Maternal but not paternal association of ambulatory blood pressure with albumin excretion in young offspring with type 1 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19918004</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population was composed of young people with type 1 diabetes and their parents recruited in the Nephropathy Family Study (NFS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal study of young people with type 1 diabetes in England, set up in 2000 within the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study of the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory. In 2000–2005 it recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol and Oxford, together with their parents. It followed them with annual urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratios and HbA1c measurements for phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19171721</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19918004</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NFS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3064014/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 2000 and 2005, the NFS recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes throughout England (8).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The NFS was set up in 2000 as part of the Juvenile Diabetes Research Foundation/Wellcome Trust Diabetes Inflammation Laboratory: Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study (14).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cameroon"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Central_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nigeria"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uganda"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Western_Africa"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90094651</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital&apos;s outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym NBCS also denotes Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study (COHO:0000572) and Norwegian Breast Cancer Study (COHO:0000573); this term is Nigerian Breast Cancer Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NBCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NigBCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Nigerian breast cancer study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nigerian Breast Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90094651</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Associations between age of menarche and genetic variation in women of African descent: genome-wide association study and polygenic score analysis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34706928</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9011920/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Root consortium is comprised of six epidemiologic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry: the Nigerian Breast Cancer Study (Ibadan, Nigeria); the Barbados National Cancer Study (Barbados); the Southern Community Cohort (southern United States); the Baltimore Breast Cancer Study (Baltimore, United States); the Racial Variability in Genotypic Determinants of Breast Cancer Risk Study (Detroit and Pennsylvania, United States); and the Chicago Cancer Prone Study (Chicago, United States).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital&apos;s outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20716701</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30130155</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40249615</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NBCS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NigBCS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uganda"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008756/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The NBCS started enrolling women with breast cancer (hereafter cases) and women without breast cancer (hereafter controls) in Nigeria in 1998 and, in 2011, enrollment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda using the same questionnaire and protocol.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90833064</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient&apos;s consent, the patient&apos;s details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NJR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Joint Registry for England and Wales</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Joint Registry for England, Wales, Northern Ireland, and the Isle of Man</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Joint Registry for England, Wales, Northern Ireland, the Isle of Man and the States of Guernsey</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">National Joint Registry</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90833064</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic study identifies novel genes in developmental dysplasia of the hip.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41912496</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13035913/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DDH samples were identified from the National Joint Registry cohort, which at the time included 5 411 adult individuals living in England who had undergone a hip replacement surgery for DDH.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient&apos;s consent, the patient&apos;s details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.njrcentre.org.uk/about-the-njr/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382"/>
