        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90277419</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PLATO</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PLATO trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PLATelet Inhibition and Patient Outcomes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PLATelet inhibition and patient Outcomes trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Platelet Inhibition and Patient Outcomes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PLATelet inhibition and patient Outcomes</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90277419</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Vascular endothelial growth factor-D plasma levels and VEGFD genetic variants are independently associated with outcomes in patients with cardiovascular disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36869765</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36869765+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Levels of VEGF biomarkers, including bFGF, Flt-1, KDR (VEGFR2), PlGF, Tie-2, VEGF-A, VEGF-C, and VEGF-D, were measured in the PLATO ACS cohort (n = 2091, discovery cohort).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
