    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90624455</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A UK research study sponsored by Guy&apos;s and St Thomas&apos; NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients&apos; relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PLUM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pustular psoriasis: eLucidating Underlying Mechanisms</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pustular Psoriasis, Elucidating Underlying Mechanisms</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624455</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide meta-analysis of palmoplantar pustulosis implicates TH2 responses and cigarette smoking in disease pathogenesis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38815935</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2024/01/17/2024.01.17.24301406.full.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UK dataset included 288 affected individuals of European descent, who were recruited in specialist dermatology centers as part of the APRICOT clinical trial4 and its sister study PLUM.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A UK research study sponsored by Guy&apos;s and St Thomas&apos; NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients&apos; relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30036598</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32936291</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PLUM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32936291+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A UK data set including 203 patients was obtained through the Anakinra in Pustular Psoriasis, Response in a Controlled Trial (2016-2019) and its sister research study Pustular Psoriasis, Elucidating Underlying Mechanisms (2016-2020).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90455614</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania&apos;s Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>POAAGG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>primary open-angle African American glaucoma genetics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90455614</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A multi-cohort genome-wide association study in African ancestry individuals reveals risk loci for primary open-angle glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38242088</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11844349</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, the POAAGG study population consists of self-identified Blacks (African American, African descent, or African Caribbean), aged 35 years or older, recruited from the Philadelphia area.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania&apos;s Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25576993</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28705151</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40782885</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>POAAGG</owl:annotatedTarget>
