        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90833053</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups&apos; ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project MinE ALS Sequencing Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project MinE ALS sequencing Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project MinE ALS sequencing consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project_MinE_ALS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Project MinE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90833053</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale exome analyses reveal new rare variant contributions in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41917433</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13083253/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Case cohorts included the Project MinE ALS sequencing consortium (7,614 cases; 2,605 controls)47, the NYGC ALS Consortium (2,650 cases; 342 controls), the ALS Sequencing Consortium (2,851 cases)5, two cohorts from the FALS consortium (1,277 cases; phs001585), the National Institutes of Health (NIH) Exome Sequencing of FALS Project (194 cases; phs000101), two Australian cohorts described in ref. 48 (125 cases, 18 controls) and ref. 49 (568 cases), and a Chinese motor neurone disease (MND) cohort50 (583 cases, 182 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups&apos; ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29955173</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36589292</obo:IAO_0000119>
