        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of homosexual and bisexual men recruited in 1978–1980 at the San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B, whose stored serum specimens, follow-up examinations and questionnaires, and linkage to AIDS surveillance and death registries were later used to study the natural history, transmission and cofactors of HIV infection and AIDS.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SFCCC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>San Francisco City Clinic Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
