        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90451657</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A national biobank of samples from patients with multiple myeloma in Sweden, based at Skåne University Hospital in Lund, whose patients&apos; germline DNA has been genotyped for genome-wide association studies of inherited susceptibility to multiple myeloma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SNMB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Swedish Myeloma Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Swedish National Myeloma Biobank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90451657</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Deciphering the genetics and mechanisms of predisposition to multiple myeloma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39103364</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-50932-7/MediaObjects/41467_2024_50932_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This project is made feasible by that fact that our constellation is closely involved in coordinating the Swedish Myeloma Biobank as well as clinical studies on MM and MGUS in Sweden and the Nordic region, providing access to samples from patient cohorts that are sufficiently large to allow a GWAS.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national biobank of samples from patients with multiple myeloma in Sweden, based at Skåne University Hospital in Lund, whose patients&apos; germline DNA has been genotyped for genome-wide association studies of inherited susceptibility to multiple myeloma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26007630</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27363682</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31363079</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SNMB</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4455110/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the Swedish-Norwegian discovery sample set, we obtained 1,668 and 157 samples from the Swedish National Myeloma Biobank (Skåne University Hospital, Lund, Sweden) and the Norwegian Biobank for Myeloma (Trondheim, Norway), respectively.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001410 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001410">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22158537</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case–control study of Korean patients with type 2 diabetes from the Diabetes Clinic of Seoul National University Hospital, South Korea, excluding patients positive for GAD antibodies, and of nondiabetic control subjects aged 60 or over with no history of diabetes in themselves or their first-degree relatives, used as a replication study in the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SNUHDS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Seoul National University Hospital Diabetes Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001410"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22158537</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies identifies eight new loci for type 2 diabetes in east Asians.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22158537</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3582398/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Stage 3 included up to, 12,284 cases and 13,172 controls from five different studies comprised of the Japan Cardiometabolic Genome Epidemiology Network (CAGE), the Shanghai Diabetes Study I/II (SDS I/II), the Chinese University of Hong Kong Diabetes Study (CUHKDS), the National Taiwan University Hospital Diabetes Study (NTUHDS) and the Seoul National University Hospital Diabetes Study (SNUHDS) for de novo replication analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001410"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control study of Korean patients with type 2 diabetes from the Diabetes Clinic of Seoul National University Hospital, South Korea, excluding patients positive for GAD antibodies, and of nondiabetic control subjects aged 60 or over with no history of diabetes in themselves or their first-degree relatives, used as a replication study in the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22158537</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
