        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.elsevier.com/about/press-releases/having-a-bad-hair-day-blame-your-genes</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The first genome-wide association study (GWAS) on human scalp hair whorls was performed among 2,149 Chinese individuals from the National Survey of Physical Traits cohort, followed by a replication study in 1,950 Chinese individuals from the Taizhou Longitudinal Study cohort.</rdfs:comment>
