    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90026612</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DEFINE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DEFINE Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DEFINE-FMD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DEFINE-FMD Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DEFINE-FMD study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Define-FMD Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Defining the Basis of Fibromuscular Dysplasia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90026612</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic investigation of fibromuscular dysplasia identifies risk loci and shared genetics with common cardiovascular diseases.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34654805</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>DEFINE-FMD purpose was to establish a library of fibroblasts, DNA, plasma and serum from patients with FMD and unaffected healthy control subjects.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31424497</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39271816</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DEFINE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DEFINE-FMD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>(9) DEFINE-FMD, USA, N: 108, N Women (%): 108 (100.0)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90255389</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COHRA2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COHRA2 study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia Cohort 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, cohort 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia cohort 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90255389</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of Early Childhood Caries with Bitter Taste Receptors: A Meta-Analysis of Genome-Wide Association Studies and Transcriptome-Wide Association Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36672800</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858612/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The second cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia (COHRA2) is a longitudinal study of the genetic, microbial, and environmental factors impacting oral health and is separate from COHRA1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26089906</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38404680</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>COHRA2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4451284/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The COHRA2 protocol is presented in detail, including inclusion criteria (healthy, adult, pregnant, US Caucasian, English speaking, and nonimmunocompromised women), recruiting (two sites: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and West Virginia, USA), assessments (demographic, medical, dental, psychosocial/behavioral, and oral microbial samples and DNA), timelines (longitudinal from pregnancy to young childhood), quality control, and retention rates.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90104565</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIT-2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIT-2 Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIT-2 study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIT2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Analysis of Idiopathic Thrombophilia 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Analysis of Idiopathic Thrombophilia 2 Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104565</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Integrated GWAS and Gene Expression Suggest ORM1 as a Potential Regulator of Plasma Levels of Cell-Free DNA and Thrombosis Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35272364</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9251712/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We aimed to identify genes involved in the regulation of cfDNA levels using data from the Genetic Analysis of Idiopathic Thrombophilia (GAIT-2) Project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26784699</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35272364</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GAIT-2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GAIT2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9251712/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All of the individuals were recruited at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau (Barcelona, Spain) from 2006 to 2010.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90000048</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of cohort studies that carries out genome-wide association meta-analyses of human reproductive behaviour, such as age at first sex, age at first birth, number of children ever born and childlessness, in people of European ancestry; after a first study of age at first birth and number of children ever born, it meta-analysed cohorts for age at first sex and age at first birth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HRBC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Human Reproductive Behaviour Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90000048</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of 371 genetic variants for age at first sex and birth linked to externalising behaviour.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34211149</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7612120/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Authors in the Human Reproductive Behaviour Consortium contributed the valuable data, conducted cohort specific GWAS and other analyses, and contributed through the administration, management, and data collection for the participating cohorts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of cohort studies that carries out genome-wide association meta-analyses of human reproductive behaviour, such as age at first sex, age at first birth, number of children ever born and childlessness, in people of European ancestry; after a first study of age at first birth and number of children ever born, it meta-analysed cohorts for age at first sex and age at first birth.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34211149</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
