    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90992867</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SerGen-Covid-19</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SerGenCovid19</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Serum Genetic Covid-19 study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SerGenCovid-19</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90992867</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>&lt;i&gt;CMTM8&lt;/i&gt; variants influence BNT162b2 COVID-19 vaccination response by regulating granulocytic/polymorphonuclear myeloid-derived suppressor cell activity.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41659846</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12875989/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we conducted a Genome Wide Association Study (GWAS) on anti-S IgG levels following Pfizer-BioNTech COVID-19 vaccination in 1,968 participants from the SerGenCovid-19 initiative, a cohort study comprising 7,169 genetically characterized individuals from the general Italian population.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41659846</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SerGen-Covid-19</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SerGenCovid19</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12875989/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SerGenCovid-19 project successfully collected data from 7,169 participants across Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90026609</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, three-arm phase III trial led by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B, with the North Central Cancer Treatment Group (as N063H), the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group and the Southwest Oncology Group taking part, that enrolled patients aged 18 or over with locally recurrent (stage IIIC) or metastatic (stage IV) breast cancer and no prior chemotherapy for metastatic disease at institutions in the United States from 2008 to 2011, comparing first-line paclitaxel once per week with nab-paclitaxel or ixabepilone once per week, each given with bevacizumab (optional from March 2011), with progression-free survival as the primary end point.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCCTG N063H</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CALGB 40502</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90026609</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Bevacizumab-induced hypertension and proteinuria: a genome-wide study of more than 1000 patients.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34616010</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34616010+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A genome-wide association study (GWAS) meta-analysis was performed in 1039 bevacizumab-treated patients of European ancestry in four clinical trials (CALGB 40502, 40503, 80303, 90401).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, three-arm phase III trial led by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B, with the North Central Cancer Treatment Group (as N063H), the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group and the Southwest Oncology Group taking part, that enrolled patients aged 18 or over with locally recurrent (stage IIIC) or metastatic (stage IV) breast cancer and no prior chemotherapy for metastatic disease at institutions in the United States from 2008 to 2011, comparing first-line paclitaxel once per week with nab-paclitaxel or ixabepilone once per week, each given with bevacizumab (optional from March 2011), with progression-free survival as the primary end point.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26056183</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33981951</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00785291</obo:IAO_0000119>
