        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90429011</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CORNET</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CORNET consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CORtisol NETwork</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CORtisol NETwork Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cortisol Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CORtisol NETwork consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90429011</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Assessing the Role of Cortisol in Anxiety, Major Depression, and Neuroticism: A Mendelian Randomization Study Using &lt;i&gt;SERPINA6&lt;/i&gt;/&lt;i&gt;SERPINA1&lt;/i&gt; Variants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38525495</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10959652/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CORNET consortium, with a pooled mean age (SD) of 53.3 (11.2) years and 36.3% men, was a GWAS meta-analysis of 25,314 participants of European ancestry from 17 European population-based cohorts adjusted for age, sex, and genetic principal components (PCs) for population structure.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25010111</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33469137</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CORNET</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4091794/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Western Australia Pregnancy Cohort (Raine) recruited 2,900 pregnancies from King Edward Memorial Hospital between 1989 and 1991 as part of a randomised controlled trial which evaluated repeated ultrasounds in pregnancy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Croatia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8144017/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CROATIA-Split study, Croatia, is a population-based, cross-sectional study in the Dalmatian City of Split that so far includes 1000 examinees aged 18-95.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8144017/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Helsinki Birth Cohort Study (HBCS) is composed of 8,760 individuals born between the years 1934-44 in one of the two main maternity hospitals in Helsinki, Finland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8144017/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Study of Health in Pomerania (SHIP) is a population-based project conducted in Northeast Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4091794/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The InCHIANTI study is a population-based epidemiological study aimed at evaluating factors that influence mobility in the older population living in the Chianti region of Tuscany, Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
