        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22773825</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family-based study of young-onset breast cancer, conducted by the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences as an offshoot of the Sister Study, that in 2008–2010 enrolled women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 who had a sister in the Sister Study, together with their parents, and used the breast cancer-free Sister Study sisters as matched controls, to study genetic and environmental causes of young-onset breast cancer. The affected women are followed prospectively as breast cancer survivors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>2SISTER</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Two Sister Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Two Sister Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22773825</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fertility drugs and young-onset breast cancer: results from the Two Sister Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22773825</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22773825+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted the Two Sister Study, a sister-matched case-control study, by enrolling 1422 women between September 2008 and December 2010, who were younger than age 50 years at diagnosis with breast cancer and were enrolled within 4 years of diagnosis, and 1669 breast cancer-free control sisters from the Sister Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family-based study of young-onset breast cancer, conducted by the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences as an offshoot of the Sister Study, that in 2008–2010 enrolled women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 who had a sister in the Sister Study, together with their parents, and used the breast cancer-free Sister Study sisters as matched controls, to study genetic and environmental causes of young-onset breast cancer. The affected women are followed prospectively as breast cancer survivors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22773825</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>2SISTER</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>2SISTER The Two Sister Study USA Case-only study</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:38665804</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children&apos;s Hospital and Brigham and Women&apos;s Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation&apos;s EPHect standards.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>A2A</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Women&apos;s Health Study: From Adolescence to Adulthood</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Women&apos;s Health Study: from Adolescence to Adulthood</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Women&apos;s Health Study: From Adolescence to Adulthood</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:38665804</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Plasma microRNA expression in adolescents and young adults with endometriosis: the importance of hormone use.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38665804</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38665804+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Women&apos;s Health Study: from Adolescence to Adulthood (A2A) is an ongoing WERF EPHect compliant longitudinal cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children&apos;s Hospital and Brigham and Women&apos;s Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation&apos;s EPHect standards.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32833998</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38495219</obo:IAO_0000119>
