        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32424353</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study run from the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital (NKI-AVL) in Amsterdam, whose cases are women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 (operable invasive cancers diagnosed in 1970–1994 in four Dutch hospitals and, for the iCOGS and OncoArray genotyping, patients diagnosed in 1995–2011 at the NKI-AVL) and whose controls are women recruited through the Sanquin blood bank. A familial arm, ABCS-F, adds breast cancer patients without BRCA1/2 mutations from the NKI-AVL family cancer clinic, and the study contributes to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ABCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Amsterdam Breast Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
