    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2869325/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The second cohort, based on a blood pooling design [26] was collected from Adelaide, Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37845353</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of investigators in the United Kingdom, Australia and New Zealand formed to carry out a genome-wide association study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA). Its GWAS dataset pools AAA cases with DNA from eight centres in those countries and from the UK Small Aneurysm Trial, recruited from inpatients, outpatient clinics and population screening programmes, and compares them with Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aneurysm Consortium AAA GWAS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aneurysm Consortium AAA GWAS dataset</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aneurysm Consortium GWAS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Aneurysm Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Aneurysm Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37845353</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis identifies risk loci for abdominal aortic aneurysm and highlights PCSK9 as a therapeutic target.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37845353</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These two sets of weights were then used to calculate PRS in three external validation cohorts, two with control groups representative of the general population (UK Aneurysm Growth Study-UK Biobank (UKAGS-UKB) and Aneurysm Consortium-Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium (AC-WTCCC)) and one representative of populations with cardiovascular disease (Second manifestations of ARTerial disease (SMART)).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of investigators in the United Kingdom, Australia and New Zealand formed to carry out a genome-wide association study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA). Its GWAS dataset pools AAA cases with DNA from eight centres in those countries and from the UK Small Aneurysm Trial, recruited from inpatients, outpatient clinics and population screening programmes, and compares them with Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18621558</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22055160</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37845353</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Aneurysm Consortium (AC), cases of AAA together with available DNA recruited in eight centers in the UK, Australia, and New Zealand and also samples from the United Kingdom Small Aneurysm Trial from inpatient populations, outpatient clinics, or population screening programs in the participating centers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19404257</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ACC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ACC cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Autism CaseControl cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Autism Case-Control cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19404257</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Autism genome-wide copy number variation reveals ubiquitin and neuronal genes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19404257</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2925224/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We assembled an Autism Case-Control (ACC) cohort by collecting 859 ASD cases (from a total of 1,246 ACC cases, parents, and siblings) of European ancestry, and 1,409 healthy controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19404256</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19404257</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ACC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2943511/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To boost power for identifying these associations, we examined an Autism Case-Control cohort (ACC cohort, Table 1), comprising 1,453 subjects with ASDs from several US sites, and 7,070 control subjects without ASDs from the Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia, who were also genotyped on the same platform.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30262460</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ACCORD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Action to Control Cardiovascular Risk in Diabetes</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30262460</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Tools for Coronary Risk Assessment in Type 2 Diabetes: A Cohort Study From the ACCORD Clinical Trial.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30262460</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6196830/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We also evaluated the extent to which these genetic markers improve the prediction of incident MCE when added to conventional cardiovascular risk factors and assessed whether a genetic risk score (GRS) derived from these SNPs could identify subsets of patients with type 2 diabetes with different responses to intensive glucose, blood pressure, and lipid control in the Action to Control Cardiovascular Risk in Diabetes (ACCORD) trial.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17599422</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30262460</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ACCORD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6196830/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 10,251 participants with type 2 diabetes were recruited from seven clinical networks in the U.S. and Canada between 2001 and 2005 and randomized in a 1:1 ratio to receive intensive glucose-lowering treatment, aiming for an HbA1c level below 6%, or to standard treatment, aiming for an HbA1c level between 7.0% and 7.9%.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:16256881</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population of adults in East Anglia and Wales, United Kingdom, selected at random from local general practice lists and open-access cardiovascular risk assessment clinics and studied by investigators in Cambridge and Cardiff, comprising healthy people as well as people with cardiovascular risk factors or disease, whose peripheral and central blood pressure, wave reflection and aortic pulse wave velocity were measured, with questionnaires and blood samples, to study vascular ageing, arterial stiffness and central blood pressure across the adult lifespan.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ACCT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Anglo Cardiff Collaborative Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anglo-Cardiff Collaborative Trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466"/>
