        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Republic_of_Ireland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Slovakia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South-Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:26631737</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ADVANCE also denotes ADVANCE trial (COHO:0001052) and Atherosclerotic Disease, Vascular Function, and Genetic Epidemiology Study (COHO:0001053); this term is Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease: Preterax and Diamicron-MR Controlled Evaluation.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADVANCE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADVANCE_TRIAL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Action in Diabetes and Vascular Disease: PreterAx and DiamicroN Modified-Release Controlled Evaluation</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Action in Diabetes and Vascular Disease: Preterax and Diamicron MR Controlled Evaluation</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease: preterAx and diamicroN mr Controlled Evaluation</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease; preterAx and diamicroN-MR Controlled Evaluation</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease: Preterax and Diamicron-MR Controlled Evaluation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:26631737</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Association Studies Identify Genetic Loci Associated With Albuminuria in Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26631737</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4764151/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our study was based on 30 discovery and replication studies mostly from the general population, with the exception of Action in Diabetes and Vascular Disease: Preterax and Diamicron MR Controlled Evaluation (ADVANCE) and Genetics of Diabetic Nephropathy (GENDIAN), which enrolled exclusively individuals with type 2 diabetes, totaling 67,452 participants of European ancestry across the different analyses (up to 7,787 with diabetes in discovery and replication).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:11596665</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16075030</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21972410</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31967344</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADVANCE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADVANCE_TRIAL</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7496988/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As in previous analyses based on ADVANCE 15, 19, the primary comparison in the present study was between three groupings of countries based on geography and economic development: Asia, comprising China, India, Malaysia and the Philippines; Eastern Europe, comprising the Czech Republic, Estonia, Hungary, Lithuania, Poland, Russia and Slovakia; and &apos;established market economies&apos;, comprising Australia, Canada, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy, the Netherlands, New Zealand, and the UK.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475 -->

