    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001479 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001479">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30804558</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium of autism genetics research groups at more than 50 centres in North America and Europe, initiated by the National Alliance for Autism Research (later Autism Speaks) and the US National Institutes of Health and formed from four existing consortia (the Autism Genetics Cooperative, the Autism Genetic Resource Exchange, the Collaborative Programs of Excellence in Autism and the International Molecular Genetic Study of Autism Consortium). It pools the families with autism spectrum disorder collected at its sites, diagnosed with the ADI-R and ADOS, for genome-wide linkage, copy number variation and association studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AGP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AGP Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Autism Genome Project Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Autism Genome Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001479"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30804558</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of common genetic risk variants for autism spectrum disorder.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30804558</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6454898/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, five cohorts provided genotypes to the sample (N denoting the number of trios for which genotypes were available): The Geschwind Autism Center of Excellence (ACE; N = 391), the Autism Genome Project (AGP; N = 2,272), the Autism Genetic Resource Exchange (AGRE; N = 974), the NIMH Repository, the Montreal/Boston Collection (MONBOS; N = 1,396, and the Simons Simplex Collection(SSC; N = 2,231).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001479"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of autism genetics research groups at more than 50 centres in North America and Europe, initiated by the National Alliance for Autism Research (later Autism Speaks) and the US National Institutes of Health and formed from four existing consortia (the Autism Genetics Cooperative, the Autism Genetic Resource Exchange, the Collaborative Programs of Excellence in Autism and the International Molecular Genetic Study of Autism Consortium). It pools the families with autism spectrum disorder collected at its sites, diagnosed with the ADI-R and ADOS, for genome-wide linkage, copy number variation and association studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16078860</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17322880</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24768552</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001479"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AGP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001479"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3004528/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As one of many contributors to the AGP, AGRE continues to sit on the cutting edge of research.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30804558</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A resource of biomaterials (cell lines, DNA and serum) and genetic and phenotypic data from families with autism spectrum disorder recruited from across the United States, mostly multiplex families with two or more affected members, whose diagnostic assessments (ADI-R and ADOS) and blood draws are done in the families&apos; homes. It was established in 1997 by the Cure Autism Now Foundation and the Human Biological Data Interchange, is now managed by Autism Speaks, and makes its samples and data available to qualified researchers.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AGRE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Autism Genetics Resource Exchange</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>autism genetic resource exchange</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Autism Genetic Resource Exchange</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30804558</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of common genetic risk variants for autism spectrum disorder.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30804558</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6454898/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, five cohorts provided genotypes to the sample (N denoting the number of trios for which genotypes were available): The Geschwind Autism Center of Excellence (ACE; N = 391), the Autism Genome Project (AGP; N = 2,272), the Autism Genetic Resource Exchange (AGRE; N = 974), the NIMH Repository, the Montreal/Boston Collection (MONBOS; N = 1,396, and the Simons Simplex Collection(SSC; N = 2,231).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A resource of biomaterials (cell lines, DNA and serum) and genetic and phenotypic data from families with autism spectrum disorder recruited from across the United States, mostly multiplex families with two or more affected members, whose diagnostic assessments (ADI-R and ADOS) and blood draws are done in the families&apos; homes. It was established in 1997 by the Cure Autism Now Foundation and the Human Biological Data Interchange, is now managed by Autism Speaks, and makes its samples and data available to qualified researchers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:11452364</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20955925</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28702161</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AGRE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6071802/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our study sample comprised individuals from the Autism Genetic Resource Exchange (AGRE), a volunteer research repository of families from across the United States in which typically two or more siblings have a diagnosis of ASD (multiplex families).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001481 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001481">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:28346443</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of adult glioma run by the University of California, San Francisco since 1991, whose cases are adults with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma: population-based cases living in six San Francisco Bay Area counties (Alameda, Contra Costa, Marin, San Francisco, San Mateo and Santa Clara), identified through the regional cancer registry&apos;s rapid case ascertainment, and, from 2002, clinic-based cases recruited at the UCSF Neuro-oncology Clinic. Its controls were found by random-digit dialling in the same counties and frequency-matched to cases on age, sex and ethnicity, and later drawn from UCSF clinics; it studies environmental, immunological and genetic risk factors for glioma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SFAGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>San Francisco Adult Glioma Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UCSF Adult Glioma Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>University of California, San Francisco Adult Glioma Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">San Francisco Bay Area Adult Glioma Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001481"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28346443</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of glioma subtypes identifies specific differences in genetic susceptibility to glioblastoma and non-glioblastoma tumors.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28346443</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5558246/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UCSF adult glioma case–control study (SFAGS–GWAS) included participants of the San Francisco Bay Area Adult Glioma Study (AGS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001481"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of adult glioma run by the University of California, San Francisco since 1991, whose cases are adults with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma: population-based cases living in six San Francisco Bay Area counties (Alameda, Contra Costa, Marin, San Francisco, San Mateo and Santa Clara), identified through the regional cancer registry&apos;s rapid case ascertainment, and, from 2002, clinic-based cases recruited at the UCSF Neuro-oncology Clinic. Its controls were found by random-digit dialling in the same counties and frequency-matched to cases on age, sex and ethnicity, and later drawn from UCSF clinics; it studies environmental, immunological and genetic risk factors for glioma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16749939</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28346443</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001481"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001481"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SFAGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001481"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5558246/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Population-based cases who were diagnosed between 1991 and 2009 (series 1–4) and who were residing in the six San Francisco Bay area counties were ascertained using the Cancer Prevention Institute of California’s early-case ascertainment system.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001482 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001482">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000781"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24836286</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at Aichi Cancer Center in Nagoya, Japan, part of the centre&apos;s Hospital-based Epidemiologic Research Program (HERPACC): its first collection (Aichi-1) took colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls, frequency-matched on age and sex, from the first-visit outpatients enrolled in HERPACC-II in 2000–2005, and its second (Aichi-2) recruited further cases and matched controls at the same hospital. Both collections were genotyped for the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium&apos;s genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aichi</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aichi CRC Studies</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aichi CRC Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aichi Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aichi_Con</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Asian Consortium, Colorectal Cancer Aichi</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Aichi Colorectal Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001482"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24836286</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale genetic study in East Asians identifies six new loci associated with colorectal cancer risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24836286</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4068797/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifically, stage 1 (GWAS discovery) consisted of five studies: Shanghai CRC Study 1 (Shanghai-1, n = 3,102), Shanghai CRC Study 2 (Shanghai-2, n = 908), Guangzhou CRC Study 1 (Guangzhou-1, n = 1,603), Aichi CRC Study 1 (Aichi-1, n =1,346), and Korean Cancer Prevention Study-II CRC (KCPS-II, n = 1,301).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001482"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at Aichi Cancer Center in Nagoya, Japan, part of the centre&apos;s Hospital-based Epidemiologic Research Program (HERPACC): its first collection (Aichi-1) took colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls, frequency-matched on age and sex, from the first-visit outpatients enrolled in HERPACC-II in 2000–2005, and its second (Aichi-2) recruited further cases and matched controls at the same hospital. Both collections were genotyped for the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium&apos;s genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001482"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Aichi</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
