    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41629673</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium, funded by the US National Cancer Institute as a Program Project, that pools the questionnaire data, tumour tissue and DNA of four epidemiological studies of breast cancer in African American women in the United States (two case-control studies, the Carolina Breast Cancer Study and the Women&apos;s Circle of Health Study, and two cohorts, the Black Women&apos;s Health Study and the Multiethnic Cohort Study), with tumour subtyping, genotyping and data harmonisation done centrally in shared cores, to study the causes of breast cancer subtypes, especially oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer, in African American women.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AMBER</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AMBER Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AMBER consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American Breast Cancer Epidemiology and Risk</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American Breast Cancer Epidemiology and Risk consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American breast cancer epidemiology and risk consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The African American Breast Cancer Epidemiology and Risk consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">African American Breast Cancer Epidemiology and Risk Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41629673</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Improved polygenic risk prediction models for breast cancer subtypes in women of African ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41629673</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13007722/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The genotype datasets used in this study are publicly available via dbGaP (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gap/) including AABC under accession code phs000851.v1.p1, ONCO under accession code phs001265.v1.p1, AMBER under accession code phs000669.v1.p1, ROOT under accession code phs000383.v1.p1, and GBHS under accession code phs002387.v1.p1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium, funded by the US National Cancer Institute as a Program Project, that pools the questionnaire data, tumour tissue and DNA of four epidemiological studies of breast cancer in African American women in the United States (two case-control studies, the Carolina Breast Cancer Study and the Women&apos;s Circle of Health Study, and two cohorts, the Black Women&apos;s Health Study and the Multiethnic Cohort Study), with tumour subtyping, genotyping and data harmonisation done centrally in shared cores, to study the causes of breast cancer subtypes, especially oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer, in African American women.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24343304</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25849024</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AMBER</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5142758/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The analysis included 91,627 SNPs genotyped or imputed in 3,663 breast cancer cases, (1,983 ER-positive and 1,098 ER-negative) and 4,687 controls from the African American Breast Cancer Epidemiology and Risk consortium, a collaborative project of four large studies of breast cancer in African-American women (Carolina Breast Cancer Study, Black Women&apos;s Health Study, Women&apos;s Circle of Health Study, and Multiethnic Cohort).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3945713/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study began in 1995 when 59,000 AA women 21–69 years of age from across the United States completed a 14-page postal health questionnaire.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001484 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001484">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19198609</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A German case-control study of myocardial infarction whose cases were enrolled in 2004–2006 in a prospective multicentre registry at 4 heart centres and 6 cardiology departments in North Rhine-Westphalia, Lower Saxony and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: consecutive men younger than 65 admitted with ST- or non-ST-segment elevation acute myocardial infarction, all of whom underwent cardiac catheterisation and revascularisation. Its controls are participants of the population-based Dortmund Health Study, and the case-control sample served as a replication study for the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium&apos;s genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AMI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AMI Gene</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AMI Gene Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AMI Gene Study/Dortmund Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Acute Myocardial Infarction Gene Study/Dortmund Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Acute Myocardial Infarction Gene Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001484"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19198609</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association of early-onset myocardial infarction with single nucleotide polymorphisms and copy number variants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19198609</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.327/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng327_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The six studies were: i) Acute Myocardial Infarction (AMI) Gene Study/Dortmund Health Study; ii) Verona Heart Study; iii) Mid-America Heart Institute; iv) Irish Family Study; v) German MI Family Study II; and vi) INTERHEART.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001484"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A German case-control study of myocardial infarction whose cases were enrolled in 2004–2006 in a prospective multicentre registry at 4 heart centres and 6 cardiology departments in North Rhine-Westphalia, Lower Saxony and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: consecutive men younger than 65 admitted with ST- or non-ST-segment elevation acute myocardial infarction, all of whom underwent cardiac catheterisation and revascularisation. Its controls are participants of the population-based Dortmund Health Study, and the case-control sample served as a replication study for the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium&apos;s genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.327/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng327_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001484"/>
