    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31959993</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ANZRAG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australia and New Zealand Registry of Advanced Glaucoma</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian and New Zealand Registry of Advanced Glaucoma</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Australian &amp; New Zealand Registry of Advanced Glaucoma</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31959993</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multitrait analysis of glaucoma identifies new risk loci and enables polygenic prediction of disease susceptibility and progression.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31959993</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8056672/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Australian &amp; New Zealand Registry of Advanced Glaucoma (ANZRAG) comprises 3,071 POAG cases of European descent, who were compared to 6,750 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22171965</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23453510</obo:IAO_0000119>
