        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multinational, randomised, double-blind, double-dummy phase 3 trial, sponsored by Bristol-Myers Squibb and Pfizer, in which patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter and at least one additional risk factor for stroke, enrolled from 2006 at over 1,000 centres in about 40 countries, were randomly assigned to apixaban or warfarin to test whether apixaban is non-inferior to warfarin in preventing stroke or systemic embolism. The trial ended in 2011; its participants&apos; baseline blood samples and genotypes have since been used in biomarker and genetic studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
