    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20860503</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genetic study of severe asthma in the United Kingdom, supported by Asthma UK, which recruited people of European ancestry with severe asthma (Global Initiative for Asthma classes 3–5) at UK centres and compared them in genome-wide association studies with controls without asthma or wheeze, to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and whether they differ from those of mild to moderate asthma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AUGOSA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Asthma UK Genetics of Severe Asthma</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20860503</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A large-scale, consortium-based genomewide association study of asthma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20860503</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4260321</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We did find a suggestive association with rs1837253 on chromosome 5, situated within the TSLP gene, among patients with severe asthma in the SEVERE study (P = 3×10−6; odds ratio, 0.56), but this association was not replicated among patients with severe asthma in the AUGOSA (Asthma UK Genetics of Severe Asthma) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genetic study of severe asthma in the United Kingdom, supported by Asthma UK, which recruited people of European ancestry with severe asthma (Global Initiative for Asthma classes 3–5) at UK centres and compared them in genome-wide association studies with controls without asthma or wheeze, to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and whether they differ from those of mild to moderate asthma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20860503</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22561531</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AUGOSA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://thorax.bmj.com/content/67/9/762</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Only subjects in classes 3–5 were included, recruited across UK-based centres.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:39572784</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AUMC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AUMC_DCM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Amsterdam UMC cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Amsterdam UMC dilated cardiomyopathy GWAS cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:39572784</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study reveals mechanisms underlying dilated cardiomyopathy and myocardial resilience.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39572784</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11631763/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Amsterdam cohort comprised DCM patients referred for genetic testing at Amsterdam UMC, who underwent chart review for DCM diagnosis and had evidence of hypocontractility on imaging; 978 DCM cases passed all genotype quality-control criteria, of which 783 homogeneous cases of patients of European ancestry were included in GWAS (Supplementary Note and Supplementary Table 3).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39572784</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AUMC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AUMC_DCM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11631763/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The clinical DCM datasets included (1) a published GWAS by Garnier et al. that enrolled 2,651 DCM cases from France, Germany, Italy, the UK and the United States8; (2) a reanalyzed dataset of 909 DCM cases from Heidelberg, Germany10 (Supplementary Note) and (3) a new dataset of Dutch DCM cases from Amsterdam UMC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Austria"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31537649</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AusDiane</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Austrian Diabetes Nephropathy Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Austrian Diabetic Nephropathy Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31537649</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Diabetic Kidney Disease Highlights Biology Involved in Glomerular Basement Membrane Collagen.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31537649</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Austrian Diabetic Nephropathy Study (AusDiane) was initiated in 2012 in the state of Salzburg in Austria, and is part of the InterDiane Consortium (please see also the InterDiane cohort description).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
