    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:34214236</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BARCODE 1</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The BARCODE 1 Study: The Use of Genetic Profiling to Guide Prostate Cancer Targeted Screening</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BARCODE1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:34214236</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The BARCODE1 Pilot: a feasibility study of using germline single nucleotide polymorphisms to target prostate cancer screening.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34214236</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9292247/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BARCODE1 study (NCT03857477) is enrolling men of European ancestry from the community via their GPs to undergo a germline genetic profile test utilising 130 PCa risk SNPs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34214236</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34214236+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BARCODE1 Pilot has shown this community study in the UK to be feasible, with an overall uptake of 26%.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19879194</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection of patients with relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis or a clinically isolated syndrome with MRI signs of demyelination, assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from four of its clinical trials: three studies of interferon beta-1b (BENEFIT, BEYOND and the 16-year long-term follow-up of the pivotal interferon beta-1b trial in relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis) and one of a CCR1 antagonist. It was genotyped genome-wide and used as multiple sclerosis cases in genetic studies of susceptibility.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BayerScheringPharma</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Therapeutic Trial collection</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19879194</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Integration of genetic risk factors into a clinical algorithm for multiple sclerosis susceptibility: a weighted genetic risk score.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19879194</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3099419/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This sample collection is therefore referred to as the Therapeutic Trial (TT) collection.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of patients with relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis or a clinically isolated syndrome with MRI signs of demyelination, assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from four of its clinical trials: three studies of interferon beta-1b (BENEFIT, BEYOND and the 16-year long-term follow-up of the pivotal interferon beta-1b trial in relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis) and one of a CCR1 antagonist. It was genotyped genome-wide and used as multiple sclerosis cases in genetic studies of susceptibility.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19879194</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22190364</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
