    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33303219</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer&apos;s Research UK and the Alzheimer&apos;s Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King&apos;s College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BDR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BfDR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Brains for Dementia Research cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Brains for Dementia Research</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33303219</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic variants in glutamate-, Aβ-, and tau-related pathways determine polygenic risk for Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33303219</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>http://irep.ntu.ac.uk/id/eprint/42152/1/1389839_Brookes.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We have determined the predictive capacity of the Synaptic PRS in two datasets of cognitively normal controls (target dataset; n=137, validation dataset; n=80) and pathologically confirmed LOAD patients (target dataset; n=302, validation dataset; n=56) from the Brains for Dementia Research (BDR) resource.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer&apos;s Research UK and the Alzheimer&apos;s Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King&apos;s College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30452415</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BDR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BfDR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6294579/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Brains for Dementia Research (BDR) cohort and program was for planned brain donation across five UK brain banks and one donation point, with standardized operating procedures, following longitudinal clinical and psychometric assessments for people with no cognitive impairment as well as those with dementia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25229638</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective longitudinal study based at the University of Edinburgh of young people aged 16–25 at entry who were well but at high familial risk of mood disorder, having at least one first-degree or two second-degree relatives with bipolar I disorder (identified through patients with bipolar I disorder referred by psychiatrists across Scotland), and of unrelated controls with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder drawn from their social networks, assessed clinically and with brain MRI on three occasions about two years apart to study changes that precede the onset of mood disorders.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BFS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Bipolar Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SBFS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Scottish Bipolar Family Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25229638</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Dysfunction of emotional brain systems in individuals at high risk of mood disorder with depression and predictive features prior to illness.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25229638</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25229638+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Bipolar Family Study (BFS) is a prospective longitudinal study that has examined individuals at familial risk of mood disorder and healthy controls on three occasions, 2 years apart.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
