        <rdfs:comment>By use of a whole-population ascertainment scheme, 822 individuals were enrolled from a schistosomiasis-endemic area in Conde, Bahia, in Brazil.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:36520433</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer&apos;s disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer&apos;s disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BICWALZS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Biobank Innovation for Chronic Cerebrovascular Disease With Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Biobank Innovations for Chronic Cerebrovascular Disease with ALZheimer&apos;s Disease Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Biobank Innovations for Chronic Cerebrovascular Disease With Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:36520433</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Transferability of Alzheimer Disease Polygenic Risk Score Across Populations and Its Association With Alzheimer Disease-Related Phenotypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36520433</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9856322/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This was part of the ongoing BICWALZS study (Biobank Innovation for Chronic Cerebrovascular Disease With Alzheimer’s Disease Study) and data from the Center for Convergence Research of Neurological Disorders.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer&apos;s disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer&apos;s disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35042283</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
