        <obo:IAO_0000115>A German case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder, from the University of Bonn and the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, whose cases, nearly all with bipolar I disorder diagnosed by DSM-IV best-estimate consensus from structured interviews (SADS-L or SCID), were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatric inpatient units, and whose controls were drawn from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium&apos;s bipolar disorder working group.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym BOMA also denotes Bonn-Mannheim MDD study (COHO:0001542); this term is BOMA-Bipolar Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
