        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective cohort of men aged 45–59 years from the town of Caerphilly and its surrounding villages in South Wales, United Kingdom, identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists and first examined in 1979–1983 by the MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) to study risk factors for coronary heart disease, then re-examined in later phases that added cognitive testing and follow-up for dementia and other chronic diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CaPS also denotes Cancer Prostate in Sweden (COHO:0000025) and Carotid Atherosclerosis Progression Study (COHO:0001566); this term is Caerphilly Prospective Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
