        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case–control study of breast cancer in Mexican women aged 35 to 69, carried out from January 2004 to December 2007 in Mexico City, Monterrey and Veracruz by investigators of the Mexican National Institute of Public Health, in which women with newly diagnosed, untreated breast cancer were recruited at twelve public hospitals of the Mexican Social Security Institute, the Institute of Security and Social Services of State Workers and the Ministry of Health, and controls, frequency-matched to the cases by age, health-care institution and region, were chosen by multistage random household sampling; participants were interviewed on health, diet and physical activity, measured and gave blood samples, to study risk factors for breast cancer in Mexico.</owl:annotatedTarget>
