    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22792082</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CARE also denotes Los Angeles component of The Womens Contraceptive and Reproductive Experiences Study (COHO:0000110), Canadian Airways Research Group (COHO:0000229), Cholesterol and Recurrent Events (COHO:0001569) and Candidate Gene Association Resource (COHO:0001586); this term is Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARE Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARE_c</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childhood Asthma Research and Education</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childhood Asthma Research and Education network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childhood Asthma Research and Education program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22792082</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis in asthma subjects identifies SPATS2L as a novel bronchodilator response gene.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22792082</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390407/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The primary group of subjects consisted of 1,644 non-Hispanic white asthmatics from the following drug clinical trials: Childhood Asthma Management Program (CAMP) [33], Leukotriene Modifier or Corticosteroid Salmeterol study (LOCCS) [34], Effectiveness of Low Dose Theophylline as an Add-on Treatment in Asthma trial (LODO) [35], a medication trial conducted by Sepracor, Inc. [36], [37], and subsets of clinical trials within the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network [38], and the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN) [39] participating in the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) Asthma Resource project (SHARP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15157730</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17141853</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
