        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multiphase randomised trial of the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in adults aged 18–67 with chronic schizophrenia, run under the US National Institute of Mental Health&apos;s CATIE programme in 2001–2004 at 57 clinical sites across the United States (public mental health, academic, Veterans Affairs and managed care settings), whose double-blind first phase compared the first-generation drug perphenazine with the second-generation drugs olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone and ziprasidone for up to 18 months, with all-cause treatment discontinuation as the primary outcome. Participants could join an optional genetic sub-study by donating DNA.</owl:annotatedTarget>
