    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30482948</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CATS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Comorbidity and Trauma Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30482948</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Transancestral GWAS of alcohol dependence reveals common genetic underpinnings with psychiatric disorders.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30482948</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6430207/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Funding support for the Comorbidity and Trauma Study (CATS) (dbGAP accession number: phs000277.v1.p1) was provided by the National Institute on Drug Abuse (R01 DA17305); GWAS genotyping services at the CIDR at The Johns Hopkins University were supported by the National Institutes of Health (contract N01-HG-65403).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23245376</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26239289</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CATS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23245376+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The sample of the Comorbidity and Trauma Study, a genetic association study of heroin dependence, consists of Australian heroin dependent cases ascertained from opioid replacement therapy clinics and controls ascertained in nearby economically disadvantaged neighborhoods.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Croatia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30103784</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the &apos;10,001 Dalmatians&apos; study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CCCGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Croatia CRC case-control study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Croatia case-control CRC study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Croatian Colorectal Cancer Genetic Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30103784</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Exploring causality in the association between circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D and colorectal cancer risk: a large Mendelian randomisation study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30103784</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6090711/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Finally, a case–control CRC study from Croatia consisting of 764 cases and 460 population-based controls was also included in the analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the &apos;10,001 Dalmatians&apos; study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24066093</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31089142</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CCCGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Croatia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3774761/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the period from November 2008 to July 2009, a total of 338 colorectal cancer cases were recruited at departments of surgery in two hospitals in Zagreb, Croatia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22039354</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CCCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cambridgeshire Case-Control Population</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cambridgeshire case-control study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cambridgeshire Case-Control Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22039354</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Mendelian randomization study of B-type natriuretic peptide and type 2 diabetes: evidence of causal association from population studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22039354</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Cambridgeshire case-control study is a population-based study of T2D cases, aged 45–76 y, and age- and sex-matched controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12045211</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:14551916</obo:IAO_0000119>
