    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3582024/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>MetaStroke is a project of the International Stroke Genetics Consortium and comprises ischemic stroke cases whose DNA has been collected and undergone GWA scan, recruited from centers in Europe (BRAINS [Bio-Repository of DNA in Stroke], United Kingdom; DeCODE, Iceland; Cerebrovascular Diseases Registry (CEDIR), Milan, Italy; Rotterdam, the Netherlands), USA (Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities study; Cardiovascular Health Study; Framingham Heart Study; Genetics of Early Onset Stroke Study; Heart Protection Study; Heart and Vascular Health; Ischemic Stroke Genetics Study; Massachusetts General Hospital Genes Affecting Stroke Risk and Outcome study), and Australia (Australian Stroke Genetics Collaborative).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Romania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22113997</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC&apos;s lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies. Participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region&apos;s high kidney cancer rates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEERCC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEERCC case-control study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European Kidney Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European RCC case-control study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European Renal Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European Renal Cell Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Central and Eastern European Renal Cell Carcinoma Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22113997</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The chromosome 2p21 region harbors a complex genetic architecture for association with risk for renal cell carcinoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22113997</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3277315/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We genotyped 59 tagged SNPs in 2278 RCC cases and 3719 controls from two nested case–control studies [the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial and the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention (ATBC) study in Finland], a hospital-based Central and Eastern European RCC (CEERCC) case–control study and Caucasians from the United States Kidney Cancer (USKC) population-based case–control study (see Materials and Methods and Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC&apos;s lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies. Participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region&apos;s high kidney cancer rates.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19034282</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19753122</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21540858</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22113997</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CEERCC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2600689/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This hospital-based case–control study was conducted in seven centres (Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice, and Brno (Czech Republic)).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31792337</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEFALO study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cefalo</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CEFALO</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31792337</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A Weighted Genetic Risk Score of Adult Glioma Susceptibility Loci Associated with Pediatric Brain Tumor Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31792337</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31792337+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GRS was calculated in CEFALO, a population-based case-control study of brain tumors in children and adolescents including saliva DNA of 245 cases and 489 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21795665</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23652309</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26014354</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31792337</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6889151/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CEFALO is a population-based case-control study of brain tumors in children and adolescents aged 7–19 years conducted in Sweden, Denmark, Norway, and Switzerland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32820175</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Color Genomics participants</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Color genomics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Color Genomics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32820175</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic background modifies penetrance of monogenic variants for tier 1 genomic conditions.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32820175</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7441381/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Second, a breast cancer case-control study consisted of 19,264 women (1920 cases and 17,344 controls) who underwent clinical grade genetic testing for hereditary breast and ovarian cancer syndrome at a commercial testing laboratory (Color Genomics; Burlingame, CA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31771638</obo:IAO_0000119>
