    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20400780</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CARe also denotes Los Angeles component of The Womens Contraceptive and Reproductive Experiences Study (COHO:0000110), Canadian Airways Research Group (COHO:0000229), Cholesterol and Recurrent Events (COHO:0001569) and Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network (COHO:0001570); this term is Candidate Gene Association Resource.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARe Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Candidate Gene Association Resource Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Candidate gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Candidate-gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI CARe Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI Candidate Gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI_CARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute Candidate Gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Candidate Gene Association Resource</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20400780</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Candidate gene association resource (CARe): design, methods, and proof of concept.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20400780</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20400780+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute&apos;s Candidate Gene Association Resource (CARe), a planned cross-cohort analysis of genetic variation in cardiovascular, pulmonary, hematologic, and sleep-related traits, comprises &gt;40,000 participants representing 4 ethnic groups in 9 community-based cohorts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20400780</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CARe</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGARe</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NHLBI_CARe</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were recruited from six field centers across the United States: Wake Forest University, Columbia University, Johns Hopkins University, University of Minnesota, Northwestern University and University of California - Los Angeles.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:28530674</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGPS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Herlev/Østerbroundersøgelsen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Copenhagen General Population Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28530674</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fifteen new risk loci for coronary artery disease highlight arterial-wall-specific mechanisms.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28530674</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5555387/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, the European (EUR) studies comprised 16,093 CAD cases and 16,616 controls from EPIC-CVD (a case-cohort study embedded in the pan-European EPIC prospective study), the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS), the Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study (CIHDS) and the Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS) all recruited within Copenhagen, Denmark.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36214322</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36852012</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36891075</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGPS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18523221+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three studies of white individuals from Copenhagen, Denmark, were used: the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS), a 31-year prospective general population study (n = 9022; 28 heterozygotes); the Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS), a cross-sectional general population study (n = 31,241; 76 heterozygotes); and the Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study (CIHDS), a case-control study (n = 16,623; 44 heterozygotes).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
