    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37217678</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital&apos;s traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ChooseWell 365 Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ChooseWell 365</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37217678</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic predisposition to macronutrient preference and workplace food choices.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37217678</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37217678+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we examined the associations of polygenic scores for carbohydrate, fat, and protein preference with 12 months&apos; workplace food purchases among 397 hospital employees from the ChooseWell 365 study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital&apos;s traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30414448</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34097048</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8185595/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This randomized clinical trial was conducted on the main campus of Massachusetts General Hospital (MGH), a large academic teaching hospital in Boston, Massachusetts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:29273806</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and lung function tests, to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children&apos;s respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CHS also denotes Cardiovascular Health Study (COHO:0000384); this term is Children&apos;s Health Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHS_b</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childrens Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Southern California Children&apos;s Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>USC Children&apos;s Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Children&apos;s Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:29273806</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiancestry association study identifies new asthma risk loci that colocalize with immune-cell enhancer marks.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29273806</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Children&apos;s Health Study (CHS) is an ongoing cohort study in southern California investigating both genetic and environmental factors related to childhood asthma and lung function growth.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and lung function tests, to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children&apos;s respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20371422</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25694817</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29273806</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://healthstudy.usc.edu/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CHS_b</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1241973/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To assess these hypotheses, we conducted a case-control study of risk factors for early-life asthma that was nested in the Children&apos;s Health Study (CHS), a population-based study of children&apos;s respiratory health in 12 southern California communities.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:28530674</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based case-control study of ischaemic heart disease in Denmark whose cases are patients from the greater Copenhagen area referred for coronary angiography to Copenhagen University Hospital from 1991 onwards, with ischaemic heart disease documented by coronary stenosis or atherosclerosis on angiography, a positive exercise electrocardiogram or myocardial infarction, and whose controls without ischaemic heart disease are sampled from the Copenhagen General Population Study; with the Copenhagen City Heart Study and the Copenhagen General Population Study it is used in genetic and Mendelian randomization studies of cardiovascular disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CIHDS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Copenhagen Ischaemic Heart Disease Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Copenhagen ischaemic Heart Disease Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28530674</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fifteen new risk loci for coronary artery disease highlight arterial-wall-specific mechanisms.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28530674</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5555387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, the European (EUR) studies comprised 16,093 CAD cases and 16,616 controls from EPIC-CVD (a case-cohort study embedded in the pan-European EPIC prospective study), the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS), the Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study (CIHDS) and the Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS) all recruited within Copenhagen, Denmark.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based case-control study of ischaemic heart disease in Denmark whose cases are patients from the greater Copenhagen area referred for coronary angiography to Copenhagen University Hospital from 1991 onwards, with ischaemic heart disease documented by coronary stenosis or atherosclerosis on angiography, a positive exercise electrocardiogram or myocardial infarction, and whose controls without ischaemic heart disease are sampled from the Copenhagen General Population Study; with the Copenhagen City Heart Study and the Copenhagen General Population Study it is used in genetic and Mendelian randomization studies of cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22563304</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22698489</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25406188</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CIHDS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5555387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, the European (EUR) studies comprised 16,093 CAD cases and 16,616 controls from EPIC-CVD (a case-cohort study embedded in the pan-European EPIC prospective study), the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS), the Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study (CIHDS) and the Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS) all recruited within Copenhagen, Denmark.</rdfs:comment>
