    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35195259</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based cohort of Chinese adults aged 18 or over recruited in 2007–2008 by three-stage cluster random sampling at four survey sites, in Shandong, Henan and Jiangsu provinces, chosen for their different levels of economic development; it is one of the sub-cohorts of the Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR) project, followed up with the other sub-cohorts under a uniform protocol in 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident cardiovascular disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CIMIC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Community Intervention of Metabolic Syndrome in China &amp; Chinese Family Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Community Intervention of Metabolic Syndrome in China and Chinese Family Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35195259</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A polygenic risk score improves risk stratification of coronary artery disease: a large-scale prospective Chinese cohort study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35195259</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The validation cohorts were derived from three cohorts in the China-PAR project, including the International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia (InterASIA), the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (ChinaMUCA-1998), and Community Intervention of Metabolic Syndrome in China and Chinese Family Health Study (CIMIC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based cohort of Chinese adults aged 18 or over recruited in 2007–2008 by three-stage cluster random sampling at four survey sites, in Shandong, Henan and Jiangsu provinces, chosen for their different levels of economic development; it is one of the sub-cohorts of the Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR) project, followed up with the other sub-cohorts under a uniform protocol in 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31888885</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32433046</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34327424</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35195259</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CIMIC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7249710/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CIMIC was a large, community-based cohort that was established from 2007 to 2008 and selected four survey sites from three provinces (Shandong, Henan, and Jiangsu) with different economic development levels in China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30482948</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>A Probe Study of Acamprosate: Genes Associated With Response</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ACAM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CITA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mayo Clinic Center for Individualized Treatment of Addiction</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mayo Clinic Center for Individualized Treatment of Alcohol Dependence</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mayo Clinic Center for Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mayo Clinic Center for the Individual Treatment of Alcohol Dependence</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30482948</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Transancestral GWAS of alcohol dependence reveals common genetic underpinnings with psychiatric disorders.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30482948</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-018-0275-1/MediaObjects/41593_2018_275_MOESM4_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The alcohol dependent patients in this sample were recruited as part of the Mayo Clinic Center for Individualized Treatment of Addiction (CITA) pharmacogenomics study of acamprosate response.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25290263</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35752286</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
