    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32887683</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children&apos;s Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital&apos;s Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CLARITY</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CLARITY JIA Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childhood Arthritis Risk Factor Identification Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ChiLdhood Arthritis Risk factor Identification sTudY</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32887683</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genomic risk scores for juvenile idiopathic arthritis and its subtypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32887683</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7677485/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Finally, in the Australian cohort, from the ChiLdhood Arthritis Risk factor Identification sTudY (CLARITY),28 29 all the cases were JIA diagnosed by a paediatric rheumatologist.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children&apos;s Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital&apos;s Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23153063</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CLARITY</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23153063+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We have established a JIA biobank in Melbourne, Australia called CLARITY - ChiLdhood Arthritis Risk factor Identification sTudY, with the broad aim of identifying genomic and environmental disease risk factors.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:26034056</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan&apos;s electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CMHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>California Mens Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">California Men&apos;s Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:26034056</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A large multiethnic genome-wide association study of prostate cancer identifies novel risk variants and substantial ethnic differences.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26034056</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4527942/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CMHS is a prospective cohort study of KP California men.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan&apos;s electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16813653</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CMHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1569841/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 2002 – 2003, we established the California Men&apos;s Health Study (CMHS), a multiethnic cohort of 84 170 men ages 45 to 69 years who are members of the northern and southern California regions of Kaiser Permanente, the largest managed care organization in California.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32424353</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of breast cancer of the Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO) in Madrid, Spain, whose cases, recruited in 2000–2005, are consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo, and women with at least one affected first-degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid, and whose controls are women free of breast cancer attending the Menopause Research Centre in Madrid or a free medical check-up for female members of the College of Lawyers in Madrid; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CNIO-BCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Spanish National Cancer Centre Breast Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32424353</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study identifies 32 novel breast cancer susceptibility loci from overall and subtype-specific analyses.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32424353</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CNIO- BCS was supported by the Instituto de Salud Carlos III, the Red Temática de Investigación Cooperativa en Cáncer and grants from the Asociación Española Contra el Cáncer and the Fondo de Investigación Sanitario (PI11/00923 and PI12/00070).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of breast cancer of the Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO) in Madrid, Spain, whose cases, recruited in 2000–2005, are consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo, and women with at least one affected first-degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid, and whose controls are women free of breast cancer attending the Menopause Research Centre in Madrid or a free medical check-up for female members of the College of Lawyers in Madrid; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25390939</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
